2025-12-24 14:41:21 | INFO | Q03 id=gsm8k_mcq_00002 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The original cost of the house was $80,000 and the repairs cost $50,000 so the total cost is $80,000 + $50,000 = $130,000. The value of the house increased by 150% so the new value is $130,000 * 150% = $195,000. So the profit made is $195,000 - $130,000 = $65,000. Answer: C
