2025-12-24 14:45:20 | INFO | Q145 id=gsm8k_mcq_00144 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the calculation for profit can be made as follows:\n\nTotal income = Total number of clients * Cost per job\n\nSince Kim has 3 current clients and is talking to 5 more potential clients, he will have a total of 8 jobs.\n\nTotal income = 8 * ($2 + $5) = $44\n\nExpenses = Cost per job * Number of jobs\n\nExpenses = ($2 + $5) * 8 = $44\n\nProfit = Total income - Expenses\n\nProfit = $44 - $44 = $0\n\nTherefore, the profit that Kim will make each week is $0.\n\nAnswer: A) -20
2025-12-24 14:45:23 | INFO | Q131 id=gsm8k_mcq_00130 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The original statement is: "Nissa hires 60 seasonal workers to play elves in her department store's Santa village. A third of the elves quit after children vomit on them, then 10 of the remaining elves quit after kids kick their shins. How many elves are left?"\nTo solve this problem, we can start by finding the number of elves who quit after being vomited on:\n\n60 * (1/3) = 20 elves\n\nSo there are 60 - 20 = 40 elves left.\n\nNext, we need to find out how many elves quit after being kicked:\n\n40 - 10 = 30 elves\n\nTherefore, there are 30 elves left playing elves in Nissa's department store's Santa village.\n\nAnswer: C) 30
