2025-12-24 14:47:20 | INFO | Q219 id=gsm8k_mcq_00218 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The ages of Adrian, Harriet, and Zack can be represented as follows:\n\nAdrian = 3 * Harriet\nHarriet = 1/2 * Zack\n\nSubstituting the values given in the question:\n\nAdrian = 3 * 21\nHarriet = 1/2 * 21\nZack = 21 * 2\n\nTherefore, the total age of the three is:\n\nAdrian + Harriet + Zack = 3 * 21 + 1/2 * 21 + 21 * 2 = 99\n\nTo find the average age of the three in three years, we need to add three more years to their current ages. However, since the ages of the individuals are not provided in the question, it is impossible to calculate the average age of the three in three years. Therefore, the answer cannot be determined with the given information.
2025-12-24 14:47:22 | INFO | Q194 id=gsm8k_mcq_00193 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=At noon on Sunday, there were 18 pink plastic flamingos + 18 pink plastic flamingos = 36 pink plastic flamingos. At noon on Sunday, there were 36 pink plastic flamingos - 18 white plastic flamingos = 18 more pink plastic flamingos than white plastic flamingos. Answer: D) 36
