2025-12-24 14:47:37 | INFO | Q202 id=gsm8k_mcq_00201 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate John's earnings for the year as follows:\n\nFirst, let's determine his base salary before the raise. We know that he makes $2000 per week, so his base salary would be:\n\n$2000 x 52 weeks = $104,000\n\nNext, we need to add the monetary reward from the award. We know that the award has a one-time monetary reward of $5000, so we add that to his base salary:\n\n$104,000 + $5,000 = $109,000\n\nTherefore, John made $109,000 that year.\n\nAnswer: B) $109,000
2025-12-24 14:47:37 | INFO | Q232 id=gsm8k_mcq_00231 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=On Tuesday, Kylie collects 2 times more shells than she did on Monday, which was 5 more shells than Robert who collected 20 shells. Therefore, on Tuesday Kylie collects 2 * 5 = 10 shells more than she did on Monday. Adding the 5 shells that Kylie collected on Monday, she collects a total of 10 + 5 = 15 shells on Tuesday. The answer is C) 15.
