2025-12-24 14:48:53 | INFO | Q283 id=gsm8k_mcq_00282 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of people attending the soccer game is 12 team members + 3 coaches + 2 guests per team member = 17 people. Since each pizza serves 3 people, Maddy will need to buy 17/3 = 5.67 pizzas. However, since she cannot buy a fraction of a pizza, she will need to round up to 6 pizzas. Therefore, Maddy will spend 6 * $15 = $90.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
2025-12-24 14:48:56 | INFO | Q250 id=gsm8k_mcq_00249 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=On Monday, Sue ate 4 times as many cookies as her sister who ate 5 cookies. This means Sue ate 4 * 5 = 20 cookies on Monday. On Tuesday, Sue ate twice as many cookies as her sister who ate 13 cookies. This means Sue ate 2 * 13 = 26 cookies on Tuesday. In total, Sue ate 20 + 26 = 46 cookies over the two days. If each cookie has 200 calories, then Sue consumed a total of 46 * 200 = 9,200 calories. Her sister consumed a total of 5 + 13 = 18 cookies over the two days. If each cookie has 200 calories, then Sue consumed 9,200 - 18 * 200 = 2,400 more calories than her sister. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 2,400.
2025-12-24 14:48:58 | INFO | Q252 id=gsm8k_mcq_00251 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=After deleting 9 apps that Travis no longer uses and downloading 18 more, he has:\n\n61 - 9 + 18 = 52\n\nTherefore, there are 52 apps on Travis's tablet now.\n\nAnswer: D
2025-12-24 14:48:58 | INFO | Q285 id=gsm8k_mcq_00284 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of stories Alani, Braylen, and Margot wrote in the first week is 20 + 40 + 60 = 120 stories. If they each doubled the number of stories they'd written in the first week in the second week, Alani would write 20 x 2 = 40 stories, Braylen would write 40 x 2 = 80 stories, and Margot would write 60 x 2 = 120 stories. The total number of stories they wrote in the second week is 40 + 80 + 120 = 240 stories. Altogether, they wrote 120 + 240 = 360 stories. Therefore, the correct answer is C) 360.
