2025-12-24 14:49:34 | INFO | Q272 id=gsm8k_mcq_00271 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of windows in both houses can be calculated as follows:\n\nEach house has 3 bedrooms with 2 windows each, so each house has 3 * 2 = 6 windows from the bedrooms.\n\nThere are also 4 additional windows in each house that are not connected to bedrooms, so each house has 4 + 6 = 10 windows.\n\nSince John has two houses, the total number of windows between the houses is 2 * 10 = 20.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 20.\n\n反思：在第二轮问答中，我没有充分解释我的思考过程，也没有给出明确的答案。我应该更加清晰地阐述我的推理步骤，并且选择一个字母作为答案。
