2025-12-24 14:50:24 | INFO | Q333 id=gsm8k_mcq_00332 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The number of unmanned ruined castles in Scotland can be calculated as follows:\n\nOut of the total 220 castles in Scotland, 40% of them are ruins. To find the number of ruined castles, we multiply 220 by 40% (or 0.4):\n220 x 0.4 = 88\n\nOf the ruined castles, half of them are unmanned. To find the number of unmanned ruined castles, we divide the number of ruined castles by 2:\n88 / 2 = 44\n\nTherefore, there are 44 unmanned ruined castles in Scotland.\n\nAnswer: C) 44
2025-12-24 14:50:27 | INFO | Q300 id=gsm8k_mcq_00299 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that John drives 30 miles per day x 5 days per week x 50 weeks = 7,800 miles per year. He pays $2 per mile driven x 7,800 miles = $15,600 per year for driving. Additionally, he gives his driver a $150 bonus per month, which equates to $1,800 per year. Therefore, John pays a total of $15,600 + $1,800 = $17,400 per year for driving. The correct answer is A) $16,800.
2025-12-24 14:50:28 | INFO | Q335 id=gsm8k_mcq_00334 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, if the four individuals were to share their paintball guns equally, each of them would have:\n\n  * DJ: 8 guns / 4 people = 2 guns per person\n  * Nick: 10 guns / 4 people = 2.5 guns per person\n  * RJ: 1 gun / 4 people = 0.25 guns per person\n  * Richard: 5 guns / 4 people = 1.25 guns per person\n\nTherefore, the closest choice from the options provided would be A) 6, as it is the average number of guns that each person would receive if the guns were shared equally among them.
