2025-12-24 14:50:43 | INFO | Q311 id=gsm8k_mcq_00310 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total cost of the six business suits is 6 * $100 = $600\. The cost of the three suitcases is 3 * $50 = $150\. The cost of the flight ticket is $700 + 5 * $100 = $800\. The total cost of all the items mentioned is $600 + $150 + $800 = $1550\. To save $2000, Theo needs to spend $1550 - $2000 = -$450\. This means he has to spend $450 on buying gifts for his business partners in South Africa. Answer: C.
2025-12-24 14:50:45 | INFO | Q345 id=gsm8k_mcq_00344 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can see that:\n\n- Juice Box A costs $4\n- Juice Box B costs $5 more than Juice Box A, so it costs $4 + $5 = $9\n- Juice Box C costs $7 more than Juice Box A, so it costs $4 + $7 = $11\n\nTherefore, the difference between Juice Box C and Juice Box B is $11 - $9 = $2.\n\nSo the correct answer is B) 2.
