2025-12-24 14:50:54 | INFO | Q315 id=gsm8k_mcq_00314 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The statement given is that there are 105 members on a football team, and there are twice as many players on the offense as there is on the defense. Additionally, there is half the number of players on the special teams as there is on the defense. To find the number of players on the defense, we can start by setting up an equation using these pieces of information.\nLet x be the number of players on the defense. We know that there are 105 members on the team, so the total number of players on the offense and defense combined is 105. We also know that there are twice as many players on the offense as there is on the defense, so there are 2x players on the offense. Finally, we know that there is half the number of players on the special teams as there is on the defense, so there are x/2 players on the special teams.\nPutting all of this together, we can write the following equation: x + 2x + x/2 = 105. Multiplying both sides by 2, we get 3x + x = 210. Combining like terms, we get 4x = 210. Dividing both sides by 4, we get x = 52. Therefore, there are 52 players on the defense.\nAnswer: D) 35
