2025-12-24 14:51:13 | INFO | Q327 id=gsm8k_mcq_00326 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The number of people who got on the bus at the terminal can be found by adding the number of people who got on at each stop. At the first stop, 5 more people got on, so there were 5 + x people on the bus. At the second stop, 7 people got off and 8 more got on, so there were 5 + x - 7 + 8 = 5 + x + 1 person on the bus. Since there were a total of 20 people heading to the third stop, we can set up the equation 5 + x + 1 = 20. Solving for x gives us x = 14. Therefore, 14 people got on the bus at the terminal.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
