2025-12-24 14:51:33 | INFO | Q336 id=gsm8k_mcq_00335 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To find out how much sugar Mason needs to make 8 batches of suckers and 1 batch of fudge, we can set up an equation based on the amount of sugar needed for each type of candy.\nLet S be the total amount of sugar needed for all the batches of suckers and F be the total amount of sugar needed for the batch of fudge.\nWe know that S = 30 * 8 = 240 and F = 70. To find the total amount of sugar needed for all the batches of suckers and one batch of fudge, we add the amount of sugar needed for each type of candy together:\nS + F = 240 + 70 = 310\nTherefore, Mason needs 310 ounces of sugar to make 8 batches of suckers and 1 batch of fudge.\nAnswer: C) 310
