2025-12-24 14:52:59 | INFO | Q384 id=gsm8k_mcq_00383 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Millie spends $18 to buy supplies to make 3 pitchers of lemonade, which holds 12 cups of lemonade each. Therefore, she has a total of 36 cups of lemonade (12 cups x 3 pitchers). She sells each cup of lemonade for $1, so if she sells all 36 cups, she will make a profit of $36 (36 cups x $1/cup).\nTherefore, the answer is A) 2.
2025-12-24 14:53:02 | INFO | Q433 id=gsm8k_mcq_00432 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by finding out how many dragons each prince killed using their respective weapons:\n\n  * Prince Thaddeus killed 100 dragons with his sword\n  * Prince Arthur killed 100 x 3/4 = 75 dragons with his spear\n  * Prince Walter killed 75 x 2 = 150 dragons with his rusty iron axe\n  * Prince Bruce killed 150 x 1/5 = 30 dragons with his nail file\n\nTherefore, the total number of dragons killed by all four princes is:\n\n  * Prince Thaddeus + Prince Arthur + Prince Walter + Prince Bruce = 100 + 75 + 150 + 30 = 355 dragons\n\nSo the answer is A) 30.
2025-12-24 14:53:03 | INFO | Q386 id=gsm8k_mcq_00385 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The choir consists of 52 members, 50% of which are boys and 50% of which are girls. This means there are 52/2 = 26 female members in the choir. On the day of the performance, half of the people performing can't make it to the show because their bus breaks down. Since there are 26 female members, half of them cannot perform, so there are 26/2 = 13 female members who will perform. Additionally, the choir's three teachers decide to sing with them, so the total number of people singing in the performance is 13 + 3 = 16.\nTherefore, the answer is B) 16.
2025-12-24 14:53:05 | INFO | Q435 id=gsm8k_mcq_00434 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, it is not possible to determine how many candy bars George bought. We only know that he spent $5, got 3 bags of chips, and had 1% of his money left. Without knowing the value of his initial amount of money or the cost of each bag of chips, it is impossible to calculate the number of candy bars he bought. Therefore, the answer is unknown.
