2025-12-24 14:58:45 | INFO | Q649 id=gsm8k_mcq_00648 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=If Howie buys one vanilla cupcake and one chocolate cupcake for himself, his teacher, and his 25 classmates, he will be giving out a total of 2 + 2 + 25 = 30 cupcakes. To find out how many cupcakes he needs to buy in total, we need to divide the number of people by the number of cupcakes per person. In this case, there are 30 people (Howie + teacher + classmates) and each person will receive 2 cupcakes. Therefore, Howie needs to buy a total of 30 / 2 = 15 cupcakes.\nAnswer: C) 27
