2025-12-24 14:58:51 | INFO | Q651 id=gsm8k_mcq_00650 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=On Tuesday, Clara bought 20 pomegranates at $20 each, so the total cost was 20 x 20 = $400. She got $2 off because she had a voucher, so her final cost was 400 - 2 = $398. The next day, the price shot to $30 per fruit, so the total cost for 20 pomegranates became 30 x 20 = $600. The store also offered a 10% discount on the total cost, which amounted to 10/100 x 600 = $60. So, the final cost that Sheila paid was 600 - 60 = $540. Therefore, the difference between the final prices paid for the pomegranates on the two days is 540 - 398 = $142. Answer: B
2025-12-24 14:58:54 | INFO | Q590 id=gsm8k_mcq_00589 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, Martin will lose 1.25 pounds per week if he eats Cheerios every day for breakfast and gain 1.75 pounds per week if he eats donuts every day for breakfast. Therefore, over 5 weeks, he will gain 5 * 1.75 = 8.75 pounds if he eats donuts every day for breakfast and lose 5 * 1.25 = 6.25 pounds if he eats Cheerios every day for breakfast. The difference in his weight at the end of 5 weeks between the two breakfast options will be 8.75 - 6.25 = 2.5 pounds. Answer: A) 2.5
