2025-12-24 14:58:57 | INFO | Q655 id=gsm8k_mcq_00654 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Lori needs 1 whole egg to make 2 deviled egg halves, so she needs 2 / 1 = 2 eggs for all the guests. Each guest will eat 3 deviled egg halves, so she needs 2 * 3 = 6 eggs for all the guests. Since there are 16 guests, she will need 16 / 6 = 2 dozen eggs.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 4.
2025-12-24 14:59:00 | INFO | Q657 id=gsm8k_mcq_00656 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Mike has 30 days to complete the reading, and he plans to read 10 pages a day. To find out how many days before the deadline he will finish his reading, we can divide the total number of pages by the number of pages he plans to read each day.\n200 / 10 = 20\nTherefore, Mike will finish his reading 20 days before the deadline. So the answer is C: 20.
2025-12-24 14:59:02 | INFO | Q594 id=gsm8k_mcq_00593 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The beanstalk will take 2 days to be taller than Mark's window.\nTo see why, let's set up an equation representing the height of the beanstalk at each day:\nh(t) = 2 * h(t - 1)\nwhere h(t) is the height of the beanstalk at day t, and h(t - 1) is the height of the beanstalk at day t - 1.\nWe are given that the beanstalk starts out 4 feet tall, so h(0) = 4.\nSubstituting this into our equation, we get:\nh(1) = 2 * 4 = 8\nh(2) = 2 * 8 = 16\nSo after 2 days, the beanstalk will be 16 feet tall, which is taller than Mark's window (which is 20 feet off the ground).\nTherefore, the answer is D) 2.
2025-12-24 14:59:02 | INFO | Q659 id=gsm8k_mcq_00658 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=It took Finley 30 minutes to cook rice, so it took her 30 + 20 = 50 minutes to cook pork. The beans took half the combined cooking time of pork and rice, which is 50 / 2 = 25 minutes. So, it took Finley 50 + 25 = 75 minutes to cook all three foods. Therefore, the answer is B) 75.
