2025-12-24 14:59:06 | INFO | Q598 id=gsm8k_mcq_00597 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The angles in a triangle sum up to 180 degrees. Let x be the smallest angle. Then the other two angles are 2x and 3x. Adding all the angles we get 180 = x + 2x + 3x which simplifies to 6x = 180. So x = 30. Therefore, the largest angle is 3x = 3 * 30 = 90 degrees. The answer is A) 90
