2025-12-24 14:59:37 | INFO | Q682 id=gsm8k_mcq_00681 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nKatarina = Max - 5\nMax = Cookie Monster + 12\nSummer = Max + 23\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the third equation gives:\n\nSummer = (Cookie Monster + 12) + 23\nSummer = Cookie Monster + 35\n\nSubstituting that back into the first equation gives:\n\nKatarina = Max - 5\nKatarina = (Cookie Monster + 35) - 5\nKatarina = Cookie Monster + 30\n\nTherefore, Katarina has 30 fewer cookies than Max, who has 35 more cookies than the Cookie Monster. Substituting those values into the equation for Max gives:\n\nMax = Cookie Monster + 35\nMax = 35 + 35\nMax = 70\n\nFinally, substituting that value for Max into the equation for Katarina gives:\n\nKatarina = 70 - 5\nKatarina = 65\n\nTherefore, Katarina has 65 cookies. Adding the number of cookies each person has gives a total of:\n\n68 + 70 + 35 + 65 = 224\n\nTherefore, they have a total of 224 cookies.\n\nAnswer: A) 268
