2025-12-24 14:59:55 | INFO | Q694 id=gsm8k_mcq_00693 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of colored squares on Brittany's comforter can be calculated as follows:\n\n  * There are 14 red squares\n  * There are 4 more blue squares than red squares, so there are 14 + 4 = 18 blue squares\n  * There are 6 more green squares than blue squares, so there are 18 + 6 = 24 green squares\n  * There are 12 fewer white squares than green squares, so there are 24 - 12 = 12 white squares\n\nTherefore, the total number of colored squares on Brittany's comforter is:\n\n  * 14 red squares\n  * 18 blue squares\n  * 24 green squares\n  * 12 white squares\n\nMultiplying each of these quantities by the size of each square (1 foot by 1 foot), we get:\n\n  * 14 x 1 x 1 = 14 square feet\n  * 18 x 1 x 1 = 18 square feet\n  * 24 x 1 x 1 = 24 square feet\n  * 12 x 1 x 1 = 12 square feet\n\nAdding all of these quantities together, we get:\n\n  * 14 + 18 + 24 + 12 = 70 square feet\n\nTherefore, Brittany's comforter is 70 square feet.\n\nAnswer: C) 68
