2025-12-24 15:00:21 | INFO | Q710 id=gsm8k_mcq_00709 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The ice cream factory can make 100 quarts of chocolate ice cream in 2 hours, which means it has a production rate of 50 quarts per hour. It can also make 50 quarts of vanilla ice cream in 4 hours, which means its production rate is 12.5 quarts per hour.\nIf the factory runs continuously for 48 hours, it will be able to produce a total of 48 hours x 50 quarts per hour = 2400 quarts of chocolate ice cream.\nTherefore, the answer is D) 2400.
