2025-12-24 15:00:38 | INFO | Q719 id=gsm8k_mcq_00718 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by calculating the number of people who receive a job offer:\n\n30% of 100 = 30\n20% of 30 = 6\n\nSo, 6 people receive a job offer.\n\nNext, we need to find out how many people accept the job offer:\n\n6 / 3 = 2\n\nTherefore, 2 people accept the job offer.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 2.
