2025-12-24 15:00:53 | INFO | Q665 id=gsm8k_mcq_00664 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=If John spends 2 hours per class for 6 weeks, then he spends a total of 2 * 6 = 12 hours in class. If he learns a new recipe for every 1.5 hours of class time, then he will learn 12 / 1.5 = 8 new recipes. Therefore, the answer is C) 24.
