2025-12-24 15:01:12 | INFO | Q675 id=gsm8k_mcq_00674 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The given information states that Mrs. Jameson's bamboo grows up to 30 inches a day and today its height is 20 feet. We need to find out how many days it will take for the bamboo to grow to a height of 600 inches.\nTo solve this problem, we can set up an equation using the rate of growth of the bamboo. Let x be the number of days it takes for the bamboo to grow to a height of 600 inches. Then, we can write the equation as follows:\n30x = 600\nDividing both sides by 30, we get:\nx = 20\nTherefore, it will take 20 days for Mrs. Jameson's bamboo to grow to a height of 600 inches.\nAnswer: C) 20
