2025-12-24 15:01:52 | INFO | Q688 id=gsm8k_mcq_00687 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred= | followup_correct=False | raw=The problem states that there is one set of twins and one set of triplets, and one twin is seven years older than one triplet. We can represent the ages of the individuals as follows:\n\n  * T = Twin 1\n  * T2 = Twin 2\n  * T3 = Twin 3\n  * T4 = Twin 4 (the seven-year-old twin)\n  * T5 = Twin 5 (the triplet)\n\nWe are given that the combined ages of all five individuals is 44. Using algebraic equations, we can write the following system of equations:\n\n  * T + T2 + T3 + T4 + T5 = 44\n  * T2 - T4 = 7\n\nSolving the second equation for T2, we get:\n\n  * T2 = T4 + 7\n\nSubstituting this expression for T2 into the first equation, we get:\n\n  * T + (T4 + 7) + T3 + T4 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 2T4 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 2(T4 - T2) + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 2(7) + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44\n  * T + T4 + T3 + 14 + T5 = 44
2025-12-24 15:01:54 | INFO | Q768 id=gsm8k_mcq_00767 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=To make 1 liter of juice, Sam needs 5 kilograms of oranges which cost $3 per kilogram. So, to make 1 liter of juice, Sam would have to spend $3 * 5 = $15\. To make 4 liters of juice, Sam would need 4 * 5 = 20 kilograms of oranges. Therefore, Sam would have to spend $20 * 3 = $60 to make 4 liters of juice. Answer: D) 60
