2025-12-24 15:02:48 | INFO | Q722 id=gsm8k_mcq_00721 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=We can calculate Helga's total number of taps by multiplying the number of taps per minute by the duration of the dance in minutes. Since Helga raises her arms during two out of five minutes, we will consider only those two minutes.\n\nFor the first minute, Helga taps both feet at a rate of 300 + 250 = 550 taps per minute.\nFor the second minute, her tap rate slows down to 200 taps per minute with each foot, so she taps 200 x 2 = 400 times.\n\nTherefore, the combined total number of times that she taps both of her feet during these two minutes is 550 + 400 = 950 taps.\n\nSo the answer is C) 2450.
