2025-12-24 15:04:17 | INFO | Q848 id=gsm8k_mcq_00847 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=After one year, Brenda will have earned simple interest equal to 3/4 * $300 = $225. So she will have a total of $300 + $225 = $525. After two years, she will earn simple interest on $525, which is 3/4 * $525 = $393.75. So she will have a total of $525 + $393.75 = $918.75. After three years, she will earn simple interest on $918.75, which is 3/4 * $918.75 = $688.54. So she will have a total of $918.75 + $688.54 = $1608.29. Therefore, the correct answer is C) 525.
2025-12-24 15:04:18 | INFO | Q777 id=gsm8k_mcq_00776 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The original price of the laptop is $1000, and there is a 20% discount available. To calculate the discounted price, we need to find 20% of $1000.\nTo find 20% of a number, we divide that number by 100 and multiply the result by 20. In this case, 20% of $1000 is equal to:\n$1000 / 100 * 20 = $200\nSo, if you get a 20% discount on a laptop priced at $1000, you will have to pay $800. Therefore, the correct answer is B) $800.
