2025-12-24 15:07:16 | INFO | Q956 id=gsm8k_mcq_00955 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of occupied beds in the hospital after two weeks is:\n\n  * Week 1: 50 patients per day x 7 days = 350 patients\n  * Week 2: 350 patients + 50 patients = 400 patients\n\nSo, the total number of occupied beds after two weeks is 400 patients.\n\nTherefore, the number of unoccupied beds in the hospital after two weeks is:\n\n  * Total beds - Occupied beds = 1000 beds - 400 beds = 600 beds\n\nHence, the answer is A) 800.
2025-12-24 15:07:19 | INFO | Q958 id=gsm8k_mcq_00957 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nShawna = 3Aliya\nShawna's father = 5Shawna\n\nSubstituting the value of Shawna into the second equation, we get:\n\nShawna's father = 5(3Aliya)\nShawna's father = 15Aliya\n\nTherefore, Shawna's father is 15 years old.\n\nAnswer: A) 15
