2025-12-24 15:07:45 | INFO | Q975 id=gsm8k_mcq_00974 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate how many hours Tyler needs to work to afford his books, we need to determine how much money he needs to earn to purchase all three books. The total cost of the books is $18 + $13 + $8 = $39.\nWe can set up an equation to represent this as follows:\n$39 = $5x\nWhere x represents the number of hours Tyler needs to work.\nSolving for x, we get:\nx = $39 / $5\nx = 7.8\nTherefore, Tyler needs to work 7.8 hours to afford his books.\nSince Tyler cannot work fractional hours, we round up to 8 hours.\nTherefore, Tyler needs to work 8 hours to afford his books.\nAnswer: C) 8
