2025-12-24 15:08:09 | INFO | Q987 id=gsm8k_mcq_00986 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Katherine will spend $17.50 filling all 5 hanging baskets.\nTo find the total cost, we need to calculate the cost of 3 petunias per basket and 2 sweet potato vines per basket, then multiply that number by 5 since there are 5 hanging baskets.\nThe cost of 3 petunias per basket is $3.00 x 3 = $9.00\. The cost of 2 sweet potato vines per basket is $2.50 x 2 = $5.00\. Total cost per basket is $9.00 + $5.00 = $14.00\. To find the total cost of all 5 hanging baskets, we multiply the cost per basket by 5: $14.00 x 5 = $70.00\. Answer: C) 70
