2025-12-24 15:08:50 | INFO | Q931 id=gsm8k_mcq_00930 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of toys that Sophie got for her nephew is 62. We know that the bag of building blocks has 31 blocks, the bin of stuffed animals has 8 stuffed animals, and the tower of stacking rings has 9 multicolored rings. We also know that Sophie recently bought a tube of bouncy balls, which brings her total number of toys up to 62. Therefore, the number of bouncy balls that came in the tube is equal to the total number of toys Sophie got for her nephew minus the number of toys from the other three categories. This means that the number of bouncy balls is equal to 62 - 31 - 8 - 9 = 22. Therefore, the answer is D) 22.
2025-12-24 15:08:53 | INFO | Q1011 id=gsm8k_mcq_01010 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can determine that:\n\n  * Bethany can run 10 laps in one hour\n  * Trey can run 4 more laps than Bethany, so he can run 10 + 4 = 14 laps in one hour\n  * Shaelyn can run half as many laps as Trey, who can run 14 laps, so Shaelyn can run 14 / 2 = 7 laps in one hour\n  * Quinn can run 2 fewer laps than Shaelyn, who can run 7 laps, so Quinn can run 7 - 2 = 5 laps in one hour\n\nTherefore, Bethany can run 10 laps - 5 laps = 5 laps more than Quinn in one hour.\n\nAnswer: D) 5
