2025-12-24 15:09:26 | INFO | Q949 id=gsm8k_mcq_00948 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate the total commission earned from the sales of 6 copies of the New York Times and 10 copies of the Wall Street Journal, we need to find the amount of commission earned from each newspaper and then add them together.\n\nFirst, let's find the commission earned from the New York Times:\n\nThe cost of each New York Times is $5, and Cayley earns a 10% commission on each copy sold. To find the commission earned, we can multiply the cost by the commission rate:\n\n$5 * 10% = $0.50\n\nSo, Cayley will earn $0.50 per copy of the New York Times sold.\n\nNext, let's find the commission earned from the Wall Street Journal:\n\nThe cost of each Wall Street Journal is $15, and Cayley earns an 8% commission on each copy sold. To find the commission earned, we can multiply the cost by the commission rate:\n\n$15 * 8% = $1.20\n\nSo, Cayley will earn $1.20 per copy of the Wall Street Journal sold.\n\nFinally, to find the total commission earned, we can add the commission earned from each newspaper together:\n\n$0.50 + $1.20 = $1.70\n\nTherefore, Cayley will earn a total of $1.70 from the sales of 6 copies of the New York Times and 10 copies of the Wall Street Journal if each costs $5 and $15 respectively.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 17.40.
2025-12-24 15:09:30 | INFO | Q1029 id=gsm8k_mcq_01028 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Tom needs to make a monthly payment of 10% of the remaining amount after he pays for part of the bedroom set with the money from selling his old bedroom.\nFirst, let's find out how much money Tom has left over after paying for part of the bedroom set:\n$3000 - $1000 = $2000\nNext, we need to find out how much the remaining amount is after Tom makes his monthly payment. We can do this by multiplying the remaining amount by 10% (or 0.1):\n$2000 x 0.1 = $200\nTherefore, Tom has to pay $200 per month for the bedroom set.\nAnswer: B) $200
