2025-12-24 15:11:35 | INFO | Q1102 id=gsm8k_mcq_01101 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\nAmber + Micah + Ahito = 52\n\nSubstituting the values given in the problem, we get:\n\n8 + 3.5(8) + Ahito = 52\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\n8 + 28 + Ahito = 52\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n36 + Ahito = 52\n\nSubtracting 36 from both sides, we get:\n\nAhito = 52 - 36\n\nSimplifying the right-hand side of the equation, we get:\n\nAhito = 16\n\nTherefore, Ahito ran 16 miles.\n\nAnswer: A) 16
2025-12-24 15:11:37 | INFO | Q1028 id=gsm8k_mcq_01027 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The cost of the first package is $3, which is equal to 2 sandwiches at a certain price per sandwich. The second package costs $6, which is equal to 4 sandwiches at a certain price per sandwich. Therefore, the price per sandwich is $3/2 = $1.50 for both packages. Since the price of the third package is not indicated, we can assume that it is also proportional to the number of sandwiches. Therefore, the price of the third package will be 8 * $1.50 = $12\. Answer: B
