2025-12-24 15:11:46 | INFO | Q1106 id=gsm8k_mcq_01105 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate how many more years Lauren needs to work, we can set up an equation based on the information given. Let x be the number of additional years Lauren needs to work. We know that she needs to save 20% of her current annual salary for 20 years, which is 20/100 * $100,000 = $20,000. Additionally, we know that she wants to live off 40% of her current annual salary, which is 40/100 * $100,000 = $40,000. Since these two amounts must equal $20,000, we can write the equation as follows:\n$20,000 = $40,000 / (x + 20)\nSolving for x gives us:\nx = 8\nTherefore, Lauren needs to work for another 8 years to save enough money for retirement. Answer: A
