2025-12-24 15:11:50 | INFO | Q1108 id=gsm8k_mcq_01107 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of students in the school can be found by multiplying the percentage of boys by the total number of students. If 40% of the school population is made up of 240 boys, then the total number of students in the school is 240 / 0.4 = 600. Since there are 600 students in the school and 40% of them are girls, the number of girls in the school is 600 * 0.4 = 240. Therefore, the answer is A) 360.
