2025-12-24 15:12:31 | INFO | Q1065 id=gsm8k_mcq_01064 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of classes that visited the Science Center last week is the sum of the number of classes that visited each day. We can calculate this by adding up the number of classes that visited each day:\n\nOn Monday: 32 classes\nOn Tuesday: twice as many as Monday, which is 32 x 2 = 64 classes\nOn Wednesday: three times as many as Tuesday, which is 64 x 3 = 192 classes\nOn Thursday: 30 classes\nOn Friday: 25 classes\n\nTo find the total number of classes, we add up these numbers:\n\n32 + 64 + 192 + 30 + 25 = 343 classes\n\nTherefore, the Science Center hosted a total of 343 classes last week.\n\nAnswer: D) 343
