2025-12-24 15:12:39 | INFO | Q1141 id=gsm8k_mcq_01140 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the equation as follows:\n\nGomer ate 5 less than 23 scoops = 23 - 5 = 18 scoops\n\nIt also states that it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes. We can rearrange this equation as follows:\n\n6 - 3 = 3 scoops\n3 less than 3 scoops = 0 scoops\n\nTherefore, it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 0 scoops of mashed potatoes, which means that 6 is the number of potatoes needed to make 3 scoops of mashed potatoes.\n\nSince Gomer ate 18 scoops of mashed potatoes, we can conclude that he ate 6 * 3 = 18 potatoes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 18.
2025-12-24 15:12:41 | INFO | Q1071 id=gsm8k_mcq_01070 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, Dennis needs 6 pounds of butter to make his 6 dozen croissants. The grocery store is currently offering a promotion where he can buy 1 pound of butter and get 1/2 off, so he will pay $4.00 for 1 pound of butter. To find out how much it will cost him to purchase 6 pounds of butter, we need to multiply the cost per pound by the number of pounds he needs. In this case, the cost would be $4.00 x 6 = $24.00. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 24.
