2025-12-24 15:16:20 | INFO | Q1270 id=gsm8k_mcq_01269 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by finding the total distance Elvis traveled during each leg of the journey.\nHe traveled west for 5 hours at an average speed of 18 mph, so he traveled 5 * 18 = 90 miles.\nHe then traveled east for 8 hours at an average speed of 18 mph, so he traveled 8 * 18 = 144 miles.\nThe total distance Elvis traveled is 90 + 144 = 234 miles.\nTherefore, he is 234 miles away from his house now. The answer is D.
2025-12-24 15:16:22 | INFO | Q1192 id=gsm8k_mcq_01191 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the cost of May's hair cut and color can be calculated as follows:\n\nThe total length of hair cut is 8 inches - 10 inches = -2 inches. Since the rate of charge is $30 per inch, the cost of cutting 2 inches would be 2 * $30 = $60.\n\nThe cost of coloring her hair is $40. Therefore, the total cost of her hair cut and color is $60 + $40 = $100.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 100.
2025-12-24 15:16:24 | INFO | Q1273 id=gsm8k_mcq_01272 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Helen paid $80 for one night at the hotel. Each bus trip was 10% of the price of one night at the hotel, so each bus trip cost $80 * 10% = $8. Helen rode the bus seven times during her trip, so she paid $8 * 7 = $56 for bus trips. Adding the cost of the hotel, Helen paid $80 + $56 = $136 for the hotel and bus travels during her trip. The correct answer is C) 136.
