2025-12-24 15:17:09 | INFO | Q1221 id=gsm8k_mcq_01220 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The statement given is that the longer piece is four times longer than the shorter piece. We can use this information to determine the length of the longer piece.\nFirst, we need to find the relationship between the lengths of the two pieces. Let's say the length of the shorter piece is x feet. Then, the length of the longer piece would be 4x feet.\nWe know that the total length of the board is 40 feet, so x + 4x = 40. Combining like terms, we get 5x = 40. Dividing both sides by 5, we get x = 8.\nTherefore, the length of the shorter piece is 8 feet, and the length of the longer piece is 4 * 8 = 32 feet.\nAnswer: D) 32
2025-12-24 15:17:11 | INFO | Q1304 id=gsm8k_mcq_01303 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=It takes 2 weeks to fill in all the holes.\nExplanation:\nNate's dog digs 6 holes per day for 14 days, so he digs a total of 6 * 14 = 84 holes. When Nate comes back, he starts filling in 9 holes per day, which will take him 84 / 9 = 9 days to fill in all the holes. However, the dog continues to dig 6 new holes every night, so over those 9 days, the dog will dig an additional 6 * 9 = 54 holes. Therefore, it will take an additional 54 / 6 = 9 days to fill in all the holes that the dog dug. Altogether, it will take 9 + 9 = 18 days to fill in all the holes. Since there are 7 days in a week, it will take 18 / 7 = 2 weeks to fill in all the holes. Answer: D) 2
