2025-12-24 15:17:27 | INFO | Q1233 id=gsm8k_mcq_01232 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Eve started with 20 pieces of pomelos and gave away some to her friend, so she is left with 1/4 of the original amount. To find out how many pomelos she gave away, we can set up the equation 20 = 1/4 * x, where x represents the number of pomelos Eve gave away. Solving for x gives us x = 80, so Eve gave away 80 pomelos. The correct answer is C: 15.
2025-12-24 15:17:30 | INFO | Q1235 id=gsm8k_mcq_01234 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The statement given is that Regina wrote nine novels last year, which is three-quarters of the number of novels she has written this year. To find out how many novels Regina has written this year, we need to first calculate three-quarters of nine novels, which is equal to 9 x 3 / 4 = 6.5 novels. However, since we cannot write half a novel, we must round this up to 7 novels. Therefore, Regina has written 7 novels this year. The answer is C.
2025-12-24 15:17:31 | INFO | Q1318 id=gsm8k_mcq_01317 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\n20x + 4y = 70\n\nWhere x represents the number of cows and y represents the number of chickens.\n\nWe can simplify the equation by dividing both sides by 2:\n\n10x + 2y = 35\n\nSubtracting 10x from both sides gives us:\n\n2y = 25\n\nDividing both sides by 2 gives us:\n\ny = 12.5\n\nSince we cannot have half an animal, we must round down to 12. Therefore, there are 12 chickens on the farm.\n\nAnswer: C) 12
2025-12-24 15:17:33 | INFO | Q1237 id=gsm8k_mcq_01236 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of grapes used by Madeline and her brother is 6 + 5 x 6 = 36 grapes. Since their mother used the remaining grapes to make 4 pies, she used 36 - 4 x 12 = 24 grapes. Therefore, there were 24 grapes at the beginning if the pie recipe calls for 12 grapes per pie.\n\nAnswer: D) 78
