2025-12-24 15:18:06 | INFO | Q1257 id=gsm8k_mcq_01256 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total distance that Phineas needs to travel is 200 yards, which is split into two parts: half on land and half in water.\nLet x be the number of minutes it takes Phineas to travel the distance on land. Since he travels at a speed of 20 yards per minute, it will take him x minutes to travel the first part of the journey.\nThe second part of the journey is in the water, and Phineas travels at a speed of 10 yards per minute. To find the time it takes him to travel this part of the journey, we can set up the equation: 200/2 = 10x. Solving for x gives us x = 40.\nTherefore, the total time it takes Phineas to travel the entire distance is 40 + x minutes. Substituting x = 40 into the equation gives us a total time of 80 minutes.\nSo the answer is C) 20.
