2025-12-24 15:22:30 | INFO | Q63 id=gsm8k_mcq_00062 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=If Marcy works for the same company for 40 years, she gets an annual pension of $50,000/year. Starting after 20 years, she becomes entitled to 5% of the value of the pension per year. This means that after 20 years, her pension will increase by 5% annually.\nTherefore, if she quits after 30 years, her annual pension will be higher than $50,000 because it will have increased by 5% annually for 10 years. To calculate her annual pension, we need to determine the value of her pension at the time she quits.\nLet's assume that the value of her pension at the time she quits is V. We can calculate V as follows:\nV = $50,000 * (1 + 5%)^20\nV = $50,000 * (1.05)^20\nV = $50,000 * 1.1025\nV = $58,643.75\nTherefore, Marcy's annual pension when she quits will be $58,643.75. The closest option among the choices is A) $37,500, which is incorrect. The correct answer is D) $58,643.75.
2025-12-24 15:22:31 | INFO | Q54 id=gsm8k_mcq_00053 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=On Thursday, the mechanic earns $60 x 6 = $360 from repairing truck tires and $40 x 4 = $160 from repairing car tires. So, on Thursday, the mechanic earns a total of $360 + $160 = $520. On Friday, the mechanic earns $40 x 12 = $480 from repairing car tires. Therefore, on Friday, the mechanic earns a total of $480 - $0 = $480. So, on the day with higher revenue, which is Friday, the mechanic earned a total of $480 + $520 = $900. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 80.
