2025-12-24 15:27:46 | INFO | Q212 id=gsm8k_mcq_00211 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\n3R + 5W = 42\n\nWhere R represents the number of red chickens and W represents the number of white chickens.\n\nWe also know that there are two more white chickens than red chickens. Let's represent this with another equation:\n\nW = R + 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\n3R + 5(R+2) = 42\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n3R + 5R + 10 = 42\n8R = 32\nR = 4\n\nTherefore, Jerry has 4 red chickens. Answer: D) 3
