2025-12-24 15:28:03 | INFO | Q244 id=gsm8k_mcq_00243 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To solve this problem, we need to calculate how many minutes Jason has used for his calls so far this month.\nFirst, we add up the number of minutes he spends on daily calls with his boss: 15 minutes x 30 days = 450 minutes\nNext, we add the number of extra minutes he has used for calls to other people: 300 minutes\nFinally, we subtract these two amounts from his monthly phone plan: 1000 minutes - 450 minutes - 300 minutes = 250 minutes\nTherefore, Jason has 250 minutes left in his phone plan for this month.\nAnswer: C) 250
