2025-12-24 15:28:31 | INFO | Q237 id=gsm8k_mcq_00236 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of pens that Ram gets to have after buying 25 pens and using them to make new pens when the ink runs low depends on how many pens he needs before running out of ink. If Ram needs 5 pens to mix with each other to make one full pen, then he will need to use 25/5=5 sets of 5 pens to make new pens. In this case, he will end up with a total of 5*5=25 pens. If Ram needs more than 5 pens to make one full pen, then he will not have enough pens left over after making new pens from the 25 purchased pens. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 25.
2025-12-24 15:28:31 | INFO | Q253 id=gsm8k_mcq_00252 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=My apologies for the confusion in my previous response. Let me provide a revised answer based on the information provided in the audio.\nAccording to the information given in the audio, last night Rick killed ten wolves and fifteen cougars. Today, he killed three times as many wolves as cougars and three fewer cougars than the previous night. Let's break down the information to find out how many animals Rick killed today.\nFirst, we know that Rick killed three times as many wolves as cougars today. Let's call the number of wolves he killed today x. Therefore, the number of cougars he killed today is 3x.\nWe also know that Rick killed three fewer cougars today than the previous night. Let's call the number of cougars he killed the previous night y. Therefore, the number of cougars he killed today is y - 3.\nUsing this information, we can set up two equations to represent the total number of wolves and cougars that Rick killed yesterday and today:\ny + x = 10 + 15 (the total number of wolves and cougars killed last night)\n3x + (y - 3) = (x * 3) + (y - 3) (the total number of wolves and cougars killed today)\nSimplifying the second equation, we get:\n3x + y - 3 = 3x + y - 3 (since y - 3 is the same in both equations)\nTherefore, the two equations are equal, which means they represent the same information. This tells us that the value of x and y must be the same.\nSubstituting the value of y from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n3x + (10 + 15) - 3 = 3x + (x - 3)\nSimplifying the right-hand side of the equation, we get:\n3x + 22 = 3x + x - 3\nTherefore, the left-hand side of the equation represents the total number of wolves and cougars killed today, which is 3x + 22. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get:\n3x + 22 = 10 + 15\nSolving for x, we get:\n3x = 37\nx = 12.37\nTherefore, the number of wolves that Rick killed today is approximately 12.37. Since we cannot have a fraction of an animal, we need to round this number down to 12. Therefore, the total number of animals that Rick killed today is 12.\nFinally, we can use the information given in the audio to determine the total number of animals that Rick killed yesterday. We know that yesterday Rick killed three fewer cougars than the previous night, so the number of cougars he killed yesterday was y - 3. We also know that yesterday Rick killed ten wolves, so the total number of wolves and cougars he killed yesterday was y + 10. Using these values, we can write the following equation:\ny + 10 = 10 + 15 (the total number of wolves and cougars killed yesterday)\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\ny = 25\nTherefore, the number of cougars that Rick killed yesterday was 25. Since yesterday Rick also killed ten wolves, the total number of wolves and cougars he killed yesterday was 25 + 10 = 35.\nTherefore, the total number of animals that Rick killed yesterday and today is 35 + 12 = 47. Answer: \boxed{D} (47).
