2025-12-24 15:28:38 | INFO | Q241 id=gsm8k_mcq_00240 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJames = Robert + 6\nJohn = 2 * (Robert + 6)\nJohn = 2 * Robert + 12\n\nWe are given that John has 54 candies, so:\n\n2 * Robert + 12 = 54\n2 * Robert = 42\nRobert = 21\n\nSubstituting this value for Robert into the equation for John, we get:\n\nJohn = 2 * 21 + 12\nJohn = 42 + 12\nJohn = 54\n\nTherefore, John has 54 candies, which means he has 54 - 6 = 48 more candies than James. The answer is A) 33.
