2025-12-24 15:28:56 | INFO | Q250 id=gsm8k_mcq_00249 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=On Monday, Sue ate 4 times as many cookies as her sister who ate 5 cookies. This means Sue ate 4 * 5 = 20 cookies on Monday. On Tuesday, Sue ate twice as many cookies as her sister who ate 13 cookies. This means Sue ate 2 * 13 = 26 cookies on Tuesday. In total, Sue ate 20 + 26 = 46 cookies over the two days. If each cookie has 200 calories, then Sue consumed a total of 46 * 200 = 9,200 calories. Her sister consumed a total of 5 + 13 = 18 cookies over the two days. If each cookie has 200 calories, then Sue consumed 9,200 - 18 * 200 = 2,400 more calories than her sister. Therefore, the correct answer is (D) 2,400.
