2025-12-24 15:31:01 | INFO | Q313 id=gsm8k_mcq_00312 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equations:\n\nTrent = Jane + 5\nJane = Quinn - 3\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\nTrent = (Quinn - 3) + 5\nTrent = Quinn + 2\n\nGiven that Quinn is 30, we can substitute this value into the equation above to find Trent's age:\n\nTrent = 30 + 2\nTrent = 32\n\nTherefore, Trent is 32 years old.\n\nAnswer: A) 32
2025-12-24 15:31:06 | INFO | Q339 id=gsm8k_mcq_00338 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The problem states that the class of 200 students is split into three groups with two groups having the same number of students and the third group being 10 less than each of the other groups. We can start by finding the total number of students in the two groups with the same number of students.\nLet x be the number of students in each of these two groups. Then, we have:\n2x + 10 = 200\nSolving for x gives us:\n2x = 190\nx = 95\nSo there are 95 students in each of the two groups with the same number of students. Therefore, the total number of students in these two groups is:\n2 * 95 = 190\nNow we need to find the number of students in the smallest group. The problem tells us that the smallest group is 10 less than each of the other groups. Since there are two groups with the same number of students, each of these groups has 95 students. Therefore, the smallest group is 10 less than 95, which means it has:\n95 - 10 = 85 students\nTherefore, there are 85 students in the smallest group. The answer is C) 57.
