2025-12-24 15:36:02 | INFO | Q468 id=gsm8k_mcq_00467 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=My apologies, let me rephrase my previous response.\nBased on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the number of pieces of laundry for each room as follows:\n\n- Two sheets\n- One comforter\n- Twice as many pillow cases as sheets, which means 2 x 2 = 4 pillow cases\n- Twice as many towels as pillow cases, which means 2 x 4 = 8 towels\n\nTherefore, the total number of pieces of laundry for each room is:\n\n- Two sheets + one comforter + four pillow cases + eight towels = 15 pieces of laundry\n\nSince there are 80 rooms in the hotel, the total number of pieces of laundry would be:\n\n- 80 rooms x 15 pieces of laundry/room = 1200 pieces of laundry\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is option C: 1200.\n\nThank you for bringing this to my attention.
