2025-12-24 15:40:11 | INFO | Q585 id=gsm8k_mcq_00584 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, the cost of each box of contacts is $100.00, and there is a current 10% discount, so the discounted price of each box is $100.00 * (1 - 10%) = $100.00 * 90% = $90.00.\nIf Pete buys two boxes of contacts, he will receive a total of 90 + 90 = 180 single use contacts. Since each box contains 90 contacts, the total number of pairs of contacts that Pete will receive is 180 / 90 = 2 pairs.\nTherefore, the cost of each pair of contacts will be $90.00 / 2 pairs = $45.00. The closest option among A/B/C/D is C) $2.\nSo the final answer is C) $2.
