2025-12-24 15:40:37 | INFO | Q657 id=gsm8k_mcq_00656 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Mike has 30 days to complete the reading, and he plans to read 10 pages per day. To find out how many days before the deadline he will finish his reading, we can divide the total number of pages by the number of pages he plans to read each day.\n200 / 10 = 20\nTherefore, Mike will finish his reading 20 days before the deadline. So the answer is C: 20.
2025-12-24 15:40:39 | INFO | Q598 id=gsm8k_mcq_00597 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The problem states that the sum of the three angles in a triangle is 180 degrees. Let's call the smallest angle x. Then, we know that one angle is twice x, which means it is 2x. And another angle is three times x, which means it is 3x.\nSince the sum of all three angles is 180, we can write the equation as follows:\nx + 2x + 3x = 180\nCombining like terms, we get:\n6x = 180\nDividing both sides by 6, we get:\nx = 30\nTherefore, the smallest angle in the triangle is 30 degrees. Since one angle is three times the smallest angle, the other angle is 3 * 30 = 90 degrees. And since one angle is twice the smallest angle, the largest angle is 2 * 30 = 60 degrees.\nSo the measure of the largest angle in the triangle is 60 degrees, which corresponds to choice B.
