2025-12-24 15:41:04 | INFO | Q608 id=gsm8k_mcq_00607 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The jumbo bottle of shampoo costs $24.00. The directions say to use 2 pumps of shampoo and this will give you 120 washings. If Jackie only uses 1 pump per wash, how much will each pump cost, in cents?\n\nTo calculate the cost of each pump, we need to divide the total cost of the shampoo by the number of washes it will provide when used according to the instructions.\nFirst, let's find out how many cents are in $24.00:\n\n$24.00 = 24 x 100 cents\n\nSo, $24.00 is equal to 2400 cents.\n\nNext, let's find out how many washes the jumbo bottle of shampoo will provide when used according to the instructions:\n\n120 washings = 120 x 1 pump\n\nSince Jackie only uses 1 pump per wash, she will use the entire bottle of shampoo for 120 washes.\n\nFinally, let's find out how much each pump will cost if the entire bottle of shampoo is used for 120 washes:\n\n2400 cents / 120 washes = 20 cents/pump\n\nTherefore, each pump of the jumbo bottle of shampoo will cost 20 cents.\n\nAnswer: A) 20
