2025-12-24 15:41:46 | INFO | Q634 id=gsm8k_mcq_00633 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=My apologies for the confusion. Let me rephrase the question and provide the answer.\n\nQuestion: If Bob is 75 miles ahead of Tom, who is driving at 55 mph, and Tom is driving at 70 mph, how long will it take for Tom to catch up with Bob?\nChoice: A) 5 hours B) 7.5 hours C) 0.6 hours D) 1.36 hours\n\nAnswer: A) 5 hours\n\nTo determine how long it will take for Tom to catch up with Bob, we can use the formula:\n\ntime = distance / speed\n\nFirst, let's find the relative speeds of both vehicles. We can do this by subtracting the speed of one vehicle from the other:\n\nrelative speed of Tom = 70 mph - 55 mph = 15 mph\n\nNow we can plug these values into the time formula:\n\ntime = 75 miles / 15 mph = 5 hours\n\nTherefore, it will take Tom 5 hours to catch up with Bob.
