2025-12-24 15:44:07 | INFO | Q778 id=gsm8k_mcq_00777 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate the total cost of replacing Mike's movie collection with digital versions, we need to determine how many of the movies are in series and how many are older movies. We can then use this information to calculate the cost of each type of movie and add them up.\n\nFirst, we find that a third of the movies are in various series, so there are 600 / 3 = 200 movies in series. We also know that we can buy these movies for only $6 each, so the total cost of the series is 200 * $6 = $120.\n\nNext, we find that 40% of the remaining movies are older movies, which means that there are 600 - 200 = 400 movies left. We also know that the cost of these older movies is $5 each, so the total cost of the older movies is 400 * $5 = $200.\n\nFinally, we add the cost of the series and the cost of the older movies together to get a total cost of $120 + $200 = $320.\n\nTherefore, the total cost of replacing Mike's movie collection with digital versions is $320. Answer: D) 3200
