2025-12-24 15:44:14 | INFO | Q714 id=gsm8k_mcq_00713 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=To find out how many mosaic tiles Mr. Borden would need to cover two-thirds of his 36 sq ft bathroom, we need to calculate the area that needs to be covered. \n\nTo do this, we can multiply the total area of the bathroom by two-thirds:\n\n36 sq ft x 2 / 3 = 24 sq ft\n\nNow we can use the number of tiles needed per square foot to find out how many tiles Mr. Borden would need for the entire bathroom:\n\n24 sq ft x 24 tiles/sq ft = 576 tiles\n\nTherefore, Mr. Borden would need 576 mosaic tiles to cover two-thirds of his 36 sq ft bathroom.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 576.
