2025-12-24 15:44:21 | INFO | Q784 id=gsm8k_mcq_00783 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The information provided states that Bob initially had 7 fish in his ornamental fish pond, 3 of which were orange and 4 were white. It also states that he went to the pet store and had a sales assistant dip out 17 fish from a mixed tank containing both white and orange fish. After adding these new fish to his pond, he found that he now had twice as many orange fish as white fish.\nTo determine how many white fish Bob bought at the store, we can set up an equation based on the information given. Let x be the number of white fish that Bob bought at the store. We know that before going to the store, Bob had 7 fish in his pond, 3 of which were orange and 4 of which were white. After buying the additional fish, he now has 7 + 17 = 24 fish in his pond. We also know that he now has twice as many orange fish as white fish, which means he has 24/2 = 12 orange fish. Since there were 4 white fish before buying the additional fish, this means that Bob bought 12 - 4 = 8 white fish at the store.\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 8.
