2025-12-24 15:46:53 | INFO | Q795 id=gsm8k_mcq_00794 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The zookeeper has counted 12 female lions, which means there are 1/2 as many male lions as female lions. Therefore, there are 12 / 2 = 6 male lions. Adding the number of female and male lions gives us a total of 12 + 6 = 18 lions. Additionally, the zookeeper has counted 14 lion cubs, so we add these to the total to get 18 + 14 = 32 lions. Therefore, there are 32 lions in the enclosure.\n\nAnswer: C) 32
2025-12-24 15:46:57 | INFO | Q867 id=gsm8k_mcq_00866 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=My apologies for the confusion. Let me provide a correct answer.\nTogether, Sofie, Anne, and Fawn have 85 books. If Sofie has 25 more books than Anne, and Anne has 12 fewer books than Fawn does, we can set up the following equation:\nS + A + F = 85\nS = A + 25\nA = F - 12\nSubstituting the second and third equations into the first equation, we get:\n(A + 25) + (F - 12) + F = 85\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n3F + 13 = 85\nSubtracting 13 from both sides, we get:\n3F = 72\nDividing both sides by 3, we get:\nF = 24\nTherefore, Fawn has 24 books. The answer is C.
2025-12-24 15:46:58 | INFO | Q797 id=gsm8k_mcq_00796 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The company hires 20 new employees every month, so at the end of three months (90 days), it will have hired 20 * 90 = 1800 new employees. The company's initial employee number is 200, so the total number of employees after three months will be 1800 + 200 = 2000. Each employee is paid a $4000 salary per month, so the total amount of money the company pays to its employees after three months will be 2000 * $4000 = $8000000. Therefore, the correct answer is A) $8000000.
