2025-12-24 15:47:04 | INFO | Q871 id=gsm8k_mcq_00870 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To find out how much Keenan spends per week if Madeline pays 60% of the cost, we need to first determine how much Madeline pays for the groceries each month. Since they share the cost of groceries in total, and Madeline pays 60% of the cost, she pays 60/100 * $400 = $240 per month.\nSince there are four weeks in a month, Madeline pays $240 / 4 = $60 per week for groceries.\nTherefore, Keenan spends the remaining amount of $400 - $60 = $340 per week on groceries. Since Keenan shares the cost of groceries with Madeline, he spends $340 / 2 = $170 per week on groceries.\nHence, the correct answer is C) 40.
