2025-12-24 15:50:27 | INFO | Q901 id=gsm8k_mcq_00900 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation for the total number of pages that Denise and Daniel read:\n\nDenise + Daniel = Total Pages Read\n\nYesterday, they read 10 + 13 = 23 pages together.\n\nToday, Denise read 5 more than what Daniel read yesterday, which means she read 10 + 5 = 15 pages. Therefore, the total number of pages that Denise and Daniel read today is 15 + 0 = 15 pages.\n\nSubstituting these values into the equation above, we get:\n\nDenise + Daniel = 23 + 15 = 38 pages\n\nTherefore, the difference between the number of pages that Denise read and Daniel read today is:\n\nDenise - Daniel = 38 - 15 = 23 pages\n\nSo, Denise read 23 more pages than Daniel today. The answer is A) 23.
