2025-12-24 15:51:28 | INFO | Q1017 id=gsm8k_mcq_01016 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The correct answer is A) 135.\nTo arrive at this answer, we can set up an equation for the price of carrots after three years as follows:\nPrice after 3 years = Original price + Increase after 1 year * (3 - 1) Price after 3 years = 120 + 120 * 2 Price after 3 years = 120 + 240 Price after 3 years = 360\nSince the price increase is 5% of the original price, we can calculate the increase after one year as follows:\nIncrease after 1 year = 5% of 120 Increase after 1 year = 6\nSo the price of carrots after one year will be:\nPrice after 1 year = 120 + 6 = 126\nWe can repeat this process to find the price of carrots after two years:\nPrice after 2 years = 126 + 5% of 126 = 126 + 6.3 = 132.3\nSince we cannot sell prices that are not whole numbers, we round 132.3 down to 132. Therefore, the price of carrots after three years will be 135.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 135.
