2025-12-24 15:52:14 | INFO | Q957 id=gsm8k_mcq_00956 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=She sends 7 work emails a day which leaves 16 - 7 = 9 emails left. Two thirds of these are to family, so she sends 9 * (2 / 3) = 6 emails to family. One third of the remaining emails are to her boyfriend, so she sends 6 * (1 / 3) = 2 emails to her boyfriend. Therefore, Robyn sends 7 + 6 + 2 = 15 emails a day to her boyfriend. The answer is A) 6.
2025-12-24 15:52:15 | INFO | Q1039 id=gsm8k_mcq_01038 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by calculating the total amount of money that Jim made during his four years at college, which is $50,000 per year for four years = $200,000.\nNext, we need to determine how much his college degree increased his income by. We are given that his college degree tripled his income, so his income increased by 3倍 = 3 * $200,000 = $600,000.\nNow we can subtract the amount of money Jim made from his job before college ($25,000 per year for four years = $100,000) from the amount of money his college degree increased his income by ($600,000 - $100,000 = $500,000).\nFinally, we can divide the amount of money Jim lost from not working while in school by the amount of money he makes per year with his new job ($500,000 / $50,000 per year = 10 years)\nTherefore, it would take Jim 10 years to earn the money equivalent to the loans and the money lost from not working while in school.\nAnswer: B) 12
