2025-12-24 15:54:22 | INFO | Q1106 id=gsm8k_mcq_01105 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate how many more years Lauren needs to work to save for a retirement period of 20 years, we can use the following formula:\nNumber of years needed = (Total amount of savings needed / Annual savings rate) x Number of years until retirement\nFirst, let's find out how much money Lauren needs to save for a retirement period of 20 years. We can assume that she wants to have 40% of her current annual salary as her retirement income, which means she needs to save:\n40% of $100,000 = $40,000\nTo save this amount over 20 years, she needs to make annual contributions of:\n$40,000 / 20 years = $2,000 per year\nNext, we need to find out how much money Lauren saves each paycheck. If she saves 20% of every paycheck, that means she saves:\n20% of $100,000 = $20,000 per paycheck\nFinally, we can divide the amount she needs to save per year by the amount she saves per paycheck to find out how many more years she needs to work:\n$2,000 per year / $20,000 per paycheck = 0.1 years per paycheck\nThis means that Lauren needs to work 0.1 years (or about 7 hours) per paycheck to save enough money for her retirement. Since she works 5 days a week, that means she needs to work:\n0.1 years per paycheck x 5 days per week = 0.5 hours per week\nTherefore, Lauren needs to work for approximately 50 weeks (or about 3 years) to save enough money for her retirement.\nSo the answer is A) 3.
