2025-12-24 15:54:54 | INFO | Q1126 id=gsm8k_mcq_01125 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each large bag contains 300 M&Ms because 10 ounces x 30 M&Ms = 300 M&Ms.\nSince John buys 3 large bags, he will have a total of 300 M&Ms * 3 = 900 M&Ms.\nIf he puts 10 M&Ms in each small bag, he can make 900 M&Ms / 10 M&Ms = 90 small bags.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 90.
2025-12-24 15:54:55 | INFO | Q1038 id=gsm8k_mcq_01037 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=She spends 22 dollars on cheese because 2 x 11 = 22. She has 28 dollars left because 50 - 22 = 28. She can buy 14 pounds of meat because 28 / 7 = 4. She has 2 dollars left because 28 - 14 x 2 = 2. The answer is A) 2.
2025-12-24 15:54:59 | INFO | Q1040 id=gsm8k_mcq_01039 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=To find the amount of fabric Jim needs, we first need to calculate the area of the bed. The bed is 6 feet long by 8 feet wide, so its area is 6 * 8 = 48 square feet.\nThe comforter will be 2 feet longer and 2 feet wider than the bed, so it will be 6 + 2 = 8 feet long and 8 + 2 = 10 feet wide. The area of the comforter will be 8 * 10 = 80 square feet.\nSince Jim needs two pieces of fabric for the comforter, he will need 80 * 2 = 160 square feet of fabric.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 160.
2025-12-24 15:55:00 | INFO | Q1128 id=gsm8k_mcq_01127 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The reasoning for my answer is as follows:\n\n  * We know that the fastest car was 1.25 times faster than the second fastest car.\n  * The second fastest car was 5 times faster than the average car.\n  * The average car goes 120 miles per hour.\n\nUsing this information, we can set up the following equation:\n\n  * Fastest car = 1.25 x Second fastest car\n  * Second fastest car = 5 x Average car\n\nSubstituting the values from the above equations into the first equation, we get:\n\n  * Fastest car = 1.25 x (5 x Average car)\n  * Fastest car = 6.25 x Average car\n\nFinally, solving for the fastest car, we get:\n\n  * Fastest car = 78.125 miles per hour\n\nTherefore, the faster car goes 78.125 miles per hour, which corresponds to choice C.
2025-12-24 15:55:03 | INFO | Q1042 id=gsm8k_mcq_01041 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount that Molly will pay for the catering can be calculated as follows:\n\n10 people want the chicken salad, which costs $6.50 per person, so the cost of the chicken salad is 10 * $6.50 = $65.\n\n6 people want the pasta salad, which also costs $6 per person, so the cost of the pasta salad is 6 * $6 = $36.\n\nTherefore, the total amount that Molly will pay for the catering is $65 + $36 = $101.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 101.
2025-12-24 15:55:06 | INFO | Q1044 id=gsm8k_mcq_01043 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by finding the total number of people living in all the cities in South America. To do this, we need to multiply the number of cities by the number of people living in each city. In this case, that would be:\n\n26 cities * 5000 people/city = 130000 people\n\nTherefore, the total number of people living in all the cities in South America is 130000. The answer is B) 130000.
