2025-12-24 15:57:10 | INFO | Q1103 id=gsm8k_mcq_01102 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Sheila charged $85.00 worth of merchandise on her credit card. She ended up returning one item that cost $15.00. So she spent $85 - $15 = $70 on the remaining items. After she returned the item, she bought a frying pan that was on sale for 20% off $20.00, so she saved 20/100 * $20 = $4 on the frying pan. The frying pan now costs $20 - $4 = $16. She also bought a set of towels that was 10% off $30.00, so she saved 10/100 * $30 = $3 on the towels. The towels now cost $30 - $3 = $27. Adding the cost of the frying pan and towels, she spent $16 + $27 = $43 on the two items. Therefore, the new balance on her credit card is $70 - $43 = $27. Answer: C) 27
