2025-12-24 15:57:17 | INFO | Q1109 id=gsm8k_mcq_01108 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=My mom spent $19 on pots and $26 on soil, so she spent a total of $19 + $26 = $45 at the gardening shop. However, she used a coupon for $7 off, so she actually paid $45 - $7 = $38. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 38.
2025-12-24 15:57:19 | INFO | Q1193 id=gsm8k_mcq_01192 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=We can calculate Jen's earnings for April as follows:\n\n  * She works for 7.5 hours per day x 6 days per week = 45 hours per week\n  * Her hourly rate is $1.5, so her daily earnings are $1.5 x 45 = $71.25 per day\n  * For the entire month of April with 4 weeks, she will work for 45 hours per week x 4 weeks = 180 hours\n  * Therefore, her total earnings for April will be $71.25 per day x 180 hours = $12930\n\nIn addition to her regular earnings, Jen also receives an additional $10 if she has complete attendance. Since she did not incur any absences for April, she will receive this bonus.\n\n  * The bonus amount is $10, so her total earnings for April will be $12930 + $10 = $12940\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 280.
