2025-12-24 15:59:42 | INFO | Q1256 id=gsm8k_mcq_01255 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=To find out how many cups of water Crista needs for her plants, we need to add up the amount of water each plant needs. We can do this by adding up the number of plants that need half a cup of water, the number of plants that need a cup of water, and the number of plants that need a quarter of a cup of water.\nFirst, we add up the number of plants that need half a cup of water: 4 plants + 8 plants = 12 plants\nNext, we add up the number of plants that need a cup of water: 12 plants + 8 plants = 20 plants\nFinally, we add up the number of plants that need a quarter of a cup of water: 20 plants - 12 plants - 8 plants = 0 plants\nTherefore, Crista needs 12 cups of water for her plants every day. This is the single best answer because it adds up all the amounts of water needed for the plants and results in a whole number.
