2025-12-24 16:01:55 | INFO | Q1249 id=gsm8k_mcq_01248 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the historical averages provided, for every 25 telephone calls made to potential customers, there is a 1/25 chance that a customer will visit the dealership. Since Jason needs to sell 15 cars this month, he would need to make 15 / (1/25) = 375 telephone calls to potential customers. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 375.
