2025-12-24 16:01:58 | INFO | Q01 id=gsm8k_mcq_00064 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=To calculate how many miles Sophia can drive on a single tank of gas, we need to determine how many miles she can travel on 12 gallons of gas. We know that she has already driven 100 miles and needed 4 gallons of gas to refill her tank, so we can use this information to calculate her fuel efficiency.\nFirst, let's find out how many miles Sophia can travel on 4 gallons of gas. To do this, we divide the number of miles she has already driven (100) by the number of gallons of gas she added to her tank (4). This gives us a fuel efficiency of 25 miles per gallon.\nNext, we can use this fuel efficiency to calculate how many miles Sophia can travel on 12 gallons of gas. To do this, we multiply the fuel efficiency by the number of gallons of gas in her tank (12). This gives us a total distance of 25 miles per gallon x 12 gallons = 300 miles.\nTherefore, Sophia can drive 300 miles on a single tank of gas. The correct answer is B) 300.
