2025-12-24 16:02:04 | INFO | Q1255 id=gsm8k_mcq_01254 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The time it takes for the coat of varnish to dry on six paintings with the new varnish is 12 minutes x 6 = 72 minutes. The time it takes for the coat of varnish to dry on six paintings with the old varnish is 7 minutes x 6 = 42 minutes. Therefore, the difference in drying time is 72 - 42 = 30 minutes. The correct answer is D) 30.
2025-12-24 16:02:12 | INFO | Q1257 id=gsm8k_mcq_01256 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=medium | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=To solve this problem, we can break down the journey into two parts: the part on land and the part in water.\nLet x be the total distance Phineas needs to travel to get back home. We know that x = 200 yards, so we can write:\nx = 200\nSince half of the distance is on land and half is in water, we can say that:\nx/2 = 100\nNow we can substitute this expression for x/2 into the equation above to find the time it takes Phineas to travel on land:\n200 / 20 = 10 minutes\nThis means it takes Phineas 10 minutes to travel 100 yards on land. Since there are 200 yards in total, it takes him 200 / 100 = 2 times as long to travel on land as it does to travel in water. Therefore, the time it takes Phineas to travel on land is 2 * 10 = 20 minutes.\nFinally, we can add the time it takes Phineas to travel in water to the time it takes him to travel on land to find the total time it takes him to get back home:\n20 + 10 = 30 minutes\nTherefore, Phineas will take 30 minutes to return home.\nThe answer is C: 30.
