2025-12-24 16:05:42 | INFO | Q26 id=gsm8k_mcq_00025 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, Marie spent a total of $50 on a chicken meal, 5 packs of milk, 4 apples, and some boxes of pizza. We can set up an equation to represent this as follows:\n$12 + $3 x 5 + $1.50 x 4 + Y = $50\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n$12 + $15 + $6 + Y = $50\nSubtracting $12 from both sides, we get:\n$15 + $6 + Y = $38\nSubtracting $6 from both sides, we get:\n$9 + Y = $38\nFinally, subtracting $9 from both sides, we get:\nY = $29\nTherefore, Marie spent $29 on boxes of pizza. Since each box costs $8.50, Marie ordered 29 / 8.5 = 3 boxes of pizza.\nAnswer: C) 3
