2025-12-24 16:07:48 | INFO | Q93 id=gsm8k_mcq_00092 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equations:\n\nAmy = 5 + x\nJackson = 5 - x + 2\nCorey = 5 - x - 2\n\nWhere x represents the number of years between Amy and Jackson, and between Jackson and Corey.\n\nWe also know that James is 10 years old and one year younger than Corey. Therefore:\n\nJames = 10 - 1 = 9\n\nSubstituting this into the equation for Corey, we get:\n\n9 = 5 - x - 2\nx = 3\n\nTherefore, Jackson is 5 - 3 = 2 years old.\n\nAnswer: B) 4
