2025-12-24 16:07:57 | INFO | Q98 id=gsm8k_mcq_00097 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Freda used 32 ounces of tomato sauce, which was made from each of 16 ounce cans of tomatoes that contain three tomatoes. Therefore, Freda used 32 / 16 = 2 cans of tomatoes. Since each can contains three tomatoes, Freda used 2 * 3 = 6 tomatoes. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 6.
2025-12-24 16:07:59 | INFO | Q95 id=gsm8k_mcq_00094 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of rabbits = Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nWe also know that there are two cats for every dog, so we can write:\n\nNumber of dogs = Number of cats / 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = Number of cats / 2 + Number of cats - 12\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits = Number of cats + Number of cats - 24\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits = 2 * (Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12) = 2 * (60 + Number of cats - 12) = 120 + 2 * Number of cats\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 120 + 2 * Number of cats\n\nSubstituting this expression for Number of rabbits into the original equation, we get:\n\n120 + 2 * Number of cats = Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n120 + 2 * Number of cats = 60 + Number of cats - 12\n\nAdding 12 to both sides, we get:\n\n132 = 72 + Number of cats\n\nSubtracting 72 from both sides, we get:\n\n60 = Number of cats\n\nFinally, substituting the value of Number of cats into the expression for Number of rabbits, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 120 + 2 * 60 = 120 + 120 = 240\n\nTherefore, the total number of pets in the neighborhood is 240.\n\nAnswer: A) 348
