2025-12-24 16:08:31 | INFO | Q116 id=gsm8k_mcq_00115 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate the total revenue from selling the leftover boards as follows:\n\n10 2x4x10 boards at $10 each = $100\n5 4x4x10 boards at $16 each = $80\n\nTotal revenue = $100 + $80 = $180\n\nTo find the profit, we subtract the cost of the lumber from the total revenue:\n\nCost of lumber = 10 2x4x10 boards at $10 each = $100\n+ 5 4x4x10 boards at $16 each = $80\n= $180\n\nProfit = Total revenue - Cost of lumber = $180 - $180 = $0\n\nTherefore, the profit made by selling all the leftover boards is $0.\n\nFinal Answer: C) 0
