2025-12-24 16:09:52 | INFO | Q151 id=gsm8k_mcq_00150 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The winner will be waiting at their house for 30 minutes before the loser finishes the race.\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to first find out how long it takes each person to travel the distance between their house and the school.\nSteve travels 3 miles at a speed of 440 feet per minute, so it takes him 3/440 = 0.068 minutes to travel that far. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, this equates to 0.068 minutes * 60 = 4.08 minutes.\nTim travels 2 miles at a speed of 264 feet per minute, so it takes him 2/264 = 0.079 minutes to travel that far. Again, converting this to hours gives us 0.079 minutes * 60 = 4.74 minutes.\nTherefore, Tim will finish the race in 4.74 minutes, while Steve will finish in 4.08 minutes. This means that the winner will be waiting at their house for 4.74 - 4.08 = 0.66 minutes, which is equal to 30 seconds.\nTherefore, the answer is B) 30.
