2025-12-24 16:10:22 | INFO | Q172 id=gsm8k_mcq_00171 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of legs that Jake sees is the sum of the legs of the spiders, insects, and invertebrates. To find the total number of legs, we add up the number of legs from each group:\n\n80 spiders * 8 legs = 640 legs\n90 insects * 6 legs = 540 legs\n3 invertebrates * 10 legs = 30 legs\n\nTotal legs = 640 + 540 + 30 = 1210 legs\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 1210.\n\n反思：本题考察对加法的理解和应用。在解题过程中，我们需要仔细读题，理解题目中的关键信息，并运用加法运算求得答案。同时，我们也需要注意检查自己的计算是否正确，避免出现错误。
