2025-12-24 16:12:10 | INFO | Q227 id=gsm8k_mcq_00226 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of cards is 30 + 20 + 40 = 90 cards. Out of these, 40 are water type, 20 are grass type, and 30 are fire type. After losing 8 water type cards, the total number of water type cards remaining is 40 - 8 = 32. After buying 14 grass type cards, the total number of grass type cards becomes 20 + 14 = 34. The total number of cards remaining is 32 + 34 = 66. Therefore, the probability of drawing a water type card is 32 / 66 = 47.5%. Rounding this to the nearest integer, the percentage chance is 48. So the answer is (A).
2025-12-24 16:12:13 | INFO | Q230 id=gsm8k_mcq_00229 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=When Ashlyn came back two weeks later, 3/4 of the remaining melons were ready for harvest. This means that 1 - 3/4 = 1/4 of the melons were not ready for harvest. Since there were 120 baby watermelons, 1/4 of them would be 120 x 1/4 = 30 melons. Therefore, 30 melons were not ready to be harvested after the two weeks. The answer is D) 30.
