2025-12-24 16:13:25 | INFO | Q260 id=gsm8k_mcq_00259 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nAndrea = Jamal + 8\nJamal = Apples + 4\nJamal = Bananas / 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the third equation gives:\n\nApples + 4 = Bananas / 2\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * (Apples + 4) = Bananas\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * (Andrea + 8) = Bananas\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea + 16 = Bananas\n\nSubtracting 16 from both sides gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Bananas - 16\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 16\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 32\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 28\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 28\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 20\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 20\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 40\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 36\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 36\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 44\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 44\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 88\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 84\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 84\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 92\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 92\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 184\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 180\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 180\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 188\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 188\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 376\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 372\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 372\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 380\n\nSubstituting the second equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Apples + 4) / 2 - 380\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2 gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples + 4 - 744\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Apples - 740\n\nSubstituting the first equation into this gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = (Jamal + 8) - 740\n\nSimplifying gives:\n\n2 * Andrea = Jamal - 748
2025-12-24 16:13:27 | INFO | Q277 id=gsm8k_mcq_00276 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of cards that have the letter A and B as follows:\n\n2/5 * 80 = 32 cards\n1/2 * (80 - 32) = 24 cards\n5/8 * (80 - 32 - 24) = 27 cards\n\nTherefore, the total number of cards that have either the letter A or B is 32 + 24 = 56 cards.\n\nOut of the remaining 80 cards, 5/8 * 24 = 18 cards have the letter C. Therefore, the total number of cards that have either the letter A, B, or C is 56 + 18 = 74 cards.\n\nFinally, the number of cards that have the letter D is 80 - 74 = 6 cards.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 3.
