2025-12-24 16:14:14 | INFO | Q284 id=gsm8k_mcq_00283 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=To find out how many sterling silver beads Katerina uses per necklace, we need to calculate the number of spaces between the topaz gemstones that will be filled with sterling silver beads. Since each topaz gemstone is one inch long, we can divide the total length of the necklace by the length of each topaz gemstone to find out how many spaces there are between them. In this case, the total length of the necklace is 25 inches, and each topaz gemstone is one inch long, so there are 24 spaces between the gemstones.\nSince each sterling silver bead is one-quarter of an inch long, we can divide the number of spaces between the gemstones by the length of each silver bead to find out how many silver beads Katerina uses per necklace. In this case, there are 24 spaces between the gemstones, and each silver bead is one-quarter of an inch long, so Katerina uses 24 / (1/4) = 96 sterling silver beads per necklace.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 68.
