2025-12-24 16:14:58 | INFO | Q308 id=gsm8k_mcq_00307 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The question states that Sandy wants to lose as much weight as Joey does in four weeks, but Joey loses eight pounds in four weeks. To determine how many weeks it will take Sandy to lose the same amount of weight, we need to divide the amount of weight Joey loses by the number of weeks he loses it.\nIn this case, Joey loses eight pounds in four weeks, so he loses 8 pounds / 4 weeks = 2 pounds per week. Therefore, it will take Sandy four weeks to lose the same amount of weight as Joey does in a single week.\nTherefore, the answer is C) 4.
