2025-12-24 16:15:09 | INFO | Q345 id=gsm8k_mcq_00344 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can see that:\n\n- Juice Box A costs $4\n- Juice Box B costs $5 more than Juice Box A, so it costs $4 + $5 = $9\n- Juice Box C costs $7 more than Juice Box A, so it costs $4 + $7 = $11\n\nTherefore, the difference between Juice Box C and Juice Box B is $11 - $9 = $2.\n\nSo the correct answer is B) 2.
2025-12-24 16:15:10 | INFO | Q315 id=gsm8k_mcq_00314 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of offensive players = 2 * Number of defensive players\n\nNumber of special team players = Number of defensive players / 2\n\nGiven that the football team has 105 members, we can substitute these values into the equations to get:\n\nNumber of offensive players = 2 * Number of defensive players\n105 = 2 * Number of defensive players\n\nNumber of special team players = Number of defensive players / 2\n105 = Number of defensive players / 2\n\nMultiplying both sides of the second equation by 2 gives:\n\n210 = Number of defensive players\n\nTherefore, there are 210 players on the defense. The answer is B.
2025-12-24 16:15:11 | INFO | Q347 id=gsm8k_mcq_00346 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of cookies that Jenny and her husband consume is 4 + 1 + 7 = 12 cookies. Since the bag of cookies has 36 cookies, then Jenny eats 36 - 12 = 24 cookies.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 16.
2025-12-24 16:15:15 | INFO | Q317 id=gsm8k_mcq_00316 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=To find the total weight of marbles Solomon has in the store, we need to add the number of marbles he bought from Johanna and the number his father gave him.\nSolomon bought 20 marbles from Johanna, so he has 20 marbles in the store. His father gave him 2/5 times as many marbles as he bought from Johanna, which is 2/5 * 20 = 8 marbles. Therefore, Solomon has a total of 20 + 8 = 28 marbles in the store.\nThe weight of each marble is 2kg, so the total weight of the marbles in the store is 28 * 2kg = 56kg.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 56.
2025-12-24 16:15:15 | INFO | Q349 id=gsm8k_mcq_00348 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The factory is now making 5 times as many silos per day compared to when they were making tractors. To find the percentage increase in their daily earnings, we can set up the following equation:\n((220/100) * 5 - (100/10)) / (100/10) = percentage increase\nSimplifying the equation gives us:\n(110 - 10) / 10 = 100%\nTherefore, the factory is making 100% more per day now than they did when they were making tractors. The answer is B: 100.
