2025-12-24 16:15:36 | INFO | Q327 id=gsm8k_mcq_00326 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The number of people who got on the bus at the terminal can be found by adding the number of people who got on at each stop. At the first stop, 5 more people got on, so there were 5 + x people on the bus. At the second stop, 7 people got off and 8 more got on, so there were (5 + x) - 7 + 8 = (5 + x) + 1 people on the bus. Since these two equations equal the same thing, we can set them equal to 20: (5 + x) + 1 = 20 Subtracting 1 from both sides gives us (5 + x) = 19 Subtracting 5 from both sides gives us x = 14 Therefore, there were 14 people who got on the bus at the terminal. Answer: C) 14
2025-12-24 16:15:36 | INFO | Q365 id=gsm8k_mcq_00364 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of fourth-grade students at Small Tree School is 96, and out of these, 43 are girls. On Friday, 5 girls and 4 boys were absent. To find the number of fourth-grade boys who were present on Friday, we need to subtract the number of absent students from the total number of students.\nSo, the number of fourth-grade boys who were present on Friday is 96 - 43 - 5 = 48.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 48.\nFinal Answer: The correct answer is D) 48.
