2025-12-24 16:15:40 | INFO | Q367 id=gsm8k_mcq_00366 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=To determine the minimum number of points Jane must score on the third test to pass, we need to add up the scores from her first two tests and see if they total at least 42 points.\nFirst test: 15 points\nSecond test: 18 points\nTotal so far: 15 + 18 = 33 points\nWe need a total of at least 42 points, so Jane needs to score at least 42 - 33 = 9 points on the third test to pass.\nTherefore, the minimum number of points Jane must score on the third test is D) 9.\nFinal Answer: D) 9
