2025-12-24 16:16:53 | INFO | Q370 id=gsm8k_mcq_00369 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total cost for the senior gifts is calculated as follows:\n\n  * 44 seniors x $20/picture frame = $880\n  * 20% additional cost per frame = $880 x 20% = $176\n  * 2 seniors will receive $5/pin = $10\n  * 1/4 of the seniors are officers = 44 seniors / 4 = 11 seniors\n  * 11 seniors will receive $12/cord = $132\n  * Total cost for all senior gifts = $880 + $176 + $10 + $132 = $1198\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 1198.\n\nTo arrive at this answer, we first calculate the cost of the picture frames, which is $880. We then add the additional 20% cost per frame, which equals $880 x 20% = $176. Next, we add the cost of the two pins, which is $5/pin x 2 = $10. Then, we find how many seniors are officers, which is 1/4 of the total number of seniors, or 44 seniors / 4 = 11 seniors. Finally, we multiply the number of officers by the cost of their cords, which is $12/cord x 11 = $132. Adding up all these costs gives us a total of $880 + $176 + $10 + $132 = $1198.
