2025-12-24 16:18:18 | INFO | Q416 id=gsm8k_mcq_00415 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Joanne gathered a total of 30 + 15 + X = 45 apples from the three types of trees. Her sister, on the other hand, gathered 60 + 90 + 0 = 150 apples from the same three types of trees. Together, they gathered 200 apples. Since they have gathered a combined total of 500 apples, we can find the value of X by subtracting their combined total from 500: 500 - 200 = 300. Therefore, Joanne gathered X = 300 / 2 = 150 apples from the average trees. Answer: C) 150
2025-12-24 16:18:18 | INFO | Q476 id=gsm8k_mcq_00475 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Jason has three weeks to break in his new shoes by walking four days a week. To determine how much time he needs to spend walking each day, we need to divide the total number of minutes required to break in the shoes by the number of days he plans to walk per week.\nTherefore, we can calculate the number of minutes Jason needs to spend walking each day as follows:\n240 minutes / 4 days = 60 minutes per day\nSo, Jason needs to spend 60 minutes walking each day to break in his new shoes.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 60.
2025-12-24 16:18:20 | INFO | Q478 id=gsm8k_mcq_00477 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that:\n\n9 + 6 + 3 = 28 kids in Gina's class who are either allergic to dairy, peanuts, or both.\n\nTherefore, the number of kids who are not allergic to anything is:\n\n32 - 28 = 4\n\nSo the answer is A) 23.
