2025-12-24 16:18:42 | INFO | Q426 id=gsm8k_mcq_00425 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Lillian can expect to see a total of 40 birds in her garden each day if the same amount keeps coming to her bird feeders. This is because each bird feeder attracts 20 birds throughout the day, and Lillian has built three bird feeders and bought three more, for a total of six feeders. The bird feeders she made herself attract 10 more birds each than the store-bought ones, so each of her homemade feeders will attract 30 birds, while each of the store-bought feeders will attract 20 birds. Therefore, the total number of birds attracted by all six feeders is 6 x 30 + 6 x 20 = 180 birds. However, since each bird feeder can hold only 20 birds at a time, Lillian can only expect to see 20 birds at each feeder at any given time. Therefore, the total number of birds she can expect to see in her garden each day is 20 x 6 = 120 birds. Answer: A) 120
2025-12-24 16:18:42 | INFO | Q491 id=gsm8k_mcq_00490 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=It would take the child 6 days to save the remaining amount of money if he promises to save $2 daily from his allowance.\nTo see why, we can set up an equation representing the amount of money the child has saved each day as a function of the number of days that have passed. Let S be the amount of money the child has saved after n days. We know that S = 2n + 4 for all n >= 0.\nWe want to find the smallest integer n such that S >= 12. Substituting S = 2n + 4 into the equation above, we get 2n + 4 >= 12, which simplifies to 2n >= 8, or n >= 4.\nTherefore, it takes the child 4 days to save the remaining amount of money if he promises to save $2 daily from his allowance. The correct answer is C.
