2025-12-24 16:18:52 | INFO | Q495 id=gsm8k_mcq_00494 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The height of the human pyramid can be found by adding up the heights of each layer. \n\nThe bottom layer has 4 girls who are all 64" tall, so their total height is:\n\n4 x 64 = 256 inches\n\nThe second layer has 3 girls who stand on top of the 4 girls from the previous layer. Since each girl in the second layer is shorter than the corresponding girl in the first layer, we can assume that the sum of their heights is less than 256 inches. Let's call this sum X.\n\nThe third layer has 2 girls who stand on top of the 3 girls from the second layer. Again, we can assume that the sum of their heights is less than X.\n\nFinally, the top layer consists of the shortest girl, who is 60" tall. Therefore, the total height of the human pyramid is:\n\nX + 2(60) < 256\nX < 224\n\nSince X represents the sum of the heights of the second and third layers, it must be less than 224 inches. The closest choice among the options provided is A) 21 inches, which is less than 224 inches. Therefore, the human pyramid will be 21 inches tall in feet.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 21.
