2025-12-24 16:20:54 | INFO | Q574 id=gsm8k_mcq_00573 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=After two years,Katina will have removed $2400 from her account because $100 x 24 = $2400\. To find out how much money will be remaining in the account, we need to subtract this amount from the initial balance of $3000. $3000 - $2400 = $600\. Therefore, there will be $600 remaining in the account after two years. The answer is C.
2025-12-24 16:20:56 | INFO | Q512 id=gsm8k_mcq_00511 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, Gerald earned $30 per day for a week, which means he earned $30 x 7 = $210. He spent a total of $100, so he has $210 - $100 = $110 left.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 110.
