2025-12-24 16:22:18 | INFO | Q562 id=gsm8k_mcq_00561 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total weight of Mark and Susan is 150 + 20 = 170 pounds. Bob weighs twice as much as Susan, who weighs 20 pounds less than Mark, so Bob weighs 2 * 20 = 40 pounds more than Susan. Therefore, Bob weighs 150 + 40 = 190 pounds. The total weight of all three friends is 170 + 190 = 360 pounds. The average weight of the three friends is 360 / 3 = 120 pounds. Answer: D) 130
2025-12-24 16:22:20 | INFO | Q631 id=gsm8k_mcq_00630 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the number of men who can stay upright on the wave as follows:\n\nOut of 100 surfers, 60% are women, so:\n\n100 x 60% = 60 surfers\n\nOut of these 60 surfers, only 25% can stay upright on the wave over 30 feet. So:\n\n60 x 25% = 15 surfers\n\nTherefore, out of 100 surfers, only 15 men can stay upright on the wave.\n\nSo the answer is C) 15.
2025-12-24 16:22:23 | INFO | Q633 id=gsm8k_mcq_00632 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Max bought 16 snowflake stamps, 3 more truck stamps than snowflake stamps, which equals 16 + 3 = 19 truck stamps. He also bought 9 fewer rose stamps than truck stamps, which equals 19 - 9 = 10 rose stamps. Therefore, Max bought a total of 16 + 19 + 10 = 45 stamps at the post office. The correct answer is C) 45.
2025-12-24 16:22:24 | INFO | Q564 id=gsm8k_mcq_00563 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the most suitable answer would be B) $9.\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to determine how many packs of candles James needs to buy. Since he has two sons, one of whom is 12 years old and the other is four years younger, we can assume that the older son is 12 and the younger son is 8. Therefore, James needs to buy two packs of candles, each containing five candles. Since a pack of five candles costs $3, this means that James spends $3 x 2 = $6 on candles. However, since the question asks for the amount he spends "on candles," not "for candles," we simply divide the total cost by the number of items purchased, which gives us a cost per item of $6 / 2 = $3. Therefore, James spends $3 on each pack of candles, for a total of $3 x 2 = $6 on candles. Answering with B) $9 would require choosing the wrong option and potentially confusing the listener.
2025-12-24 16:22:25 | INFO | Q635 id=gsm8k_mcq_00634 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nTommy + 3 = Darren - 6\nTommy = Darren + 3 + 6\n\nGiven that Naomi caught 17 fish, we can substitute that value into the equation for Darren:\n\nTommy = (Darren + 3 + 6) - 6\nTommy = Darren + 9\n\nTherefore, Tommy caught 9 fish.\n\nAnswer: C) 9
2025-12-24 16:22:28 | INFO | Q567 id=gsm8k_mcq_00566 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The information provided states that Shiloh is 44 years old today and in 7 years he will be three times as old as his nephew. Let's call the age of Shiloh's nephew x.\nIn 7 years, Shiloh will be 44 + 7 = 51 years old. According to the problem statement, at that time he will be three times as old as his nephew, so we can write: 51 = 3x\nSolving for x gives us: x = 17\nSo, his nephew is 17 years old today. The correct answer is B) 17.
