2025-12-24 16:23:32 | INFO | Q676 id=gsm8k_mcq_00675 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The correct answer is C) 17.\nTo arrive at this answer, we can break down the problem into steps:\n\n  1. James initially had 4 toys for 4 dogs, so each dog needed 1 toy. This means he had 4 toys + 4 dogs = 8 toys in total.\n  2. There are now 8 more dogs in the shelter, so the total number of dogs is 8 + 8 = 16 dogs.\n  3. Since each dog needs 1 toy, James needs 16 toys for all the dogs.\n  4. After buying more toys, the total number of dogs remains 16, but there are now 16 - 3 = 13 dogs who still need toys.\n  5. Since each dog needs 1 toy, James needs 13 toys for these 13 dogs.\n\nTherefore, the total number of toys that James needs is 8 + 13 = 21 toys. However, since we cannot use more than 10 letters in our answer, we must round this number down to 20. The closest choice from the options provided is C) 17, which rounds this number down to 17.
2025-12-24 16:23:32 | INFO | Q602 id=gsm8k_mcq_00601 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of games that Steve receives each year is 5 + 5 = 10 games. In the first year, he saves up enough money to buy 1 game per month for 12 months, so he will receive 10 games + 12 = 22 games in the first year. In the second year, he starts buying 2 games per month, so he will receive 22 games - 12 = 10 games in the second year. In the third year, he buys 4 games per month, so he will receive 10 games + 4 * 12 = 64 games in the third year. Therefore, the total number of games that Steve has after 3 years is 22 + 10 + 64 = 96 games. The closest choice from the options provided is A) 99, which is incorrect. The correct answer is D) 94.
2025-12-24 16:23:37 | INFO | Q678 id=gsm8k_mcq_00677 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=To determine how many signatures the sisters need to collect to reach their goal of 100 signatures, we can set up an equation representing the total number of signatures they need to collect as a function of the number of signatures each sister has collected so far. Let S be the total number of signatures the sisters need to collect. We know that S = 2C + 4J, where C is the number of signatures Carol has collected and J is the number of signatures Jennifer has collected. Since Carol has 20 signatures and Jennifer has 44, we can substitute these values into the equation to get S = 2(20) + 4(44) = 176. Therefore, the sisters need to collect 176 more signatures to reach their goal of 100 signatures. So the answer is A) 24.
2025-12-24 16:23:37 | INFO | Q604 id=gsm8k_mcq_00603 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Ruiz makes 120 pounds of chocolates in two hours, which means he makes 120 pounds / 2 hours = 60 pounds per hour.\nMarissa makes three-fourths as many pounds of chocolates in an hour as Ruiz does in two hours, which means she makes 3/4 * 60 pounds = 45 pounds per hour.\nIf they both work for 12 hours in a day, then Ruiz will make 60 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 720 pounds.\nMarissa will also make 45 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 540 pounds.\nTherefore, the total amount of chocolate pounds they made together is 720 pounds + 540 pounds = 1260 pounds.\nThe correct answer is D) 1260.
2025-12-24 16:23:40 | INFO | Q680 id=gsm8k_mcq_00679 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate that each potato will yield approximately 6 hash browns. Therefore, to find out how many hash browns you can make out of 96 potatoes, you simply need to multiply the number of potatoes by the number of hash browns per potato. \n\nSo, 96 potatoes * 6 hash browns per potato = 576 hash browns\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 576.\n\nFinal Answer: The correct answer is B) 576.
2025-12-24 16:23:42 | INFO | Q606 id=gsm8k_mcq_00605 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of cups of lemonade that Patrick sold was 15 + 10 = 25 cups. He sold each cup for $0.50 during the first four hours, so he earned 25 x $0.50 = $12.50 during this time. During the next two hours, he sold 10 cups of lemonade per hour at a price of $0.60 per cup, so he earned 10 x $0.60 = $6.00 during this time. Therefore, Patrick earned a total of $12.50 + $6.00 = $18.50 from selling lemonade for six hours. The correct answer is C) 18.50.
2025-12-24 16:23:45 | INFO | Q608 id=gsm8k_mcq_00607 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The jumbo bottle of shampoo costs $24.00, and the directions say to use 2 pumps of shampoo to get 120 washings. If Jackie only uses 1 pump per wash, then she will use 120/1=120 pumps of shampoo. Since the jumbo bottle costs $24.00, each pump of shampoo will cost $24.00/120=$0.20 in cents. Therefore, the answer is A) 20.
2025-12-24 16:23:47 | INFO | Q682 id=gsm8k_mcq_00681 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nKatarina = Max - 5\nMax = Cookie Monster + 12\nSummer = Max + 23\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the third equation gives us:\n\nSummer = (Cookie Monster + 12) + 23\n\nSolving for Max, we get:\n\nMax = Cookie Monster + 35\n\nSubstituting that back into the first equation, we get:\n\nKatarina = (Cookie Monster + 35) - 5\n\nSolving for Cookie Monster, we get:\n\nCookie Monster = 30\n\nSubstituting that back into the second equation, we get:\n\nMax = 30 + 12 = 42\n\nSubstituting that back into the third equation, we get:\n\nSummer = 42 + 23 = 65\n\nFinally, substituting all of those values into the equation for Katarina, we get:\n\nKatarina = 65 - 5 = 60\n\nTherefore, the total number of cookies that Katarina has is 60. The answer is A) 268.
2025-12-24 16:23:48 | INFO | Q610 id=gsm8k_mcq_00609 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Juan will need 1/4 pound of butter to make each dozen croissants. Since he wants to make 4 dozen croissants per day for a week (7 days), he will therefore need 1/4 * 4 = 1 pound of butter per day. Therefore, Juan will need 1 pound of butter to make these croissants.\nAnswer: D) 1
2025-12-24 16:23:49 | INFO | Q685 id=gsm8k_mcq_00684 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, John and Jack take 6+13 = 19 minutes to reach their destination. Since they have 30 minutes to walk to school together, they have 30-19 = 11 minutes left without being late. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 11.
2025-12-24 16:23:50 | INFO | Q614 id=gsm8k_mcq_00613 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total number of posts that the group will have in March as follows:\n\nNumber of days in March = 31\nAverage number of posts per member per day = 3\nTotal number of posts per member in March = 31 x 3 = 93\n\nTherefore, the total number of posts that the group will have in March is 9300.\n\nAnswer: C) 9300
