2025-12-24 16:24:05 | INFO | Q624 id=gsm8k_mcq_00623 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Charmaine is currently 16 - 12 = 4 years younger than 16 years old. Therefore, she will be 16 + 4 = 20 years old in 4 years. Thus, Charmaine will be 20 - 4 = 16 years old four years from now. The correct answer is D) 16.
2025-12-24 16:24:07 | INFO | Q626 id=gsm8k_mcq_00625 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of flowers in Arianna's garden is 10 rows * 20 flowers = 200 flowers. Since only 4/5 of the flowers have bloomed, the number of bloomed flowers is 4/5 * 200 = 160 flowers. Therefore, the correct answer is C) 160.
2025-12-24 16:24:11 | INFO | Q698 id=gsm8k_mcq_00697 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of great-grandbabies that Great Grandma Jones will be able to kiss at the family reunion is 30.\nTo see why, let's break down the generations:\n\n  * Great Grandma Jones has three children\n  * Each of her children has three children of their own (who are her grandchildren)\n  * Each of her grandchildren has three babies of their own (who are her great-grandchildren)\n\nWe can use multiplication to find the total number of great-grandbabies:\n\n  * 3 children x 3 grandchildren = 9 great-grandchildren\n  * 9 great-grandchildren x 3 babies per great-grandchild = 27 great-grandbabies\n\nHowever, since each great-grandbaby has three siblings (the babies of their own parents), we need to divide the total number of great-grandbabies by 3 to account for them:\n\n  * 27 great-grandbabies / 3 siblings per great-grandbaby = 9 great-grandparents\n\nTherefore, there will be 9 great-grandparents at the family reunion, each with 3 babies, for a total of 27 great-grandbabies. However, since each great-grandparent has three children of their own, we need to add those to the total as well:\n\n  * 9 great-grandparents x 3 children per great-grandparent = 27 great-grandchildren + 27 children = 54 people at the family reunion\n\nSince Great Grandma Jones is one of the people at the family reunion, she will be able to kiss 54 people - 1 (herself) = 53 people at the family reunion. Therefore, there will be 53 great-grandbabies for Great Grandma Jones to kiss at the family reunion.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 30.
2025-12-24 16:24:12 | INFO | Q628 id=gsm8k_mcq_00627 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of cars the tow truck towed that week as follows:\n\nOn the first three days, the tow truck pulled ten cars per day, so it towed a total of 3 x 10 = 30 cars.\n\nOn the remaining four days, the tow truck pulled four fewer cars per day than the previous day, which means it towed 10 - 4 = 6 cars per day. Therefore, it towed a total of 4 x 6 = 24 cars during these four days.\n\nTherefore, the total number of cars the tow truck towed that week is 30 + 24 = 54. The correct answer is A).
