2025-12-24 16:25:53 | INFO | Q688 id=gsm8k_mcq_00687 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The problem states that there is one set of twins and one set of triplets, and one twin is seven years older than one triplet. We are given that their combined ages are forty-four. Let's call the age of the triplet x and the age of the twin y. Therefore, we have two equations:\n\ny = x + 7\nx + y + z = 44\n\nWhere z is the age of the triplet.\n\nWe can rearrange the second equation to get:\n\nz = 44 - (x + y)\n\nSubstituting the value of y from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n\nz = 44 - (x + (x + 7))\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nz = 27\n\nTherefore, the age of the triplet is 27. Substituting this value back into either equation, we can find the ages of the twin and the triplet. For example, substituting z = 27 into the first equation, we get:\n\ny = 27 + 7\ny = 34\n\nTherefore, one of the twins is 34 years old. The answer is A) 34.
2025-12-24 16:25:55 | INFO | Q770 id=gsm8k_mcq_00769 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=On Monday, Tanya earned $15 per hour * 5 hours = $75 for her classes. Additionally, since she taught four classes, she earned an extra $5 per class * 4 classes = $20. So on Monday, Tanya earned a total of $75 + $20 = $95\. On Wednesday, Tanya earned $15 per hour * 2 hours = $30 for her classes. Since she taught two classes, she earned an extra $5 per class * 2 classes = $10. So on Wednesday, Tanya earned a total of $30 + $10 = $40\. Therefore, over the two days of teaching, Tanya earned a total of $95 + $40 = $135\. Answer: C) 105
