2025-12-24 16:25:58 | INFO | Q691 id=gsm8k_mcq_00690 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Rong has been saving 20 coins in his piggy bank every month for 10 years, which means he will have saved 20 x 12 = 240 coins in 10 years. Neil has been saving 2/5 times more coins in his piggy bank per month than Rong, who saves 20 coins, so Neil saves 20 x 2 / 5 = 8 coins more per month than Rong. Therefore, Neil saves 20 + 8 = 28 coins per month. Over 10 years, Neil will have saved 28 x 12 = 336 coins. Therefore, they will have 240 + 336 = 576 coins 10 years after they started their savings. The answer is C) 5760.
