2025-12-24 16:26:41 | INFO | Q716 id=gsm8k_mcq_00715 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The company initially intended to pay $700 for each computer, so the cost for 500 computers would be:\n\n500 * $700 = $35000\n\nHowever, when they ordered, they found that the price of each computer was 10% higher than their initial plan. To calculate the total cost at the new prices, we need to multiply the number of computers by the increased price per computer.\n\nThe increased price per computer is 10% higher than the original price, which means the new price is:\n\n$700 + ($700 * 10%) = $700 + $700 * 0.1 = $700 + $70 = $770\n\nSo, the total cost for 500 computers at the new prices would be:\n\n500 * $770 = $385000\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) $385000.
