2025-12-24 16:28:35 | INFO | Q781 id=gsm8k_mcq_00780 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the difference between Ava and Emma's scores would be 30 points.\nTo see why, let's consider the different factors that affect their scores:\n\n  * Each enemy jumped on gives Ava 10 points and Emma 5 points, so for each extra enemy Ava jumps on, she gets an additional 5 points.\n  * Each berry collected gives Ava 5 points and Emma 5 points, so for each extra berry Ava collects, she gets an additional 5 points.\n  * Each second left on the timer gives Ava 30 points and Emma 30 points, so for each second Ava finishes the level faster, she gets an additional 30 points.\n\nGiven these rules, if Ava jumps on 8 more enemies than Emma and collects 3 more berries, but finishes the level 4 seconds slower, then the difference in their scores would be as follows:\nAva's score = 10 _8 + 5_ 3 + 30_ (60 - 4) = 400 + 150 + 1800 = 2750 points Emma's score = 5 _8 + 5_ 3 + 30_ (60 - 4) = 400 + 150 + 1800 = 2750 points\nTherefore, the difference between their scores would be 0 points, since both players have the same number of enemies, berries, and time remaining on the timer. The correct answer is C: 25.
2025-12-24 16:28:36 | INFO | Q867 id=gsm8k_mcq_00866 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The information provided states that together, Sofie, Anne, and Fawn have 85 books. If Sofie has 25 more books than Anne, and Anne has 12 fewer books than Fawn does, we can set up the following equation:\n\nS + A + F = 85\n\nWe also know that Sofie has 25 more books than Anne, so:\n\nS = A + 25\n\nWe also know that Anne has 12 fewer books than Fawn, so:\n\nA = F - 12\n\nSubstituting the second two equations into the first equation, we get:\n\n(A + F - 12) + A + F = 85\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n2A + 2F = 97\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\nA + F = 48.5\n\nSince A and F must be whole numbers, the closest option is A = 48 and F = 47. Therefore, Fawn has 47 books.\n\nAnswer: D) 16
