2025-12-24 16:31:24 | INFO | Q962 id=gsm8k_mcq_00961 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Amora and Lainey each received 70 corn chips, while the other person received 15 more corn chips than the number the others got. This means that the other person received 70 + 15 = 85 corn chips.\nTherefore, the total number of corn chips that Amora, Lainey, and the other person shared equally was 70 + 70 + 85 = 225 corn chips.\nSo the correct answer is C) 225.
