2025-12-24 16:32:41 | INFO | Q1007 id=gsm8k_mcq_01006 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The volume of the pool can be calculated as follows:\n14 ft x 25 ft x 4 ft = 1120 cubic feet\nTo convert cubic feet to gallons, we divide by 7.48052 (the conversion factor between cubic feet and gallons):\n1120 cubic feet / 7.48052 gallons/cubic foot = 153.82 gallons\nTherefore, the pool requires 153.82 gallons of water. To calculate the cost, we multiply that number by the cost per gallon:\n153.82 gallons x $0.10/gallon = $15.38\nSo the total cost to fill the pool would be $15.38.\nAnswer: B) 140
2025-12-24 16:32:44 | INFO | Q1009 id=gsm8k_mcq_01008 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the distance each person traveled as follows:\n\nMatteo traveled 55 mph x 4 hours = 220 miles\nShandy traveled 45 mph x 10 hours = 450 miles\n\nTherefore, Shandy drove 450 - 220 = 230 miles farther than Matteo.\n\nSo the correct answer is B) 230.
