2025-12-24 16:34:24 | INFO | Q996 id=gsm8k_mcq_00995 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Adam received $6 from his mother and twice as much from his father, which is $6 x 2 = $12\. To find out how much money Adam had to contribute from his savings, we need to add the amount of money he received from his mother and father to the cost of the trousers, which is $30. Therefore, Adam had to contribute $30 - $6 - $12 = $12 from his savings.\nAnswer: C) 12
