2025-12-24 16:35:32 | INFO | Q1110 id=gsm8k_mcq_01109 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of women wearing heels at the party is six. The sum of the heights of the heels worn by these women is 6 inches. The average height of the heels worn by these women is 1 inch.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 2.
2025-12-24 16:35:34 | INFO | Q1030 id=gsm8k_mcq_01029 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of balloons that Sally initially had was 25 + 7 + 12 = 44. After the gust of wind caused 40% of the red balloons to burst, the number of red balloons left was 44 * (1 - 0.4) = 44 * 0.6 = 26. Sally accidentally released half of the yellow balloons, which is 12 * 0.5 = 6. So the total number of balloons left was 26 + 6 = 32. Sally then found 8 blue balloons caught in a tree, so she added these to her remaining clutch of balloons, making the total number of balloons she carried into the school 32 + 8 = 40. Therefore, Sally carried a total of 40 balloons into the school.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 40.
2025-12-24 16:35:35 | INFO | Q1112 id=gsm8k_mcq_01111 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total cost of all the red balls is 3 * $9 = $27. The total cost of all the blue balls is 11 * $5 = $55. The total cost of all the green balls is 25 * $3 = $75. The total cost of all the balls is $27 + $55 + $75 = $157. Therefore, the store will have received $157 after all the balls are sold.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
