2025-12-24 16:36:17 | INFO | Q1057 id=gsm8k_mcq_01056 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Greg does approximately 52 loads of laundry per year. This is because he washes 4 twin beds and 1 king size bed each week, and his laundry machine allows him to wash 2 twin sets of sheets and 1 king set of sheets at a time. Therefore, he needs to wash 4 x 2 = 8 twin sets + 1 = 9 sets of sheets per week. Since there are 52 weeks in a year, he will do 9 x 52 = 468 loads of laundry in a year. However, since his laundry machine can only wash 2 twin sets and 1 king set at a time, he will need to wash these sets in multiple batches throughout the year. Therefore, the actual number of loads of laundry that Greg does in a year may be slightly higher than 468. Option A (104) is the closest choice, so the answer is A.
2025-12-24 16:36:18 | INFO | Q1141 id=gsm8k_mcq_01140 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The given statement is confusing as it uses variables that are not clearly defined. However, assuming that the intent of the statement is to find out how many mashed potatoes Gomer ate, we can try to solve it using the given information.\n\nWe are given that it takes 3 less than 6 potatoes to make 1 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes. This can be written as:\n\n6 - 3 = 3\n3 - 1 = 2\n\nSo, it takes 2 less than 3 scoops of mashed potatoes to make 1 scoop of mashed potatoes. Therefore, to make 5 less than 23 scoops of mashed potatoes, we need to subtract 5 from 23, which gives us:\n\n23 - 5 = 18\n\nTherefore, Gomer ate 18 mashed potatoes.\n\nAnswer: A) 18
