2025-12-24 16:36:35 | INFO | Q1151 id=gsm8k_mcq_01150 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of roses that Patricia had before giving some away is 30. After giving 24 roses to her mother, she was left with 30 - 24 = 6 roses. Then, she bought 15 more roses, so she now has 6 + 15 = 21 roses. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 21.
2025-12-24 16:36:36 | INFO | Q1065 id=gsm8k_mcq_01064 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of classes that visited the Science Center last week is not explicitly stated in the given information. Therefore, it is not possible to determine the correct answer with certainty. However, we can make some estimates based on the provided data.\nOn Monday, 32 classes visited the Science Center. If twice as many visited on Tuesday, then 32 x 2 = 64 classes visited on Tuesday. Similarly, if three times as many visited on Wednesday, then 32 x 3 = 96 classes visited on Wednesday. Therefore, a total of 32 + 64 + 96 = 204 classes visited the Science Center on Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday.\nIf another 30 classes visited on Thursday and 25 visited on Friday, then the total number of classes that visited the Science Center on those two days is 30 + 25 = 55 classes. Therefore, the total number of classes that visited the Science Center over the five days is 204 + 55 = 259 classes.\nHowever, it is important to note that this estimate may not be accurate, as the given information does not specify the exact number of classes that visited each day. Additionally, the information provided does not specify whether all 55 classes visited both Thursday and Friday, or if some classes visited on only one of those days. Therefore, the actual number of classes that visited the Science Center last week could be higher or lower than 259.
2025-12-24 16:36:40 | INFO | Q1153 id=gsm8k_mcq_01152 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the probability of Mark winning at least one lottery ticket as follows:\n\nThe probability of Mark winning at least one lottery ticket is equal to 1 minus the probability of him not winning any tickets.\n\nThe probability of Mark not winning any tickets is 1 - (1 - 0.2) * (1 - 3 * 0.2) = 1 - 0.8 * 0.6 = 0.4\n\nTherefore, the probability of Mark winning at least one ticket is:\n\n1 - 0.4 = 0.6\n\nThis means that there is a 60% chance that Mark will win at least one lottery ticket.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is A) 60.
2025-12-24 16:36:41 | INFO | Q1067 id=gsm8k_mcq_01066 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The glee club ordered 20 pizzas and ate 70% of them, so they ate 20 * 0.7 = 14 pizzas. The football team ordered twice as many pizzas as the glee club, which is 20 * 2 = 40 pizzas. They ate 80% of these, which is 40 * 0.8 = 32 pizzas. So in total, the glee club and the football team ate 14 + 32 = 46 pizzas. Since there were 20 + 40 = 60 pizzas ordered, the number of pizzas left is 60 - 46 = 14 pizzas. Answer: A) 14
