2025-12-24 16:36:52 | INFO | Q1071 id=gsm8k_mcq_01070 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The correct answer is D) 12.\nTo find out how much Dennis will pay for 6 pounds of butter, we need to first calculate how much butter he needs to buy to make 6 dozen croissants. Since he uses 1 pound of butter for every dozen croissants, he will need 6 / 12 = 0.5 pounds of butter per croissant. Therefore, he will need 0.5 x 6 = 3 pounds of butter to make 6 dozen croissants.\nNext, we need to take into account the promotion at the grocery store. For every pound of butter purchased, the customer gets half off. Since the butter costs $4.00 a pound, Dennis will receive a discount of $4.00 / 2 = $2.00 for each pound of butter he buys. Therefore, he will save $2.00 on 3 pounds of butter, which equals a total savings of $2.00 x 3 = $6.00.\nFinally, we subtract the discount from the original price to find out how much Dennis will pay for 6 pounds of butter. The original price of 6 pounds of butter is $4.00 x 6 = $24.00. However, since he received a discount of $6.00, he will pay $24.00 - $6.00 = $18.00 for 6 pounds of butter.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 12.
2025-12-24 16:36:53 | INFO | Q1162 id=gsm8k_mcq_01161 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, Abraham will be able to sell 80 - 50 = 30 square meters of land after selling half of it for $50. This means he will be left with 30 / 2 = 15 square meters of land. After a month, he will be able to sell 15 / 4 = 3.75 square meters of land for $30. This brings his total earnings to 30 + 3.75 * 10 = 43.75 dollars. Finally, he will be able to sell the remaining 15 - 3.75 = 11.25 square meters of land for $3 per square meter, which will bring his total earnings to 43.75 + 11.25 * 10 = 140 dollars. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 140.
2025-12-24 16:36:55 | INFO | Q1164 id=gsm8k_mcq_01163 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Tyrion changes his face mask two times every time he goes out, and he goes out three times a day. Therefore, he uses two face masks every time he goes out, which means he uses six face masks in total over the course of a day. Since there are two days in every two-day period, Tyrion would use twelve face masks every two days.\nTherefore, the answer to the question is D) 12.
2025-12-24 16:37:00 | INFO | Q1073 id=gsm8k_mcq_01072 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nM + R = 60    (where M is the amount of money Maggie has and R is the amount of money Riza has)\n1/4M + 1/3R = 60   (using the information that Maggie spent a quarter of her money and Riza spent one-third of her money)\n\nWe can simplify this equation by multiplying both sides by 12 to eliminate the fractions:\n\n3M + 4R = 720\n\nSubtracting 3M from both sides gives us:\n\n4R = 720 - 3M\n\nDividing both sides by 4 gives us:\n\nR = 180 - 3/4M\n\nSubstituting this expression for R into the original equation gives us:\n\nM + 180 - 3/4M = 60\n\nMultiplying both sides by 4/3 gives us:\n\n4M + 600 - 120 = 240\n\nAdding 120 to both sides gives us:\n\n4M + 720 = 240 + 120\n\nSubtracting 720 from both sides gives us:\n\n4M = 840\n\nDividing both sides by 4 gives us:\n\nM = 210\n\nTherefore, Maggie has $210 left and Riza has $180 left.\n\nFinal Answer: C) 25
