2025-12-24 16:38:41 | INFO | Q1127 id=gsm8k_mcq_01126 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The circumference of the Earth is 40,000 kilometers, and Alfie flies 400 kilometers every day. To find out how many days it will take Alfie to fly a distance equal to half of the way around the Earth, we need to divide the circumference of the Earth by 2: 40,000 / 2 = 20,000 kilometers.\nSince Alfie flies 400 kilometers every day, it will take him 20,000 / 400 = 50 days to fly a distance equal to half of the way around the Earth.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 50.
