2025-12-24 16:38:55 | INFO | Q1133 id=gsm8k_mcq_01132 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount of money that Valerie, her brother, and their mother have together can be calculated as follows:\n\nValerie earns $5000 per month, which is half of what her brother earns. Therefore, her brother earns $5000 * 2 = $10000 per month.\n\nTogether, Valerie and her brother earn $5000 + $10000 = $15000 per month.\n\nTheir mother earns twice their combined salary, which means she earns $15000 * 2 = $30000 per month.\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money that they all have together is $15000 + $30000 = $45000 per month.\n\nThe correct answer is B) $45000.
