2025-12-24 16:39:46 | INFO | Q1258 id=gsm8k_mcq_01257 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the cost of popsicle sticks for Bob's project can be calculated as follows:\n\nBob needs 56 popsicle sticks, and each box of his favorite popsicles contains 8 sticks. Therefore, he will need 56 / 8 = 7 boxes of popsicles.\n\nEach box costs $2.00, so building his project will cost 7 * $2.00 = $14.00.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 14.\n\nFinal Answer: It will cost Bob $14.00 to build his project.
2025-12-24 16:39:48 | INFO | Q1260 id=gsm8k_mcq_01259 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of doughnuts that Derrick makes in June is 30 days * 10 dozen = 300 dozen. If he sells each doughnut for $2, he makes 300 dozen * $2 = $6000 in June.\nTherefore, the correct answer is not among the options provided.
2025-12-24 16:39:49 | INFO | Q1167 id=gsm8k_mcq_01166 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of fruits an avocado tree can produce during its 10 years of life is 2350.\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to add up the fruits produced by each age of the tree:\n\n- 5-year-old tree: 50 fruits\n- 6-year-old tree: 3 x 50 = 150 fruits\n- 7-year-old tree: 7 x 50 = 350 fruits\n- 8-year-old tree: 200 fruits less than a 10-year-old tree, so it produces 100 fruits - 200 = -100 fruits (但实际上不会出现负数，这只是一个计算上的问题)\n- 9-year-old tree: doesn't produce any fruit\n- 10-year-old tree: 20 x 50 = 1000 fruits\n\nAdding up all these numbers gives us:\n\n50 + 150 + 350 - 100 + 1000 = 2350 fruits\n\nTherefore, the total number of fruits an avocado tree can produce during its 10 years of life is 2350. The correct answer is D) 2350.
