2025-12-24 16:41:02 | INFO | Q1215 id=gsm8k_mcq_01214 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Jordan's wife changes half of the diapers, which means she will change 5 diaper changes / day for each child. Since Jordan has two children, he will therefore change 5 diaper changes / day for one child and 5 diaper changes / day for the other child, for a total of 10 diaper changes / day. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 10.
2025-12-24 16:41:03 | INFO | Q1304 id=gsm8k_mcq_01303 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=It takes 2 weeks to fill in all the holes. Here's how:\n\n  * Nate's dog digs 6 holes per day for 14 days, so he digs a total of 6 * 14 = 84 holes.\n  * When Nate gets home, he starts filling in 9 holes per day. It will take him 84 / 9 = 9 days to fill in all the holes that the dog dug before he got home.\n  * At this point, there are still 6 new holes being dug every night by the dog. It will take another 9 * 6 = 54 nights for the dog to dig these new holes.\n  * Since there are 7 days in a week, it will take the dog a total of 9 + 54 / 7 = 12 weeks to fill in all the holes.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 12.
2025-12-24 16:41:06 | INFO | Q1217 id=gsm8k_mcq_01216 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of people who entered the bus at the first station is 40. 3/4 of them, which is 3/4 * 40 = 30, entered the bus at the second station. The total number of people who have entered the bus so far is 40 + 30 = 70. At the third station, the number of passengers on the bus doubled to 70 * 2 = 140. To fill the remaining spaces on the bus, we need 200 - 140 = 60 more people. Therefore, the total number of people required to fill the remaining spaces on the bus is 60. Answer: A) 60
2025-12-24 16:41:08 | INFO | Q1219 id=gsm8k_mcq_01218 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The number of students who can try the escape room at a time is limited to 8, so in order for everyone to try the escape room, it will take 8 groups x 45 minutes = 360 minutes. Therefore, the answer is B) 360.
2025-12-24 16:41:08 | INFO | Q1306 id=gsm8k_mcq_01305 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The Adams family has made a total of 7995 cookies. Out of these, they have made 2595 rainbow cookies, 3075 oatmeal cookies, and some chocolate chip cookies. To find out how many chocolate chip cookies they have made, we need to subtract the number of other types of cookies from the total number of cookies.\nSo, the number of chocolate chip cookies = total number of cookies - number of rainbow cookies - number of oatmeal cookies\nSubstituting the given values, we get:\nnumber of chocolate chip cookies = 7995 - 2595 - 3075\nSimplifying the expression, we get:\nnumber of chocolate chip cookies = 2325\nTherefore, the Adams family has made 2325 chocolate chip cookies.\nAnswer: C) 2325
2025-12-24 16:41:10 | INFO | Q1308 id=gsm8k_mcq_01307 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each table requires 4 x 2 = 8 screws. Therefore, the total number of screws required for all four tables is 4 x 8 = 32 screws. Since James has 40 screws, he will have 40 - 32 = 8 screws left over. Therefore, the correct answer is C) 8.
