2025-12-24 16:41:12 | INFO | Q1221 id=gsm8k_mcq_01220 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the longer piece is four times longer than the shorter piece. Let's assume that the shorter piece is x feet long. Therefore, the longer piece would be 4x feet long.\nWe know that the total length of the board is 40 feet, so we can set up the equation: x + 4x = 40\nSimplifying the equation, we get 5x = 40\nDividing both sides by 5, we get x = 8\nTherefore, the shorter piece is 8 feet long, and the longer piece is 4 times longer than that, which is 4 * 8 = 32 feet long. So the correct answer is D) 32.\nFinal Answer: The longer piece is 32 feet long.
2025-12-24 16:41:14 | INFO | Q1312 id=gsm8k_mcq_01311 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The caretaker needs 3 feet of line for every foot of dock, so he needs 200 * 3 = 600 feet of line. He currently has 6 feet of new line, so he needs to buy 600 - 6 = 594 feet of line in total.\nAnswer: C
2025-12-24 16:41:15 | INFO | Q1223 id=gsm8k_mcq_01222 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total width of all the windows is 5 * 35 = 175 inches. Luke needs to buy fabric equal to 2 times the total width, so he needs 2 * 175 = 350 inches of fabric. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 350.\nFinal Answer: A) 350
2025-12-24 16:41:17 | INFO | Q1314 id=gsm8k_mcq_01313 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The cost price of each watermelon is $80/50 = $1.60 since the vendor bought 50 watermelons for $80. The selling price of each watermelon is $1.60 * 1.25 = $2.00 since the vendor sold all of them at a profit of 25%.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 2.10.
2025-12-24 16:41:17 | INFO | Q1225 id=gsm8k_mcq_01224 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it is expected that on Tuesday there will be 1 more inch of rain than twice the amount of rain that fell on Monday. On Monday, it rained 2 inches. Therefore, on Tuesday, it is expected to rain 2 * 2 + 1 = 5 inches of rain. The answer is A) 5.
2025-12-24 16:41:19 | INFO | Q1316 id=gsm8k_mcq_01315 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=After one hour, Ana will have peeled 3 + 60 = 63 oranges. Jane will have peeled 4 + 60 = 64 oranges. Therefore, Ana will have peeled 63 - 64 = 1 fewer oranges than Jane after one hour. The answer is B: 1.
2025-12-24 16:41:20 | INFO | Q1227 id=gsm8k_mcq_01226 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The total cost for a basic manicure and a pedicure is $35 + $40 = $75. With a 20% discount, Karen will pay $75 * (1 - 20%) = $60. Adding nail art on each finger will cost $3 * 10 = $30. So Karen will pay $60 + $30 = $90 in all. The correct answer is D.
2025-12-24 16:41:25 | INFO | Q1318 id=gsm8k_mcq_01317 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up an equation for the number of cows and chickens on the farm:\n\nLet x be the number of cows\nLet y be the number of chickens\n\nWe know that:\n\nx + y = 20 (there are a total of 20 animals)\n4x + 2y = 70 (the total number of legs is 70)\n\nSimplifying the second equation, we get:\n\n4x + 2y = 2 * 35\n4x + 2y = 70\n\nSubtracting 2y from both sides, we get:\n\n4x = 50\n\nDividing both sides by 4, we get:\n\nx = 12.5\n\nSince we cannot have half a cow, we must round down to 12 cows. Substituting this value back into the first equation, we get:\n\n12 + y = 20\ny = 8\n\nTherefore, there are 8 chickens on the farm.\n\nAnswer: C) 8
2025-12-24 16:41:26 | INFO | Q1229 id=gsm8k_mcq_01228 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The information provided states that Samantha has 12 fewer paintings than Shelley, who has 8 paintings more than Kim. Let’s use these pieces of information to determine the number of paintings that each person has.\n\nFirst, let’s find out how many paintings Shelley has. We do this by adding 12 to the number of paintings that Samantha has:\n\nShelley = Samantha + 12\n\nWe also know that Shelley has 8 more paintings than Kim. Let’s add 8 to the number of paintings that Shelley has to find out how many paintings Kim has:\n\nKim = Shelley - 8\n\nSubstituting the value we found for Shelley into the equation for Kim, we get:\n\nKim = (Samantha + 12) - 8\n\nNow we can substitute the value we found for Samantha into the equation for Kim:\n\nKim = (27 + 12) - 8\n\nSolving for Kim, we get:\n\nKim = 39 - 8\nKim = 31\n\nTherefore, Kim has 31 paintings. The correct answer is B).
2025-12-24 16:41:28 | INFO | Q01 id=gsm8k_mcq_00037 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that John used $60 for video games because 8 x $20 = $160. We can also calculate that he sold $195 worth of lego sets because 13 x $15 = $207.50. Therefore, he has $45 left because $207.50 - $160 = $47.50. This means that John still has 13 lego sets because $47.50 / $15 = 3 lego sets. Answer: D) 13
2025-12-24 16:41:30 | INFO | Q1231 id=gsm8k_mcq_01230 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The standard fee for each lesson is $80, so Charlie earns $80 x 4 = $320 from the four standard lessons. For the two lessons with a veteran, he reduces his rate by 25%, so he charges $80 x 0.75 = $60 less per hour. Since he has two such lessons, he earns $60 x 2 = $120 less for these lessons. Therefore, he earns $320 - $120 = $200 from the two lessons with a veteran. Altogether, Charlie will make $320 + $200 = $520 for the day. Answer: C) 400
