2025-12-24 16:41:43 | INFO | Q1241 id=gsm8k_mcq_01240 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of books that Elly has is 110. We can break down the number of books each shelf can hold as follows:\n\n  * Middle shelf: 10 books\n  * Bottom shelf: 2 x 10 = 20 books\n  * Top shelf: 5 fewer than 20 = 15 books\n\nTherefore, Elly needs three bookcases to hold all of her books. The correct answer is D) 3.
2025-12-24 16:41:46 | INFO | Q1243 id=gsm8k_mcq_01242 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of hats that are not red or blue is 100 - 1/2 * 100 = 50. Since 3/5 of the remaining hats are blue, Skyler has 3/5 * 50 = 30 blue hats. Therefore, Skyler has 50 - 30 = 20 white hats.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
2025-12-24 16:41:52 | INFO | Q1245 id=gsm8k_mcq_01244 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we know that Audrey needs to correctly answer 70% of the total questions on both tests to move on to the 7th grade. We also know that the first test has 70 questions and she gets 60% of them correct, which means she got 60/70 * 70 = 42 questions correct.\nThe second test has 40 questions, so to move on to the 7th grade, she needs to get at least 70% of the total number of questions correct, which is 70 * 40 = 280 questions. To calculate how many questions she needs to get right on the second test, we divide the total number of questions she needs to get correct by the percentage she needs to get correct: 280 / 0.7 = 400 questions. This means she needs to get at least 400/40 = 10 questions correct on the second test to move on to the 7th grade.\nTherefore, the answer is D) 28.
2025-12-24 16:41:55 | INFO | Q1247 id=gsm8k_mcq_01246 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The correct answer is A) 3360.\nTo arrive at this answer, we need to multiply the number of games played by the number of points scored per game for each year. Since Ara has been playing 40 games every year and her score for every game is 21 points, we can calculate the total number of points she has scored in one year as follows:\n40 games x 21 points = 840 points\nTherefore, the total number of points she has scored in four years would be:\n40 games x 840 points = 3360 points\nThus, the correct answer is A) 3360.
2025-12-24 16:41:58 | INFO | Q1249 id=gsm8k_mcq_01248 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that for every 25 telephone calls made, on average, one customer comes to the dealership to look at new cars. Therefore, to sell 15 cars, Jason would need to make 15 / (1 / 25) = 375 telephone calls.\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 375.
2025-12-24 16:42:00 | INFO | Q1251 id=gsm8k_mcq_01250 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total number of chips that Mitchell buys is 2 * 55 = 110 chips. Since his family has five members, each person will get 110 / 5 = 22 chips.\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 22.
2025-12-24 16:42:02 | INFO | Q1253 id=gsm8k_mcq_01252 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of items that Dominick saw as follows:\n\nHalf as many robots as helmets means that there were 20/2=10 robots in the changing room.\nHalf as many helmets as footballs means that there were 20/2=10 footballs in the changing room.\n\nTherefore, Dominick saw a total of 10+10+20=30 items in the changing room.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 60.
2025-12-24 16:42:06 | INFO | Q1255 id=gsm8k_mcq_01254 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The time it takes for the coat of varnish to dry on six paintings with the new varnish is 12 minutes x 6 = 72 minutes. The time it takes for the coat of varnish to dry on six paintings with the old varnish is 7 minutes x 6 = 42 minutes. Therefore, the difference in drying time is 72 - 42 = 30 minutes. The correct answer is D) 30.\nTherefore, the total time it will take for the coat of varnish on six paintings with the new varnish to dry is 72 + 12 = 84 minutes.
2025-12-24 16:42:18 | INFO | Q1257 id=gsm8k_mcq_01256 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The total distance that Phineas needs to travel is 200 yards, which we can divide into two equal parts: half on land and half in water.\nLet's assume that the distance on land is x yards and the distance in water is y yards. We know that x + y = 200, since the total distance is 200 yards.\nWe also know that Phineas hops at a speed of 20 yards per minute on land and swims at a speed of 10 yards per minute in water. Let's assume that it takes him t minutes to travel the entire distance.\nIf half of the distance is on land and half is in water, then it takes him t/2 minutes to travel the distance on land and t/2 minutes to travel the distance in water.\nSince Phineas travels at a constant speed, we can say that the time it takes him to travel each part of the distance is proportional to the length of that part of the distance. In other words, if the distance on land is twice as long as the distance in water, then it will take him twice as long to travel the distance on land.\nTherefore, we can write the equation t/2 = x/20 + y/10. Solving for t, we get t = x/4 + y/2.\nSubstituting x + y = 200, we get t = 200/4 + y/2 = 50 + y/2.\nFinally, substituting t = x/4 + y/2 into the equation t = x/20 + y/10, we get x/20 + y/10 = 50 + y/2. Simplifying, we get x/20 = 49/2. Solving for x, we get x = 980/20 = 49.\nTherefore, the distance on land is 49 yards and the distance in water is 101 yards. It will take Phineas 50 + 101/2 = 76.5 minutes to return home.\nSo the answer is D) 15.
2025-12-24 16:42:21 | INFO | Q1259 id=gsm8k_mcq_01258 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the main phone costs twice as much as each additional phone. If the main phone plan costs $20, then each additional phone costs $20/2=$10\. Therefore, the total cost of five additional phones would be $10*5=$50\. Adding the cost of the main phone plan, the whole phone plan would cost $20+$50=$70\. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 70\.
2025-12-24 16:42:23 | INFO | Q1261 id=gsm8k_mcq_01260 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=She has 210 photos and she needs to upload them in groups of 7 photos per batch. To find out how many batches she needs to upload all of her photos, divide the total number of photos by the number of photos per batch: 210 / 7 = 30 batches. So she will need 30 days to upload all of her photos.\nTherefore, the answer is C) 30.
2025-12-24 16:42:31 | INFO | Q1263 id=gsm8k_mcq_01262 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The time it takes for John to speak 10 pages at a speed of 2.5 times his normal speed would be:\n\n10 pages * 450 words/page = 4500 words\n\nTo find how long it would take him to speak those 4500 words at his normal speed of 150 WPM, we can divide the total number of words by his normal speaking rate:\n\n4500 words / 150 WPM = 30 minutes\n\nTherefore, it would take John approximately 30 minutes to speak 10 pages at his normal speed.\n\nHowever, since John's speed has increased to 2.5 times his normal speed after training, his actual speaking time would be shorter than 30 minutes. To find the exact amount of time it would take him, we can multiply his normal speaking rate by 2.5:\n\n150 WPM * 2.5 = 37.5 WPM\n\nNow we can divide the total number of words by John's new speaking rate to find his actual speaking time:\n\n4500 words / 37.5 WPM = 120 minutes\n\nTherefore, it would take John approximately 120 minutes to speak 10 pages at his current speed.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 12.
2025-12-24 16:42:36 | INFO | Q1265 id=gsm8k_mcq_01264 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of popcorn kernels that pop during the first 30 seconds is 20. In the next 30 seconds, the rate of popping increases to three times that amount, which is 20 x 3 = 60 kernels. In the following 30 seconds, the rate of popping increases to four times the initial rate, which is 4 x 60 = 240 kernels. Therefore, the total number of popcorn kernels that pop during the first 90 seconds is 20 + 60 + 240 = 320 kernels. Since a quarter of the number of kernels that pop in the final 30 seconds also pop from the residual heat, this means that 320 x 1 / 4 = 80 kernels pop from the residual heat. Therefore, the total number of popcorn kernels that Garret eats is 320 - 80 = 240 kernels. Answer: C) 360
2025-12-24 16:42:38 | INFO | Q1267 id=gsm8k_mcq_01266 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total amount of dog food consumed by the German Shepherds and the Bulldog in a day is 5 + 3 = 8 kilograms. Therefore, they will need 8 x 7 = 56 kilograms of dog food in a week. The correct answer is D) 56.
2025-12-24 16:42:44 | INFO | Q1269 id=gsm8k_mcq_01268 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can start by setting up an equation for the total number of blocks in the tower:\n\n4 blue blocks + 2 * yellow blocks + unknown number of red blocks = 32\n\nWe can simplify this equation by combining the blue and yellow blocks:\n\n4 blue blocks + 2 * (blue blocks + yellow blocks) = 32\n\nSimplifying further, we get:\n\n4 blue blocks + 2 * 4 blue blocks + 2 * yellow blocks = 32\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n12 blue blocks + 2 * yellow blocks = 32\n\nSubtracting 12 blue blocks from both sides, we get:\n\n2 * yellow blocks = 20\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\nyellow blocks = 10\n\nTherefore, there are 10 yellow blocks in the tower. Since there are four blue blocks and twice as many yellow blocks, there must be 4 * 2 = 8 red blocks in the tower.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D) 20.
2025-12-24 16:42:50 | INFO | Q1271 id=gsm8k_mcq_01270 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The boat depreciated 30% over the first year, so its value decreased by 30/100 * $9000 = $2700. The total value of the boat after the first year was $9000 - $2700 = $6300\. The boat depreciated another 30% over the second year, so its value decreased by 30/100 * $6300 = $1890. The total value of the boat after the second year was $6300 - $1890 = $4410\. The boat depreciated another 20% over the third year, so its value decreased by 20/100 * $4410 = $882. The total value of the boat after the third year was $4410 - $882 = $3528\. Therefore, the boat is worth $3528 after the three years. Answer: C) 3528
2025-12-24 16:42:52 | INFO | Q1274 id=gsm8k_mcq_01273 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Mazie gave 21 marbles to Dallas and 21 marbles to Darla, so the total number of marbles given to the twins is 21 + 21 = 42 marbles. However, it is not specified whether these marbles were given equally to both Dallas and Darla or if they were given differently. Therefore, the answer cannot be determined with the given information.
2025-12-24 16:42:55 | INFO | Q1277 id=gsm8k_mcq_01276 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the total length of the fence is 20 feet on the long side and 15 feet on the short side. To calculate the total length of the fence, we need to add the length of both sides together: 20 + 15 = 35 feet.\nTherefore, James needs to buy 35 feet of crepe paper.\nAnswer: B
2025-12-24 16:42:57 | INFO | Q1279 id=gsm8k_mcq_01278 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of seashells found by Tom, Nancy, and Benny is 214 + 432 + 86 = 752. After cleaning, the number of good seashells found is 752 - 67 = 685. Therefore, the answer is C) 665.
2025-12-24 16:42:58 | INFO | Q1281 id=gsm8k_mcq_01280 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=It took Anna 2 hours more than half of Steve's time, which means she took 2 + (10 / 2) = 6 hours to complete the puzzle. Therefore, the answer is A) 12.
2025-12-24 16:43:01 | INFO | Q1283 id=gsm8k_mcq_01282 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of hot dogs needed for the party is 20 * 2 = 40 hot dogs. Since John already has 4 hot dogs left over from a previous party, he needs to buy 40 - 4 = 36 hot dogs. A pack of hot dogs contains 6 hot dogs, so he needs to buy 36 / 6 = 6 packs of hot dogs. Since each pack of hot dogs costs $2, John needs to spend 6 * 2 = $12 on hot dogs.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (D).
2025-12-24 16:43:05 | INFO | Q1285 id=gsm8k_mcq_01284 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The number of children following the truck at any given point is equal to the number of children who started chasing the truck plus the number of new children that joined on each subsequent street. We can calculate this as follows:\n\nAt the end of the first street, there are 5 children.\nOn the second street, each child is joined by another child, so there are 5 + 5 = 10 children.\nOn the third street, each child in the existing group is joined by another two children, so there are 10 + 2 * 5 = 25 children.\n\nTherefore, the total number of children following the truck is 25. Answer: C.
2025-12-24 16:43:08 | INFO | Q1287 id=gsm8k_mcq_01286 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount of money that James has is:\n\n1 quarter = 25 cents\n2 nickels = 10 cents each = 20 cents\n7 dimes = 10 cents each = 70 cents\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money that James has is:\n\n25 + 20 + 70 = 115 cents\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 95.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is A) 95.
2025-12-24 16:43:13 | INFO | Q1289 id=gsm8k_mcq_01288 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=We know that Charisma meditates for 15 minutes every day for 5 days a week, which equals to 75 minutes of meditation per week. Additionally, she practices yoga for 1 hour every week for 4 weeks, which equals to 4 hours of yoga practice per week.\nTherefore, the total amount of time Charisma spends on meditation and yoga practice in 4 weeks is 75 + 4 = 79 minutes.\nThe closest choice from the options provided is A) 42, which is not the correct answer.\nThe correct answer is D) 27, as we can calculate 79 - 27 = 52 minutes remaining if we subtract the time already mentioned from the total time available. However, since we cannot count partial minutes, we should round down to 50 minutes.\nHence, Charisma has spent 50 minutes on meditation and yoga practice in 4 weeks.
2025-12-24 16:43:16 | INFO | Q1291 id=gsm8k_mcq_01290 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The question states that a large sunflower has 50% more seeds than a small sunflower, which means that the large sunflower has 133.33% as many seeds as the small sunflower (since 100% + 50% = 150%). Therefore, the large sunflower has 3 x 133.33 = 400 seeds. The total number of seeds from both the small and large sunflowers is 400 + 3 x 12 = 420 seeds. The correct answer is C) 90.
2025-12-24 16:43:20 | INFO | Q1293 id=gsm8k_mcq_01292 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The information provided states that Jackie grew three inches over the summer and is now two inches shorter than Anne, who is twice the size of Albert. If Albert is thirty-six inches tall, then we can set up the following equation to find the height of Jackie before summer:\n\nAnne = 2 * (Albert + 3)\nJackie = Anne - 2\n\nSubstituting in the value for Albert, we get:\n\nAnne = 2 * (36 + 3) = 84\nJackie = 84 - 2 = 82\n\nTherefore, Jackie was eight inches taller before summer.\n\nAnswer: C) 82
2025-12-24 16:43:24 | INFO | Q1295 id=gsm8k_mcq_01294 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred= | followup_correct=False | raw=The total amount of money Jake spends at the store is $36.\nTo find the total amount of money Jake spends at the store, we need to add up the cost of the two T-shirts and the cost of the shoes.\nThe cost of the two T-shirts is 2 * $8 = $16.\nThe cost of the shoes is $40 * (1 - 40%) = $40 * 60% = $24.\nTherefore, the total amount of money Jake spends at the store is $16 + $24 = $40.\nHowever, since the question asks for the total amount of money spent at the store, not the total amount spent on individual items, the correct answer is $40.
2025-12-24 16:43:25 | INFO | Q1297 id=gsm8k_mcq_01296 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total amount that Ellen and Lani spent at the mall is $100 + $5 + $30 + $100 = $235. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 235.
2025-12-24 16:43:29 | INFO | Q1299 id=gsm8k_mcq_01298 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of dollars in the jar can be calculated by adding up the value of each type of coin:\n\n  * Quarters: 32 x $0.25 = $8\n  * Dimes: 95 x $0.10 = $9.50\n  * Nickels: 120 x $0.05 = $6\n  * Pennies: 750 x $0.01 = $7.50\n\nAdding these values together gives us a total of $8 + $9.50 + $6 + $7.50 = $24.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 31.
2025-12-24 16:43:32 | INFO | Q1301 id=gsm8k_mcq_01300 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Josh makes $4 per car and he services 3 cars per day. Therefore, his daily earnings would be $4 x 3 = $12\. Since he is open every day of the week except Sunday and Wednesday, he works for 5 days per week. Therefore, his weekly earnings would be $12 x 5 = $60\. Finally, since there are 2 weeks in a month, his monthly earnings would be $60 x 2 = $120\. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 120.
2025-12-24 16:43:36 | INFO | Q1303 id=gsm8k_mcq_01302 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount of money that Matthew would earn from selling half of his collection at $5 per toy and the other half at $7 per toy is:\n\n(12 / 2) * $5 + (12 / 2) * $7 = $30 + $42 = $72\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 72.\n\n反思：在回答问题时，我们应该仔细听取问题的描述，并结合相关知识进行推理和计算，以得出准确的答案。同时，我们也应该注意避免误解问题的要求，如选择一个字母等。
2025-12-24 16:43:39 | INFO | Q1305 id=gsm8k_mcq_01304 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The average enrollment at Norman High School is 4000 students per year. The enrollment at Butler High School is 3/4 as many students as Norman High School, which means Butler High School has 3000 students per year. Therefore, the difference between the average enrollment at Norman High School and Butler High School is 4000 - 3000 = 1000 students. The correct answer is D) 1000.
2025-12-24 16:43:41 | INFO | Q1307 id=gsm8k_mcq_01306 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Igor lost 7 beakers on the way to the lab bench. This means that the total number of beakers that Igor had placed on the lab bench was 7 + the correct number of beakers he picked up, which is 7 + 7 = 14 beakers. Therefore, the answer to the question is A) 7.
2025-12-24 16:43:43 | INFO | Q1309 id=gsm8k_mcq_01308 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The question states that there are 10 eggs in the first basket and twice as many eggs in the second basket. To find the total number of eggs in both baskets, we need to add the number of eggs in each basket together.\nTherefore, the total number of eggs in both baskets is 10 + 2 x 10 = 30.\nSo the correct answer is C: 30.
2025-12-24 16:43:45 | INFO | Q1311 id=gsm8k_mcq_01310 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\nAaron's time = 16 minutes\n\nVanessa's time = 4 miles * 2 times Aaron's speed = 4 miles * 2(16 minutes) = 64 minutes\n\nTherefore, Vanessa took 64 minutes to complete her part of the race.\n\nAnswer: B) 64
2025-12-24 16:43:49 | INFO | Q1313 id=gsm8k_mcq_01312 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the revenue generated by Tom's restaurant for two days per week as follows:\n\nThey get 6 reservations per night and typically order two meals that cost $5 each, so each reservation generates $10 in revenue. Additionally, they sell a $5 bottle of wine with each reservation, which brings in an additional $5.\n\nTherefore, for two days per week when the restaurant is open, they generate a total of 6 * 2 = 12 reservations. This means they make a revenue of 12 * 10 + 12 * 5 = $180 per week.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 180.
2025-12-24 16:43:52 | INFO | Q1315 id=gsm8k_mcq_01314 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the question, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJames = 2 * Dora + 19\nJohn's youngest son = 32 + 3\n\nSubstituting the value of James from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n\nJohn's youngest son = 32 + 3 + 19\nJohn's youngest son = 64\n\nTherefore, John's youngest son will be 64 years old in 3 years.\n\nAnswer: D) 67
2025-12-24 16:43:56 | INFO | Q1317 id=gsm8k_mcq_01316 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total cost of the new radiator is $400, but Mark got it for 80% off, so he paid $400 * (1 - 80%) = $400 * 20% = $80 less. So the price he paid for the radiator is $400 - $80 = $320. The installation of the radiator took 3 hours at $50 an hour, so he paid $50 * 3 = $150. Adding the cost of the radiator and the installation, Mark paid $320 + $150 = $470. Therefore, the correct answer is D) $470.
2025-12-24 16:43:58 | INFO | Q1319 id=gsm8k_mcq_01318 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of slices is 56 because 7 x 8 = 56. There are 4 people who want to share the pizzas equally, so each person can have 14 slices because 56 / 4 = 14.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (A).
2025-12-24 16:44:01 | INFO | Q03 id=gsm8k_mcq_00564 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=In the first week, Judy read for 15 minutes each night before going to sleep. In the second week, she read a total of 100 pages. If she can read 2 pages per 1.5 minutes, it means she read 100/2=50 pages in the second week. Therefore, in two weeks, she read a total of 50+15=65 pages. The answer is C) 65.
2025-12-24 16:44:05 | INFO | Q03 id=gsm8k_mcq_00660 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=low | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\n2x + 4y = 70 (since each sheep has 2 legs and each goose has 4 legs)\nwhere x represents the number of sheep and y represents the number of geese.\n\nWe also know that the total number of heads is 20, so:\n\nx + y = 20 (since each sheep has 1 head and each goose has 1 head)\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\n2x + 4(20 - x) = 70\n\nSimplifying and solving for x, we find that x = 15.\n\nTherefore, there are 15 sheep living on Lee's farm. The answer is A.
