2025-12-24 16:46:09 | INFO | Q46 id=gsm8k_mcq_00045 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of hours Meredith spent writing articles in the three days as follows:\n\nOn Monday, she wrote 5 articles, which took an average of 4 hours each for a total of 20 hours.\n\nOn Tuesday, she wrote twice the number of articles she wrote on Monday, which was 2 * 5 = 10 articles. Therefore, she spent 10 * 4 = 40 hours writing articles on Tuesday.\n\nOn Wednesday, she wrote twice the number of articles she wrote on Tuesday, which was 2 * 10 = 20 articles. Therefore, she spent 20 * 4 = 80 hours writing articles on Wednesday.\n\nIn total, Meredith spent 20 + 40 + 80 = 140 hours writing articles in the three days.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is not among the options provided.
2025-12-24 16:46:09 | INFO | Q53 id=gsm8k_mcq_00052 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Uriah needs to remove 15 pounds from his book bag. Each comic book weighs 1/4 pound and each toy weighs 1/2 pound. If he removes 30 comic books, then he will have removed 30 * 1/4 = 7.5 pounds from his book bag. This means that he still needs to remove 15 - 7.5 = 7.5 pounds more. Since each toy weighs 1/2 pound, Uriah would need to remove 7.5 / (1/2) = 15 toys to reach his goal of removing 15 pounds from his book bag. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 15.
2025-12-24 16:46:11 | INFO | Q48 id=gsm8k_mcq_00047 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that John bought 200/40=5 red ties, which cost 50% more than the blue ties, so he spent 500%*40=$200 on red ties. Therefore, the total amount John spent on ties is $200+$40=$240. So the answer is not A, but rather C) $240.
2025-12-24 16:46:13 | INFO | Q55 id=gsm8k_mcq_00054 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the Doubtfire family has 7 kittens adopted from the local animal shelter and their two house cats have just had kittens as well. We know that Patchy, the first cat, has had thrice the number of adopted kittens, which means she has had 7 x 3 = 21 kittens. We also know that Trixie, the other cat, has had 12 kittens. Therefore, the total number of kittens that the Doubtfire family has now is 21 + 12 + 7 = 40. So the correct answer is B) 40.
2025-12-24 16:46:14 | INFO | Q50 id=gsm8k_mcq_00049 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that there are a total of 15 * 8 = 120 units in the building. Since 3/4 of the building is occupied, then 1 - 3/4 = 1/4 of the building is unoccupied. Therefore, the total number of unoccupied units in the building is 120 * 1/4 = 30. So the answer is D) 30.
2025-12-24 16:46:16 | INFO | Q57 id=gsm8k_mcq_00056 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Peter can go to the movies 3 times this week because he has 42 dollars for the week and each movie ticket costs $7. Therefore, the total amount of money he can spend on movies is 42/7=6 dollars. Since each movie ticket costs $7, Peter can go to the movies 6/7=0.857 times, which rounds down to 0 times. However, since Peter cannot go to the movies 0 times, he can only go to the movies 3 times this week. Therefore, the answer is D) 3.
