2025-12-24 16:46:43 | INFO | Q76 id=gsm8k_mcq_00075 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can see that each level of a sandcastle has half the square footage as the level below it. Therefore, if the top level of the sandcastle has a square footage of 16, then the bottom level will have twice that amount, which is 32 square feet. The next level will have half of 32, which is 16 square feet. And finally, the bottom level of the sandcastle will have half of 16, which is 8 square feet.\nTherefore, the average square footage of a level in this sandcastle is (16 + 32 + 16 + 8) / 4 = 52 / 4 = 13 square feet. So the answer is A) 80.
2025-12-24 16:46:44 | INFO | Q64 id=gsm8k_mcq_00063 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total amount Aleena had paid for the streaming service by the end of the year as follows:\n\nThe streaming service charges her $140 per month for 12 months, so for the first six months, she pays $140 x 6 = $840.\n\nFor the second six months, the streaming service charges her 10% less money than the previous six months. Since 10% of $840 is $840 x 0.10 = $84, the streaming service charges her $840 - $84 = $756 for the second six months.\n\nTherefore, the total amount Aleena had paid for the streaming service by the end of the year is $840 + $756 = $1596.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 1596.
