2025-12-24 16:47:41 | INFO | Q93 id=gsm8k_mcq_00092 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equations:\n\nAmy = 5 + x\nJackson = 5 - x + 2\nCorey = 5 - x - 2\n\nWhere x represents the number of years between Amy and Jackson.\n\nWe also know that James is 10 years younger than Corey, so:\n\nJames = 10 - y\nwhere y represents the number of years between Corey and James.\n\nSubstituting the values for Amy, Jackson, and Corey into the equation for James, we get:\n\n10 - y = 5 - x - 2 + 2\n10 - y = 5 - x\ny = 5 - x\n\nSubstituting this value for y into the equation for Jackson, we get:\n\nJackson = 5 - x + 2\nx = 3\n\nTherefore, Jackson is 5 years old.\n\nAnswer: D) 9
