2025-12-24 16:47:57 | INFO | Q95 id=gsm8k_mcq_00094 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of rabbits = Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nWe also know that there are two cats for every dog, so we can write:\n\nNumber of dogs = Number of cats / 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = Number of cats + Number of cats / 2 - 12\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits = 2 * Number of cats + Number of cats - 24\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits = 3 * Number of cats - 24\n\nAdding 24 to both sides, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits + 24 = 3 * Number of cats\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits + 12 = Number of cats\n\nSubstituting the value of Number of dogs from the second equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits + 12 = Number of cats + Number of cats / 2\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n2 * (Number of rabbits + 12) = 2 * (Number of cats + Number of cats / 2)\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n2 * (Number of rabbits + 12) = 3 * Number of cats\n\nSubtracting 12 from both sides, we get:\n\n2 * Number of rabbits = 3 * Number of cats - 12\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 3 * Number of cats - 6\n\nSubstituting the value of Number of dogs from the second equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 3 * Number of cats - 6 + Number of dogs\n\nSince the number of rabbits is twelve less than the combined number of pet dogs and cats, we can write:\n\nNumber of rabbits = Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nSubstituting the value of Number of dogs from the second equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = (Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12) + Number of dogs\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 2 * Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nTherefore, the total number of pets in the neighborhood is:\n\n2 * Number of dogs + Number of cats - 12\n\nSubstituting the values of Number of dogs and Number of cats from the second equation, we get:\n\n2 * 60 + 1 * 2 - 12 = 120 + 2 - 12 = 120 + 10 = 130\n\nTherefore, there are a total of 130 pets in the neighborhood.\n\nAnswer: C) 372
