2025-12-24 16:48:47 | INFO | Q117 id=gsm8k_mcq_00116 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the equation as follows:\n7x + 13y = 120\nWhere x represents the number of teaspoons of sugar and y represents the number of cups of water.\nSince the ratio of sugar to water is 7:13, we can say that for every 7 teaspoons of sugar, there are 13 cups of water. Therefore, if we multiply both sides of the equation by 13/7, we get:\n13x + 19y = 160\nSubstituting the value of 120 for the left-hand side of the equation, we get:\n13x + 19(120/13) = 160\nSimplifying the right-hand side of the equation, we get:\n13x + 196 = 160\nSubtracting 196 from both sides of the equation, we get:\n13x = -36\nDividing both sides of the equation by 13, we get:\nx = -36/13\nTherefore, the number of teaspoonfuls of sugar Katy used was approximately -2.85 teaspoonfuls. However, since sugar cannot be measured in fractional amounts, we need to round this value down to the nearest whole number. Therefore, Katy used approximately 2 teaspoons of sugar. The closest choice among the options is A) 78, which is not the correct answer. The correct answer is C) 2.
