2025-12-24 16:49:04 | INFO | Q153 id=gsm8k_mcq_00152 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=If Carl pays with a $10 bill, he will receive $10 in change. This is because each pack of cookies costs $0.10, and he buys 10 packs, so the total cost is 10 * $0.10 = $1.00. If he has a $10 bill, he can pay for all 10 packs of cookies and still have $9 left over as change. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 9.40.
