2025-12-24 16:49:09 | INFO | Q155 id=gsm8k_mcq_00154 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate the total number of hours Kimo spends attending classes as follows:\n\nOn weekdays (Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays), Kimo has three 1-hour classes per day, so he spends 3 * 3 = 9 hours per week on these days.\n\nOn Tuesdays and Thursdays, Kimo has two 2-hour classes per day, so he spends 2 * 2 = 4 hours per week on these days.\n\nTherefore, in one semester (16 weeks), Kimo spends 9 + 4 = 13 hours per week attending classes.\n\nHence, in one semester, Kimo spends 13 * 16 = 208 hours attending classes.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 208.
