2025-12-24 16:51:09 | INFO | Q194 id=gsm8k_mcq_00193 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=At noon on Sunday, there were 18 pink plastic flamingos + 18 pink plastic flamingos = 36 pink plastic flamingos. At noon on Sunday, there were 36 pink plastic flamingos - 18 white plastic flamingos = 18 white plastic flamingos. Therefore, at noon on Sunday, there were 36 pink plastic flamingos - 18 white plastic flamingos = 18 more pink plastic flamingos than white plastic flamingos.\n\nThe answer is (C).
2025-12-24 16:51:09 | INFO | Q219 id=gsm8k_mcq_00218 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The ages given are:\n\n  * Adrian's age is three times the age of Harriet\n  * Harriet is half the age of Zack\n\nWe can use these equations to find the ages of Adrian and Zack.\n\n  * Adrian's age = 3 x Harriet's age\n  * Harriet's age = Zack's age / 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first gives:\n\n  * Adrian's age = 3 x (Zack's age / 2)\n  * Adrian's age = (3/2) x Zack's age\n\nSince we know that Harriet is 21 years old, we can substitute that value into the second equation to find Zack's age:\n\n  * Harriet's age = Zack's age / 2\n  * 21 = Zack's age / 2\n  * Zack's age = 42\n\nNow we can substitute the values we found for Adrian's and Zack's ages into the equation for Adrian's age:\n\n  * Adrian's age = (3/2) x 42\n  * Adrian's age = 63\n\nSo Adrian is 63 years old, Harriet is 21 years old, and Zack is 42 years old.\n\nIf we want to calculate the average age of the three in three years, we need to add their current ages together and then divide by 3. In three years, Harriet will be 24 years old, Zack will be 45 years old, and Adrian will be 66 years old. So the average age of the three in three years will be:\n\n  * (24 + 45 + 66) / 3\n  * 135 / 3\n  * 45\n\nTherefore, the average age of the three in three years will be 45 years old. The answer is B.
