2025-12-24 16:51:12 | INFO | Q196 id=gsm8k_mcq_00195 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The cost of 8 pens can be found by multiplying the cost of one pen by 8. Since a pen costs as much as a pencil and eraser combined, and a pencil costs $1.20 and an eraser costs $0.30, we can find the cost of one pen by combining the cost of a pencil and an eraser: $1.20 + $0.30 = $1.50\. Therefore, the cost of 8 pens will be $8 x $1.50 = $12\. Answer: A)
