2025-12-24 16:51:20 | INFO | Q200 id=gsm8k_mcq_00199 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Mark earns 5 cents per sentence from Publisher A, so he makes 5 * 1000 = 5000 cents from Publisher A per week. We also know that Publisher B pays him twice what Publisher A pays, which means they pay him 2 * 5 = 10 cents per sentence. Therefore, Mark earns 10 * 1000 = 10000 cents per week from Publisher B. In total, Mark makes 5000 + 10000 = 15000 cents per week. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 15000.
2025-12-24 16:51:20 | INFO | Q227 id=gsm8k_mcq_00226 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total number of cards that are not water type as follows:\n\nTotal number of cards = 30 + 20 + 40 = 90\n\nNumber of water type cards lost = 8\nNumber of grass type cards bought = 14\n\nNumber of cards remaining = 90 - 8 + 14 = 86\n\nTherefore, the percentage chance of a randomly picked card being a water type is:\n\nNumber of water type cards / Total number of cards * 100 = 86 / 90 * 100 ≈ 95.56%\n\nRounding this to the nearest integer gives us 96.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 36.
2025-12-24 16:51:25 | INFO | Q230 id=gsm8k_mcq_00229 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the number of watermelons that were not ready to be harvested after the two weeks as follows:\n\nAt two months, Ashlyn found out that 30% of the watermelons were ready for harvest, so she took 100% - 30% = 70% of the watermelons home. This means she took 120 x 70% = 84 watermelons.\n\nTwo weeks later, 3/4 of the remaining melons were ready for harvest, so she harvested 3/4 x 84 = 63 watermelons.\n\nTherefore, the number of watermelons that were not ready to be harvested after the two weeks is 84 - 63 = 21.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 21.
2025-12-24 16:51:26 | INFO | Q202 id=gsm8k_mcq_00201 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate John's earnings for the year as follows:\n\nFirst, let's find out how much money John makes each week:\n\nIf he makes $2000 per week and there are 52 weeks in a year, then he makes $2000 x 52 = $104,000 per year.\n\nNow, let's add the monetary reward of $5000 and the 5% raise in salary:\n\nThe monetary reward is a one-time payment of $5000, so it will be added to John's base salary for the entire year. The raise in salary is 5%, which means his new salary will be 104,000 x 1.05 = $110,000.\n\nTherefore, John made a total of $110,000 + $5,000 = $115,000 that year.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) $114,200.
2025-12-24 16:51:28 | INFO | Q232 id=gsm8k_mcq_00231 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Kylie collects 5 more shells than Robert on Monday, who collects 20 shells. Therefore, Kylie collects 20+5 = 25 shells on Monday. On Tuesday, Kylie collects two times more shells than she did on Monday, which was 25 shells. Therefore, Kylie collects 25 x 2 = 50 shells on Tuesday. The answer is A) 50.
2025-12-24 16:51:29 | INFO | Q204 id=gsm8k_mcq_00203 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Carl consumed a total of 2 + 3 = 5 slices of cheese during the week. He used 2 slices on each sandwich for a total of 5 sandwiches * 2 slices = 10 slices of cheese. He used 3 slices per omelette for a total of 3 * 3 = 9 slices of cheese. In the macaroni and cheese dish, he used 8 slices of cheese. Therefore, Carl used a total of 10 + 9 + 8 = 27 slices of cheese during the week. The correct answer is A) 27.
2025-12-24 16:51:30 | INFO | Q234 id=gsm8k_mcq_00233 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that 36/3 = 12 penguins go inside the cave to eat their dinner. Therefore, the number of penguins still left sunbathing is 36 - 12 = 24. So the answer is B) 24.
2025-12-24 16:51:32 | INFO | Q236 id=gsm8k_mcq_00235 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, John needs to order 20 pizzas because there are 20 friends in total and he wants to ensure that each friend gets 4 slices. Since pizzas are only sold sliced into 8 portions, ordering 20 pizzas will give each person 4 slices. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 20.
2025-12-24 16:51:33 | INFO | Q206 id=gsm8k_mcq_00205 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Brinley's current average is (89 + 71 + 92 + 100 + 86) / 5 = 84. To achieve an average of 93, she needs to have a total of 5 * 93 = 465 points over the six tests. Since each test is worth 100 points, she needs to score at least 465 - 450 = 15 points on the sixth test. Therefore, the answer is A) 98.
2025-12-24 16:51:36 | INFO | Q208 id=gsm8k_mcq_00207 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total weight of the chocolate bars is 25 * 40 = 1000 grams. The total weight of the candied apples is 80 * 2 = 160 grams. The total weight of the candy is 1000 + 160 = 1160 grams. Therefore, the bag of candy weighs 1160 grams. Answer: C
2025-12-24 16:51:36 | INFO | Q238 id=gsm8k_mcq_00237 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Johnny had a total of $20 + $10 = $30 after adding his allowance and the extra $10. Since the amount he invested tripled in a year, we can assume that he earned a return of 3 * $30 = $90. Therefore, Johnny had a total of $90 + $30 = $120 after a year. The closest option from the choices provided is A) $70, but it is not the correct answer. The correct answer is B) $90.
2025-12-24 16:51:39 | INFO | Q210 id=gsm8k_mcq_00209 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total cost of buying each cup as follows:\n\nFirst, let's find out how much less twenty dozen cups cost compared to half a dozen plates:\n\n$1200 less than $6000 = $4800\n\nNow, we can divide $4800 by 20 (since there are 20 cups in a dozen) to find the cost per cup:\n\n$4800 / 20 = $240\n\nTherefore, the total cost of buying each cup is $240.\n\nSo the answer is C) 145.
2025-12-24 16:51:39 | INFO | Q240 id=gsm8k_mcq_00239 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of students who went out through exit A is 30% * 1000 = 300 students. This means that 70% of the students remained in the building. Out of the remaining students, 3/5 = 60% went out through exit B. The number of students who went out through exit B is 60% * 70% = 420 students. Therefore, the number of students who went out through exit C is 1000 - 300 - 420 = 380 students. Answer: C
2025-12-24 16:51:43 | INFO | Q242 id=gsm8k_mcq_00241 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Dolly and Pandora will read a total of 3 books by the end. Each person will read 2 books (one of their own and one of the other person's), so together they will read 2 * 2 = 4 books. However, since they will be reading each other's books as well, the total number of books they will read will be 4 + 2 = 6 books. Therefore, the answer is B) 6.
2025-12-24 16:51:46 | INFO | Q244 id=gsm8k_mcq_00243 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Jason has used 15 minutes x 30 days = 450 minutes for his daily calls with his boss. He has also used an additional 300 minutes for calls to other people, so he has used a total of 450 + 300 = 750 minutes. Since each month is given 1000 minutes, Jason has 1000 - 750 = 250 minutes remaining for the rest of the month.\nTherefore, the answer is C) 250.
2025-12-24 16:51:48 | INFO | Q212 id=gsm8k_mcq_00211 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up an equation to represent the number of red and white chickens that Jerry has.\nLet R be the number of red chickens and W be the number of white chickens. We know that:\nR + W = total number of chickens (42)\n3R + 5W = total number of eggs collected each day (42)\nWe can rearrange the second equation to get:\n3R = 42 - 5W\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get:\n3R + 5W = 42\n3(42 - 5W) + 5W = 42\n126 - 15W + 5W = 42\n126 - 10W = 42\n10W = 84\nW = 8.4\nSince W must be an integer, we cannot have 8.4 white chickens. This means that there must be either no white chickens or exactly one white chicken.\nIf there are no white chickens, then R = 42 / 3 = 14. So Jerry has 14 red chickens.\nIf there is exactly one white chicken, then R = 42 / (3 + 5) = 7. So Jerry has 7 red chickens.\nTherefore, the possible answers are A) 4 and D) 3, with the correct answer being D) 3.
2025-12-24 16:51:50 | INFO | Q214 id=gsm8k_mcq_00213 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=On the second day, Sloane counted 100 + 50 = 150 customers. On the third day, she counted 150 x 2 = 300 customers. Therefore, Sloane counted 300 customers on the third day. Answer: C
2025-12-24 16:51:50 | INFO | Q246 id=gsm8k_mcq_00245 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of snails in one aquarium = 4\nNumber of snails in another aquarium = 32\n\nThe difference between the number of snails in the two aquariums is twice the amount of fish in both aquariums. Let F be the number of fish in each aquarium. Therefore:\n\n32 - 4 = 2F\n\nSolving for F, we get:\n\n28 = 2F\nF = 14\n\nTherefore, each aquarium has 14 fish.\n\nSo the answer is A) 14.
2025-12-24 16:51:52 | INFO | Q216 id=gsm8k_mcq_00215 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total amount of money that Lori needs to earn for her purchases by adding the cost of the shoes and the belt: $320 + $32 = $352\. We can then divide this total amount by her hourly wage to determine how many hours she needs to work to earn enough money for her purchase: $352 / $8 = 44 hours.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 44.
2025-12-24 16:51:53 | INFO | Q249 id=gsm8k_mcq_00248 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The chef bought 4 bags of onions, each weighing 50 pounds. To find out how much the chef spent, we need to multiply the number of bags by the weight of each bag.\nSo, the chef bought 4 * 50 = 200 pounds of onions.\nSince a pound of onions costs $1.50, the chef spent 200 * $1.50 = $300.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 300.
2025-12-24 16:51:55 | INFO | Q218 id=gsm8k_mcq_00217 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that there are 4 roses in the vase. We also know that there are 7 more dahlias than roses in the vase. Therefore, the number of dahlias in the vase is 4 + 7 = 11.\nSo, the total number of flowers in the vase is 4 + 11 = 15.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 15.
2025-12-24 16:51:56 | INFO | Q251 id=gsm8k_mcq_00250 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of students in the school is 3 * 20 = 60 students. Since the school is 50% boys and 50% girls, there are 60 / 2 = 30 boys in the school. The first class has 15 girls, and the second class has 12 girls, so together the first two classes have 15 + 12 = 27 girls. Therefore, the third class has 30 - 27 = 3 boys. Answer: D) 7
2025-12-24 16:52:00 | INFO | Q220 id=gsm8k_mcq_00219 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that:\n\n  * Naomi scored 68 points\n  * Yuri scored 10 more than half as many points as Naomi, which means he scored 68 / 2 + 10 = 39 points\n  * Brianna scored 17 points more than Naomi, which means she scored 68 + 17 = 85 points\n\nTherefore, the total number of points scored by Naomi, Yuri, and Brianna is 68 + 39 + 85 = 282 points.\n\n  * The total number of points scored by all four students is 251 points, so Jojo scored 251 - 282 = -31 points.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 88.
2025-12-24 16:52:01 | INFO | Q253 id=gsm8k_mcq_00252 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of animals that Rick killed as follows:\n\nLast night: 10 wolves + 15 cougars = 25 animals\nToday: 3 x 15 wolves = 45 wolves (three times as many as cougars)\nToday: 3 fewer cougars than the previous night = 12 cougars (since the audio states that today Rick killed three fewer cougars than before, we subtract 3 from the previous night's count of 15 to get 12)\nTotal for today: 45 wolves + 12 cougars = 57 animals\n\nTherefore, the total number of animals that Rick killed is 57 + 25 = 82.\n\nAnswer: D) 82
