2025-12-24 16:52:11 | INFO | Q226 id=gsm8k_mcq_00225 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Andrew will take 6 days to travel by bus from New Jersey to Rochester and half as many days to travel by car from New Jersey to Rochester. Since half of 6 days is 3 days, he will take 3 days to travel by car from New Jersey to Rochester. Therefore, the total number of days he will travel if he plans to go to Rochester by bus and return from Rochester by car is 6 + 3 = 9 days. The answer is B) 9.
