2025-12-24 16:52:37 | INFO | Q241 id=gsm8k_mcq_00240 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJames = Robert + 6\nJohn = 2 * (Robert + 6)\nJohn = 2 * Robert + 12\n\nWe are given that John has 54 candies, so:\n\n2 * Robert + 12 = 54\n\nSubtracting 12 from both sides gives us:\n\n2 * Robert = 42\n\nDividing both sides by 2 gives us:\n\nRobert = 21\n\nSubstituting this value into the equation for James gives us:\n\nJames = 21 + 6 = 27\n\nTherefore, John has 27 more candies than James.\n\nAnswer: C) 27
