2025-12-24 16:53:58 | INFO | Q282 id=gsm8k_mcq_00281 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each cobra has 70 spots and each mamba has fewer spots than a cobra. Therefore, the total number of spots for the cobras is 40 _70 = 2800 spots. The total number of spots for the mambas is 60_ (70/2) = 210 spots. Altogether, the cobras and mambas have 2800 + 210 = 3010 spots. Half of this number is 3010 / 2 = 1505 spots. Therefore, the correct answer is C) 2800.
2025-12-24 16:54:02 | INFO | Q284 id=gsm8k_mcq_00283 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each necklace consists of 8 topaz gemstones, each one inch long. This means that the total length of the topaz gemstones in each necklace is 8 * 1 = 8 inches.\nThe spaces between the gemstones are filled with sterling silver beads. Each topaz gemstone is one inch long, so there are 8 - 1 = 7 inches of space between the gemstones. Since each sterling silver bead is one-quarter of an inch long, Katerina uses 7 / (1/4) = 7 * 4 = 28 sterling silver beads per necklace.\nTherefore, the answer is C) 34.
2025-12-24 16:54:03 | INFO | Q324 id=gsm8k_mcq_00323 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each ice cube cools the coffee by 13 degrees and makes the coffee 12 milliliters weaker. Therefore, when Shannon adds 15 milliliters of cream to her iced coffee that has been cooled by 65 degrees, the total amount of cooling will be 65 degrees + 15 milliliters = 80 degrees. Since each degree of cooling weakens the coffee by 1/13th of a milliliter, the coffee will become 80 degrees / 13 = 6.21 milliliters weaker. Therefore, the final volume of Shannon’s iced coffee will be 12 milliliters - 6.21 milliliters = 5.79 milliliters. Therefore, the answer is C) 80.
2025-12-24 16:54:05 | INFO | Q286 id=gsm8k_mcq_00285 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information given in the audio, Ann is 9 years old and her brother is twice her age. This means that her brother is 9 * 2 = 18 years old.\nIn three years, Ann will be 9 + 3 = 12 years old. Therefore, her brother will be 18 + 3 = 21 years old in three years.\nThe correct answer is B) 21.
2025-12-24 16:54:08 | INFO | Q288 id=gsm8k_mcq_00287 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can see that the 76-star flag has three rows of 8 stars, which makes a total of 24 stars. It also has two rows of 6 stars, which makes a total of 12 stars. The remaining stars are 5-star rows, so there must be a total of 76 - 24 - 12 = 30 five-star rows on the flag. Therefore, the answer to the question is C) 30.
2025-12-24 16:54:09 | INFO | Q326 id=gsm8k_mcq_00325 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total amount of money the company pays to all the programmers per month as follows:\n\n  * The number of junior programmers is 2/5 of the total number of employees, which means there are 2/5*100 = 40 junior programmers.\n  * Each junior programmer is paid $2000 per month, so the total amount of money paid to the junior programmers is 40*$2000 = $80000.\n  * Senior programmers are paid $400 more than junior programmers, so each senior programmer is paid $2000+$400 = $2400 per month. Since there are 100-40 = 60 senior programmers, the total amount of money paid to the senior programmers is 60*$2400 = $144000.\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money the company pays to all the programmers per month is $80000 + $144000 = $224000. The correct answer is C).
2025-12-24 16:54:13 | INFO | Q290 id=gsm8k_mcq_00289 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The cars travel different distances at different speeds, so we cannot directly compare their times. However, we can use the relative speeds and distances to estimate the time ratio they would take to travel 480 miles.\nLet's assume that the car in the slow lane takes t hours to travel 480 miles. Since the car in the fast lane is traveling at twice the speed of the car in the slow lane, it will take half the time to travel the same distance. Therefore, the car in the fast lane will take t/2 hours to travel 480 miles.\nSince the total distance traveled by both cars is the same, we can write:\n60t = 1/2 * 30t\nSolving for t, we get:\nt = 8 hours\nTherefore, the car in the slow lane took 8 hours to travel 480 miles.\nAnswer: D) 8
2025-12-24 16:54:14 | INFO | Q328 id=gsm8k_mcq_00327 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Oscar starts with 24 lollipops and eats 2 on his way to school, so he has 24 - 2 = 22 lollipops left. He then gives away 14, so he has 22 - 14 = 8 lollipops left. He buys twice as many lollipops on his way home as he gave to his friends, which is 14 * 2 = 28 lollipops. He eats 3 more that night and 2 more in the morning, so he has 8 + 28 + 3 + 2 = 39 lollipops. Therefore, Oscar has 39 lollipops. The answer is A) 32.
2025-12-24 16:54:15 | INFO | Q292 id=gsm8k_mcq_00291 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each adult gets 6 chocolate bars, which leaves 8 - 6 = 2 chocolate bars for the children to share equally. Therefore, each child will get 2 / 8 = 0.25 chocolate bars, which is closest to option C (2).\nTherefore, the answer is C) 2.
2025-12-24 16:54:17 | INFO | Q331 id=gsm8k_mcq_00330 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The customer received $80 in rewards from their previous shopping trip. They spent $43 on this shopping trip, so they will receive $80 - $43 = $37 in rewards for this trip. The coupon took twice the amount of rewards off the price, so it took $37 * 2 = $74 off the price. Thus, the customer paid $80 - $74 = $6 on this shopping trip. The correct answer is D) 6.
