2025-12-24 16:58:53 | INFO | Q509 id=gsm8k_mcq_00508 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The farm has 30 cows and the zoo has 20 sheep. The zoo has twice as many cows as the farm does, so the zoo has 30 * 2 = 60 cows. The farm has half as many sheep as the zoo does, so the farm has 20 / 2 = 10 sheep. Therefore, the total number of animals on the farm and in the zoo is 30 + 60 + 10 = 100. So the answer is A) 120.
