2025-12-24 16:58:58 | INFO | Q440 id=gsm8k_mcq_00439 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The distance from Bernadette's apartment to the theater is four times the distance from Wayne's hotel to the theater. Since it takes Wayne four minutes to be driven to the theater, it would take him 4 * 4 = 16 minutes to drive from his hotel to the theater. Therefore, Bernadette would need to leave 16 - 5 = 11 minutes before Wayne to get to the theater first. So the answer is B) 11.
2025-12-24 16:59:01 | INFO | Q442 id=gsm8k_mcq_00441 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of beads that each sister has as follows:\n\nElizabeth has 1 + 2 = 3 packs of beads\nMargareth has 3 + 4 = 7 packs of beads\n\nTherefore, Margareth has 7 - 3 = 4 more packs of beads than Elizabeth.\n\nSince each pack of beads contains 20 pieces of beads, Margareth has 4 x 20 = 80 more beads than Elizabeth.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 80.
2025-12-24 16:59:03 | INFO | Q515 id=gsm8k_mcq_00514 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the equation: H + L = $120,000 Where H represents the cost of the house and L represents the cost of the lot.\nWe are given that the house costs three times as much as the lot, so we can write: H = 3L\nSubstituting this into the original equation, we get: 3L + L = $120,000 Combining like terms, we get: 4L = $120,000 Dividing both sides by 4, we get: L = $30,000\nTherefore, the cost of the house is 3 times the cost of the lot, which means the house cost $3 * $30,000 = $90,000. The correct answer is A) $90,000.
2025-12-24 16:59:06 | INFO | Q444 id=gsm8k_mcq_00443 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that James' time for the swim was 40 minutes / 1.1 = 36.7 minutes faster than Jon's time. Since James took 5 minutes longer on the bike, his total time for the bike ride was 60 + 5 = 65 minutes. Therefore, his total time for the triathlon was 65 + 36.7 + 50 = 151.7 minutes. If Jon won by 10 minutes, then his time for the run was 151.7 - 10 = 141.7 minutes. So, it took James 141.7 minutes to do the run. The answer is A) 59.
2025-12-24 16:59:06 | INFO | Q517 id=gsm8k_mcq_00516 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total number of punches that Joe threw as follows:\n\nEach round of the fight lasts 3 minutes, so there are a total of 5 rounds * 3 minutes = 15 minutes of fighting time.\n\nOn average, Joe throws 25 punches per minute, so during the entire fight he would throw:\n\n25 punches/minute x 15 minutes = 375 punches\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 375.\n\nSecond-round QA response: Yes, I am sure about my answer.
2025-12-24 16:59:10 | INFO | Q519 id=gsm8k_mcq_00518 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate Ali's total amount of money as follows:\n\n4 x $10 = $40\n6 x $20 = $120\n\nTherefore, Ali has a total of $40 + $120 = $160.\n\n半价给他姐姐，所以他有$160 * 1/2 = $80\n\n然后他用三五分之二的钱吃饭，所以他用$80 * 3/5 = $48\n\n所以他在吃完饭后还剩下$80 - $48 = $32\n\n答案是A。
2025-12-24 16:59:11 | INFO | Q446 id=gsm8k_mcq_00445 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the cost of the hay as follows:\n\nFor every mile the horse runs, he eats 1/2 a bail of hay. Since the horse runs for 30 minutes at 32MPH, which is approximately 15 miles, he will eat 15/2 = 7.5 bales of hay.\n\nA bail of hay costs $3, so the total cost of the hay will be 7.5 * 3 = $22.5.\n\nMichael has six 5-dollar bills, so he will have 6 * 5 = $30 after buying the hay.\n\nTherefore, Michael will have $30 - $22.5 = $7.5 left over after buying the hay.\n\nThe answer is C) $4.
