2025-12-24 16:59:32 | INFO | Q533 id=gsm8k_mcq_00532 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation for the age of Jame's cousin in 8 years:\n\nIn 8 years, Jame's cousin will be 5 years younger than twice Jame's current age + 8 = 27 + 8 = 35.\n\nSolving for the current age of Jame's cousin, we get:\n\nJame's cousin's current age = 35 - 5 = 30\n\nSubstituting this value into the equation for Jame's age in 5 years, we get:\n\nJame's age in 5 years = 27 + 5 = 32\n\nTherefore, the current age difference between Jame and his cousin is:\n\n35 - 32 = 3 years\n\nSo the answer is A) 3.
