2025-12-24 17:00:36 | INFO | Q574 id=gsm8k_mcq_00573 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=After two years, Katina will have removed $2400 from her savings account because $100 x 24 = $2400. Therefore, there will be $3000 - $2400 = $600 remaining in her account after two years. The answer is C.
