2025-12-24 17:01:05 | INFO | Q520 id=gsm8k_mcq_00519 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the equation as follows:\n\nRoyce time = Double Rob time + 40 minutes\n\nSubstituting Rob's time of 2 hours (which is 120 minutes), we get:\n\nRoyce time = 2 * 120 + 40\nRoyce time = 240 + 40\nRoyce time = 280\n\nTherefore, Royce takes 280 minutes to shingle a house.\n\nAnswer: A) 280
2025-12-24 17:01:07 | INFO | Q595 id=gsm8k_mcq_00594 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that John gets 3 grams of protein per mushroom. Since he eats 200 grams of mushrooms every day, he would get 200 grams of protein per day. Therefore, over the course of a week (7 days), John would get 200 grams of protein x 7 days = 1400 grams of protein per week. The closest option from the choices provided is A) 420, which is incorrect. The correct answer is C) 210.
2025-12-24 17:01:07 | INFO | Q522 id=gsm8k_mcq_00521 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=On Tuesday, Chris completes 3 * 12 = 36 math problems. On Wednesday, he completes 100 - 12 - 36 = 52 / 4 = 13 problems. So, on Thursday, Chris has 52 - 13 = 39 math problems left to complete. The answer is B.
2025-12-24 17:01:12 | INFO | Q524 id=gsm8k_mcq_00523 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The bakers at the Beverly Hills Bakery baked 200 loaves of bread on Monday morning. They sold 93 loaves in the morning and 39 loaves in the afternoon. A grocery store returned 6 unsold loaves. To find out how many loaves of bread they had left, we need to subtract the number of loaves that were sold from the total number of loaves that were baked.\nSo, the total number of loaves baked - the number of loaves sold = the number of loaves left.\nWe can calculate this as follows:\n200 - 93 - 39 = 68\nTherefore, the bakers at the Beverly Hills Bakery had 68 loaves of bread left.\nAnswer: C) 68
2025-12-24 17:01:12 | INFO | Q597 id=gsm8k_mcq_00596 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total cost of the dental work as follows:\n\nBase price of each implant: $2000\nExtra cost for porcelain crown: $500\nTotal cost per implant including crown: $2000 + $500 = $2500\n\nSince George has already put down a deposit of $600, he needs to come up with an additional amount of $2500 - $600 = $1900.\n\nTo determine how many hours he needs to work to earn this amount, we can divide the total amount needed by his hourly rate of $15:\n\n$1900 / $15 per hour = 127 hours\n\nTherefore, George needs to work 127 hours before he has enough money to pay for the dental work.\n\nAnswer: C) 260
