2025-12-24 17:01:26 | INFO | Q532 id=gsm8k_mcq_00531 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=After the first stop, there are 48 - 8 = 40 people left on the bus. 5 times as many people as the number who got off from the bus, which is 8, get into the bus, so 5 * 8 = 40 more people get on. This means that there are now 40 + 8 = 48 people on the bus. At the second stop, 21 passengers get off, leaving 48 - 21 = 27 people on the bus. 3 times fewer passengers get on than the number who got off, which is 21, so 3 * 21 = 63 fewer people get on. This means that 27 - 63 = -36 people get on the bus. However, since it is not possible for the number of people on the bus to be negative, this answer is incorrect. Is there something I am missing or misunderstanding?
