2025-12-24 17:01:30 | INFO | Q607 id=gsm8k_mcq_00606 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Jeremy's car drives 400 miles / 2 miles = 200 times per month. Therefore, the tires rotate 200 times x 725 rotations = 145,000 times per month. To find out how many years before the tire needs to be replaced, we divide 145,000 rotations x 12 months = 1,728,000 rotations by 10,440,000 rotations per year. This gives us approximately 16.8 years before the tire needs to be replaced. Therefore, the answer is closest to choice B) 6.
2025-12-24 17:01:32 | INFO | Q534 id=gsm8k_mcq_00533 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\n2400 = 1100 + 2x + y\n\nWhere x represents the cost of the computer and y represents the cost of the printer.\n\nWe also know that y = x - 400, so we can substitute that into the equation above:\n\n2400 = 1100 + 2x + (2x - 400)\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\n2400 = 1100 + 4x - 400\n\nAdding 400 to both sides, we get:\n\n2800 = 4x\n\nDividing both sides by 4, we get:\n\n700 = x\n\nTherefore, the cost of the computer is $700. Substituting that value back into the equation for y, we get:\n\ny = 700 - 400 = 300\n\nSo the cost of one monitor is $300. Therefore, the answer is A) 300.
