2025-12-24 17:01:44 | INFO | Q542 id=gsm8k_mcq_00541 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Elvis wants to save twice as much daily in the second half of the month as he saves in the first half in order to hit his target of $1125. Since there are 30 days in a month, we can divide the total savings target by the number of days in the month to get the daily savings target: $1125 / 30 days = $38 daily.\nTherefore, Elvis has to save $38 for each day in the second half of the month in order to hit his target. The closest option among the choices provided is A) $75, which is half of $38. Therefore, the answer is A) $75.
