2025-12-24 17:01:48 | INFO | Q619 id=gsm8k_mcq_00618 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of seats in the school auditorium as follows:\n\nThere are 4 rows of seats and each row has 18 seats, so there are a total of 4 * 18 = 72 seats in the auditorium.\n\nOne-fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators, which is 72 * (1/4) = 18 seats.\n\nSo, the number of seats remaining is 72 - 18 = 54 seats.\n\nOne-third of the remaining seats were occupied by the parents, which is 54 * (1/3) = 18 seats.\n\nTherefore, the number of students who occupied the remaining seats is 54 - 18 = 36 students.\n\nHence, the answer to the question is option D: 36.
