2025-12-24 17:02:12 | INFO | Q633 id=gsm8k_mcq_00632 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Max bought 16 snowflake stamps, 3 more truck stamps than snowflake stamps, which equals 16 + 3 = 19 truck stamps. He also bought 9 fewer rose stamps than truck stamps, which equals 19 - 9 = 10 rose stamps. Therefore, Max bought a total of 16 + 19 + 10 = 45 stamps at the post office. The answer is C) 45.
2025-12-24 17:02:16 | INFO | Q564 id=gsm8k_mcq_00563 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the cost of candles can be calculated as follows:\n\nOne son is 12 years old, so he needs 12 candles.\nThe other son is 4 years younger, so he needs 12 - 4 = 8 candles.\n\nTherefore, James needs a total of 12 + 8 = 20 candles.\n\nSince a pack of 5 candles costs $3, the total cost of 20 candles would be 20 / 5 * 3 = $12.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) $12.\n\nJames spends $12 on candles.
