2025-12-24 17:03:04 | INFO | Q662 id=gsm8k_mcq_00661 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total cost of everything can be calculated as follows:\n\nThe normal brand of coffee costs $5 per pound, and Roger needs to buy a week's worth of coffee which is equal to 7 days * 1 pound of coffee per day = 7 pounds of coffee. Therefore, the cost of the normal brand of coffee will be 7 pounds * $5/pound = $35.\n\nRoger also has to buy a more expensive brand of coffee that costs 20% more than the normal brand. To find the cost of this brand, we need to calculate 20% of $35, which is 20% * $35 = $7. So the cost of the more expensive brand of coffee will be $35 + $7 = $42.\n\nFinally, Roger decides to buy a donut for $2. Adding up all these costs, we get:\n\n$35 + $42 + $2 = $79\n\nTherefore, the total cost of everything is $79. The closest choice from the options provided is A) $44, so the final answer is A).
