2025-12-24 17:03:35 | INFO | Q604 id=gsm8k_mcq_00603 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Ruiz makes 120 pounds of chocolates in two hours, which means he makes 120 pounds / 2 hours = 60 pounds per hour.\nMarissa makes three-fourths as many pounds of chocolates in an hour as Ruiz does in two hours, which means she makes 3/4 * 60 pounds = 45 pounds per hour.\nIf they both work for 12 hours in a day, then Ruiz will make 60 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 720 pounds.\nMarissa will also make 45 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 540 pounds.\nTherefore, the total amount of chocolate pounds they made together is 720 pounds + 540 pounds = 1260 pounds.\nThe answer is D) 1260.
