2025-12-24 17:04:24 | INFO | Q634 id=gsm8k_mcq_00633 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that the relative speed difference between Bob and Tom is 5 mph (70 - 55 = 5). To find how long it will take for Tom to catch up with Bob, we can divide the distance between them by their relative speed difference. The distance between Bob and Tom is 75 miles, so it will take him 75 / 5 = 15 hours to catch up with Bob.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 5.
