2025-12-24 17:04:33 | INFO | Q640 id=gsm8k_mcq_00639 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=It would take Bob approximately 72 seconds to dig the hole. To calculate this, we need to determine the volume of earth that needs to be dug. The volume of a rectangular prism is length x width x height. In this case, the length is 6 feet, the width is 4 feet, and the height is 3 feet. So the volume of the earth that needs to be dug is 6 ft x 4 ft x 3 ft = 72 cubic feet. Since it takes him 3 seconds to shovel a cubic foot of earth, it will take him 72 seconds to dig the hole. Therefore, the answer is B) 72.
