2025-12-24 17:05:48 | INFO | Q772 id=gsm8k_mcq_00771 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Bennett makes $60 from selling 20 eggplants at $3 each, so he needs to make $75 more to reach a total of $135. Since he also has 25 ears of corn that he can sell, let's assume he sells each ear of corn for $x.\nTo make a total of $75, he will need to sell 75 / x ears of corn. We can rearrange this equation to find the value of x:\n75 / x = 75 - 60\n75 / x = 15\nx = 5\nTherefore, Bennett should sell each ear of corn for $5.\nAnswer: C) 5.4
