2025-12-24 17:07:55 | INFO | Q753 id=gsm8k_mcq_00752 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, each roommate will pay $100 per month for electricity. Since there are four roommates, the total cost of electricity for the year will be $100 x 12 = $1200. If the cost is divided equally among the four roommates, then each roommate will pay $1200 / 4 = $300 per year for electricity.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 300.
2025-12-24 17:07:58 | INFO | Q837 id=gsm8k_mcq_00836 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJada = 2x\nRory = x + 20\nKora = x\n\nGiven that Kora made 20 clay dishes, we can substitute x with 20 into the equation for Kora to get:\n\nKora = 20\n\nSubstituting this value into the equation for Rory gives:\n\nRory = 20 + 20 = 40\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the equation for Jada gives:\n\nJada = 2(20) = 40\n\nTherefore, the total number of clay dishes that Jada, Rory, and Kora make together is:\n\n40 + 40 + 20 = 100\n\nThe answer is A) 100.
2025-12-24 17:08:01 | INFO | Q755 id=gsm8k_mcq_00754 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Lorraine starts with 30 small stickers and 40 large stickers. She trades 90% of her small stickers for large buttons, which is equal to 90/100 * 30 = 27 small stickers. She then has 30 - 27 = 3 small stickers left. She also trades 50% of her large stickers for large buttons, which is equal to 50/100 * 40 = 20 large stickers. She then has 40 - 20 = 20 large stickers left. Finally, she trades the rest of her large stickers for small buttons, which is equal to 20 - (40 - 20) = 20 - 20 = 0 large stickers. Therefore, by the end of the trade, Lorraine has 3 + 20 = 23 buttons. The answer is not among the choices provided, but the closest choice is C) 23.
