2025-12-24 17:08:08 | INFO | Q759 id=gsm8k_mcq_00758 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the bag has a 5% discount if it is marked $140. To find out how much you will pay after the discount, we need to calculate 5% of $140.\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\nDiscount = Original Price x Percentage/100\nPlugging in the values given in the question, we get:\nDiscount = $140 x 5/100\nDiscount = $7\nSo the bag will be discounted by $7, bringing the new price down to $140 - $7 = $133.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 133.
