2025-12-24 17:08:37 | INFO | Q865 id=gsm8k_mcq_00864 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of burritos ordered by George is 600, and he ate 20 of them, so he gave 600 - 20 = 580 burritos to the students. Since each student received 10 burritos, there were a total of 50 * 10 = 500 burritos given to all the students. The total number of leftover burritos is 580 - 500 = 80.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 80.
2025-12-24 17:08:43 | INFO | Q781 id=gsm8k_mcq_00780 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate Ava and Emma's scores as follows:\n\nAva's score = 10 * number of enemies + 5 * number of berries + 30 * (level time - actual time)\nEmma's score = 10 * number of enemies + 5 * number of berries + 30 * (level time - actual time)\n\nSince Ava jumps on 8 more enemies than Emma and collects 3 more berries, we can assume that she will have a higher score than Emma. However, if Ava finishes the level 4 seconds slower than Emma, then Emma's score will be higher because the bonus points for completing the level within the time limit will be greater for Emma.\n\nTherefore, the difference between their two scores will be:\n\nAva's score - Emma's score = (number of enemies + berries + bonus points for completing the level within time limit) - (number of enemies + berries + bonus points for completing the level within time limit)\n\nWithout knowing the specific values of the number of enemies, berries, and bonus points for each level, it is not possible to determine the exact difference between their two scores. Therefore, the answer cannot be determined with the given information.
2025-12-24 17:08:44 | INFO | Q867 id=gsm8k_mcq_00866 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nS + A + F = 85\nS = A + 25\nA = F - 12\n\nSubstituting the second and third equations into the first equation, we get:\n\nA + F + (A + 25 + F - 12) = 85\nS + A + F = 85\nA + F = 73\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the fourth equation, we get:\n\nA + F = 73\nA = F - 12\nF = A + 12\n\nSubstituting the value of F back into the equation for A, we get:\n\nA = (A + 12) - 12\nA = A\nThis equation is true, but it doesn't give us any useful information about the number of books that Fawn has.\n\nTherefore, I cannot be sure about the correctness of the answer. It could be A) 41, B) 12, C) 28, or D) 16, as none of these choices contradict the given information.
