2025-12-24 17:09:43 | INFO | Q902 id=gsm8k_mcq_00901 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of bowls of soup that can be made is 4 adult bowls + 8 child bowls = 12 bowls. Since there are 5 people in total (Calvin, his adult wife, and their two children), each person will be able to have 12 bowls / 5 people = 2.4 bowls of soup per person. Since we cannot eat fractional amounts of soup, each child will be able to have 2 bowls of soup for lunch from the leftover soup. Therefore, the answer is C) 2.
2025-12-24 17:09:43 | INFO | Q818 id=gsm8k_mcq_00817 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Paul already has 8 chocolate cupcakes and 40 toffee cupcakes, so he needs to buy 63 - 8 - 40 = 55 more cupcakes. Therefore, the answer is A) 15.
2025-12-24 17:09:47 | INFO | Q820 id=gsm8k_mcq_00819 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\n$50,000 + x_1 * 20 = 175,000$\n\nWhere $x_1$ represents the amount of money raised by each student.\n\nSolving for $x_1$, we get:\n\n$x_1 = (175,000 - 50,000) / 20 = 6,250$\n\nTherefore, each student raised $6,250.\n\nAnswer: C) 6,250
2025-12-24 17:09:47 | INFO | Q904 id=gsm8k_mcq_00903 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=To find out how much material Jo would need to make 20 small and 8 large masks, we need to calculate the amount of material needed for each type of mask separately and then add them together.\nFor the small masks, Jo can use 2 yards of material per mask, so she would need 20 * 2 = 40 yards of material.\nFor the large masks, Jo can use 2.25 yards of material per mask, so she would need 8 * 2.25 = 18 yards of material.\nTherefore, Jo would need a total of 40 + 18 = 58 yards of material to make 20 small and 8 large masks for her class.\nSo the answer is B) 28.
2025-12-24 17:09:49 | INFO | Q906 id=gsm8k_mcq_00905 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Harold works two hours less than he sleeps, which means he works for 10 - 2 = 8 hours. Additionally, he walks his dog for an hour each day. Therefore, Harold has 24 - 8 - 1 = 17 hours of free time in his day. The answer is C.
2025-12-24 17:09:51 | INFO | Q908 id=gsm8k_mcq_00907 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Joseph had 9 x 2 = 18 books. However, he lost 2 of them, so he currently has 18 - 2 = 16 books. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 16.
2025-12-24 17:09:52 | INFO | Q822 id=gsm8k_mcq_00821 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total number of cars Hunter counted during lunch break can be calculated as follows:\n\n- He counted 50 cars when entering class one morning\n- During the first break, he counted 20 more cars, so there were now 50 + 20 = 70 cars in the parking lot\n- When he got out of class for the lunch break, he realized that half the number of cars in the parking lot had gone. Since half the total number of cars is 70 / 2 = 35, then the number of cars that had gone was 35\n- Therefore, the total number of cars Hunter counted during lunch break is the remaining number of cars, which is 70 - 35 = 35\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 35.\n\nHence, the total number of cars Hunter counted during lunch break is 35.
2025-12-24 17:09:56 | INFO | Q824 id=gsm8k_mcq_00823 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total number of points that Sasha scored during both games can be calculated as follows:\n\nIn the first game, Sasha scored 14 points.\nIn the second game, Julie's home court gave her an advantage, and she scored more points than Sasha did in the first game. Specifically, Julie scored four fewer points than Sasha in the first game, which means she scored 14 - 4 = 10 points in the second game. Therefore, the total number of points that Sasha scored in both games is 14 + 10 = 24.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is not among the options provided.
2025-12-24 17:09:57 | INFO | Q910 id=gsm8k_mcq_00909 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nDuncan's current age = Adam's current age + 8\n\nWe also know that eight years ago, Duncan's age was two times Adam's age four years ago. We can use this information to write another equation:\n\nDuncan's age 8 years ago = 2 * (Adam's age 4 years ago) = 2 * 4 = 8\n\nSubstituting the value of Duncan's current age into the first equation, we get:\n\n60 = Adam's current age + 8\n\nSolving for Adam's current age, we get:\n\nAdam's current age = 52\n\nFinally, we can use the information that Adam's age four years ago was 4 to find his current age:\n\nAdam's current age = 4 + 4 = 8\n\nTherefore, Adam will be 8 years older than he is now in 8 years.\n\nAnswer: C) 42
2025-12-24 17:10:00 | INFO | Q912 id=gsm8k_mcq_00911 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Colby earns $0.20 for every package he completes. If he completes 10 less than 50 packages per hour, let's assume he completes 40 packages per hour. In a typical eight-hour workday, he would complete 320 packages. Therefore, he would earn $0.20 x 320 = $64 in a typical eight-hour workday. So the correct answer is B) 64.
2025-12-24 17:10:05 | INFO | Q826 id=gsm8k_mcq_00825 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nBecca = 12 + X\nSmendrick = 3 * (PJ)\nTotal = Becca + Smendrick + PJ\n\nSubstituting the values for each variable into the equation above, we get:\n\nTotal = 12 + 3 * (PJ) + PJ\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get:\n\nTotal = 12 + 3 * (2 * PJ) = 12 + 6 * PJ\n\nSince there is a total of 341 cards, we can set the equation equal to 341:\n\n12 + 6 * PJ = 341\n\nMultiplying both sides by 2, we get:\n\n24 + 12 * PJ = 682\n\nSubtracting 24 from both sides, we get:\n\n12 * PJ = 658\n\nDividing both sides by 12, we get:\n\nPJ = 54.83\n\nSincePJ must be an integer, we can round down to get:\n\nPJ = 54\n\nSubstituting this value back into the equation for Smendrick, we get:\n\nSmendrick = 3 * 54 = 162\n\nFinally, substituting these values back into the equation for Becca, we get:\n\nBecca = 12 + 54 = 66\n\nTherefore, Becca has 66 magic cards.\n\nAnswer: C) 153
2025-12-24 17:10:07 | INFO | Q914 id=gsm8k_mcq_00913 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Benny threw 58 pieces of bologna in total at the balloons, and he threw two pieces of bologna at each red balloon and three pieces of bologna at each yellow balloon. We also know that twenty of the balloons were red.\nTo find out how many of the balloons were yellow, we can set up an equation using the total number of bologna thrown and the number of red balloons. Let X be the number of yellow balloons. We can write:\n2 * 20 + 3 * (58 - 20) = 58\nSimplifying this equation gives us:\n40 + 3 * 38 = 58\n40 + 114 = 154\nTherefore, there were 154 pieces of bologna thrown in total, and 114 of those were thrown at yellow balloons. This means that there were 154 - 114 = 40 red balloons. And since Benny threw two pieces of bologna at each red balloon, there must have been 40 / 2 = 20 red balloons in the bundle. Therefore, the answer is A) 38.
2025-12-24 17:10:10 | INFO | Q916 id=gsm8k_mcq_00915 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Bruce works for 5 hours on Tuesday. On Wednesday, he works twice as much as he works on Tuesday, which means he works for 5 * 2 = 10 hours on Wednesday. On Thursday, he works 2 hours less than the time he works on Wednesday, which means he works for 10 - 2 = 8 hours on Thursday. Therefore, in all three days, Bruce works for 5 + 10 + 8 = 23 hours. The answer is A) 23.
2025-12-24 17:10:10 | INFO | Q828 id=gsm8k_mcq_00827 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, the cost of shipping the book would be calculated as follows:\n\n  * The book weighs 4 pounds, so the shipping cost would be 4 * $0.35 = $1.40\n  * The book needs to be shipped 20 miles, so the additional cost would be 20 * $0.08 = $1.60\n\nThe total cost of shipping would therefore be $1.40 + $1.60 = $3.\n\nIf Amazon only refunds 75% of the book's purchase price, then Milly would lose 25% of the purchase price. Since the book cost $32, Milly would lose 25% of $32, which equals $8.\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money that Milly would lose is $8 for the loss on the book and $3 for the shipping costs, for a total loss of $11.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 11.
2025-12-24 17:10:14 | INFO | Q918 id=gsm8k_mcq_00917 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of fruits that Kira bought as follows:\n\n3 apples + 5 bananas + 6 oranges = 14 pieces of fruit\n\nSince Lola ate 2 pieces of fruit, the number of pieces of fruit left would be:\n\n14 - 2 = 12 pieces of fruit\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 12.\n\nSecond-round QA response: The correct answer is C) 12 because there are 12 pieces of fruit left after Lola ate 2 of them.
2025-12-24 17:10:16 | INFO | Q830 id=gsm8k_mcq_00829 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The information provided indicates that Boris produces 50,000 bars of chocolate each month, with the exception of his production for the first two weeks of the month. In the first week, Boris produces 8,000 bars of chocolate. In the second week, Boris produces half as many bars as the first week, which would be 8,000 / 2 = 4,000 bars of chocolate. In the third week, Boris produces three times as many bars as the first week, which would be 3 x 8,000 = 24,000 bars of chocolate. Therefore, in the fourth week, Boris would produce 50,000 - 8,000 - 4,000 - 24,000 = 7,000 bars of chocolate. The answer to the question is A) 6,000.
2025-12-24 17:10:17 | INFO | Q920 id=gsm8k_mcq_00919 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The class was able to raise $150 from the profit of selling lollipops. Each student sold 10 lollipops at $0.8 per lollypop, so each student contributed $8 towards the class fund. The class had 30 students, so the total amount raised from selling lollipops is 30 * $8 = $240. Since the lollipops were bought for $0.5 each, the class made a profit of $240 - $150 = $90. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 90.
2025-12-24 17:10:20 | INFO | Q922 id=gsm8k_mcq_00921 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Josh can eat 2 x 2 = 4 slices per day. Therefore, together, Abby and Josh can eat 2 + 4 = 6 slices per day. To find out how many days the loaf of bread will last, we divide the total number of slices by the number of slices consumed per day: 24 / 6 = 4 days. Therefore, the loaf of bread will last 4 days. Answer: C
2025-12-24 17:10:21 | INFO | Q832 id=gsm8k_mcq_00831 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the cost for Angela's installation will be $129.00 for the basic package which includes hanging four mirrors, two shelves, one chandelier, and ten pictures. She will need an additional $15.00 for each additional item, so for the six mirrors and two chandeliers she needs installed, she will pay an extra $15.00 * 8 = $120.00. For the twenty pictures, she will pay an extra $15.00 * 20 = $300.00. Therefore, the total cost for Angela's installation will be $129.00 + $120.00 + $300.00 = $459.00. The correct answer is not among the choices provided.
2025-12-24 17:10:25 | INFO | Q834 id=gsm8k_mcq_00833 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equations:\n\nNaruto can lift a mountain 10 times higher than Kagiyami who can lift a mountain 4 times higher than Saskay who can lift a mountain 12 times higher than Pompei who can lift a mountain 1 inch.\n\nSo, we can write:\nNaruto = 10 * Kagiyami\nKagiyami = 4 * Saskay\nSaskay = 12 * Pompei\nPompei = 1\n\nSubstituting the values, we get:\nNaruto = 10 * 4 * 12 * 1 = 480\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 480.\n\nSecond-round QA:\nIs there anything else you would like to add or clarify?
2025-12-24 17:10:28 | INFO | Q924 id=gsm8k_mcq_00923 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Lana divided the 27 cups of tea into three rows and created equal amounts of chamomile and mint tea cups in each row. Let's assume that there are x cups of chamomile tea and y cups of mint tea in each row.\nSince there are three rows, we can write the equation as follows:\nx + y = 27\nWe also know that the total number of cups of tea that Lana brewed is 27 cups + 15 cups = 42 cups.\nSince each row contains an equal amount of chamomile and mint tea, we can say that the total number of cups of chamomile and mint tea in all three rows is 2x + 2y = 42.\nSubstituting the value of x + y from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n2x + 2y = 42\nx + y = 21\nTherefore, each row contains 21 cups of tea, which includes 9 cups of mint tea.\nSo the answer is C) 9.\nNote: We assumed that there were equal amounts of chamomile and mint tea in each row, but the audio does not specify this explicitly. Therefore, the answer may be slightly different if the proportions of chamomile and mint tea in each row are not equal.
2025-12-24 17:10:30 | INFO | Q836 id=gsm8k_mcq_00835 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate that the speed of the kangaroos is:\n\n18 hours / 3 kangaroos = 6 hours/kangaroo\n\nSince each turtle travels at half the speed of a kangaroo, their speed would be:\n\n6 hours/kangaroo / 2 = 3 hours/turtle\n\nTherefore, it would take four turtles 3 hours × 4 = 12 hours to travel across the highway.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 12.\n\nSecond-round QA response: I'm sorry, but my previous answer was incorrect. Thank you for pointing out my mistake. After reviewing the information again, I agree that the correct answer is 12 hours.
2025-12-24 17:10:32 | INFO | Q926 id=gsm8k_mcq_00925 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that the tank contains 10000 / 2 = 5000 gallons of water. If the tank is emptied at a rate of 500 gallons per day, it will take 5000 / 500 = 10 days for the tank to be completely emptied. Therefore, after 6 days, there will be 5000 - (500 x 6) = 5000 - 3000 = 2000 gallons of water remaining in the tank. The answer is B) 2000.
2025-12-24 17:10:35 | INFO | Q928 id=gsm8k_mcq_00927 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of calories in the mini cinnamon rolls is 200 * 600 = 120000 calories. The total number of calories in the mini blueberry muffins is 300 * 450 = 135000 calories. The total number of calories in the pastries he baked is 120000 + 135000 = 255000 calories. Therefore, the answer is C) 875000.
2025-12-24 17:10:37 | INFO | Q838 id=gsm8k_mcq_00837 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total amount of money that Erika has in her purse is not explicitly stated in the given information. We only know that she has some savings in her purse, has been paid $150 for her part-time job, and her mom will give her $80 to help her buy the laptop. To find out how much money Erika has in her purse, we need to add up all the amounts of money mentioned.\nFirst, we add the $150 that Erika earned from her part-time job to her savings: $150 + $0 = $150\nNext, we add the $80 that Erika's mom will give her to her savings: $150 + $80 = $230\nFinally, we subtract the discount of $200 that Erika gets when trading in her old laptop from the price of the new laptop: $600 - $200 = $400\nTherefore, Erika needs an extra $50 to buy the laptop, so she has a total of $230 in her purse. This means that Erika has $230 - $50 = $180 left in her purse after buying the laptop. Answer: C) 220
2025-12-24 17:10:38 | INFO | Q930 id=gsm8k_mcq_00929 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the bus traveled 60 miles per hour for 5 hours, so its total distance traveled would be 60 * 5 = 300 miles. The car traveled 30 miles per hour for 8 hours, so its total distance traveled would be 30 * 8 = 240 miles. Therefore, the bus traveled 300 - 240 = 60 miles farther than the car. The answer is C: 60.
2025-12-24 17:10:40 | INFO | Q841 id=gsm8k_mcq_00840 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the total length of the glue sticks that are not used can be calculated as follows:\n\nThe first glue stick has 12 mm left, so it is not used.\n\nThe second glue stick has 2/3 * 12 = 8 mm left, so it is also not used.\n\nThe third glue stick has 1/2 * 12 = 6 mm left, so it is also not used.\n\nTherefore, the total length of the glue sticks that are not used is 12 + 8 + 6 = 26 mm.\n\nSo the answer is D) 20.
2025-12-24 17:10:44 | INFO | Q843 id=gsm8k_mcq_00842 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Thea paid $70 for the hat by giving the craftsman four $20 bills. To find out how much change she got, we need to subtract the price of the hat from the amount of money she gave the craftsman.\nSo, Thea gave the craftsman $20 x 4 = $80. Therefore, she got $80 - $70 = $10 in change.\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 10.
2025-12-24 17:10:46 | INFO | Q845 id=gsm8k_mcq_00844 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can reason that:\n\n  * Peter has twice as many socks as Jack, so Peter has 60/2=30 socks.\n  * Peter has half as many dishes as Jack, so Peter has 60/2=30 dishes.\n\nTherefore, the total number of socks and dishes that Peter has is 30+30=60.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 90.
2025-12-24 17:10:47 | INFO | Q932 id=gsm8k_mcq_00931 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\nPeter + Paul + Jean = 100\n\nWe also know that Paul is 10 years older than John, so:\n\nPaul = John + 10\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get:\n\nPeter + John + 10 + Jean = 100\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nPeter + John + Jean = 90\n\nNow we know that Peter's age is equal to the sum of Paul and John's ages. Let's call this value X.\n\nSo, X = Paul + John\n\nSubstituting the expression for Paul from the second equation, we get:\n\nX = (John + 10) + John\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\nX = 2John + 10\n\nSubtracting 10 from both sides, we get:\n\nX = 2John\n\nFinally, substituting this value for X into the equation we derived earlier, we get:\n\n2John + John + Jean = 90\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n3John = 90\n\nDividing both sides by 3, we get:\n\nJohn = 30\n\nSubstituting this value for John into the expression for Paul, we get:\n\nPaul = 30 + 10 = 40\n\nTherefore, Peter's age is:\n\nPeter = X = 2John = 2(30) = 60\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 50.\n\nTherefore, I am sure that my answer is correct.
2025-12-24 17:10:49 | INFO | Q847 id=gsm8k_mcq_00846 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, each group has a total of 10 minutes on stage (2 minutes to get on stage + 6 minutes to perform + 2 minutes to exit). This means that there are 2 hours (120 minutes) / 10 minutes per group = 12 groups that can perform in the concert.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 12.
2025-12-24 17:10:50 | INFO | Q934 id=gsm8k_mcq_00933 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, the total number of boxes of stuff that the charity group has is 10 + 10 = 20 boxes. Each table can fit 2 boxes of stuff, so the maximum number of tables they can use is 20 / 2 = 10 tables. Since they already own 15 tables, they need 10 - 15 = -5 tables. However, since it is not possible to have negative tables, the answer must be incorrect. The most likely explanation is that there is an error in the question or the calculation.
2025-12-24 17:10:51 | INFO | Q849 id=gsm8k_mcq_00848 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that:\n\n- There are 40/2 = 20 white shirts without collars.\n- There are 50 - 20 = 30 floral shirts with buttons.\n- Therefore, there are 30 - 20 = 10 more floral shirts with no buttons than white shirts with no collars.\n\nSo the answer is D) 10.
2025-12-24 17:10:56 | INFO | Q936 id=gsm8k_mcq_00935 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The Widgeteer 3000 makes 60 widgets per hour, so in a day it would make 60 x 24 = 1440 widgets. For a month with 30 days, it would make 1440 x 30 = 43200 widgets. The WidgetMaster 9000 makes 45 widgets per hour, so in a day it would make 45 x 24 = 1080 widgets. For a month with 30 days, it would make 1080 x 30 = 32400 widgets. Therefore, Fern would make 43200 - 32400 = 10800 more widgets from the Widgeteer 3000 than the WidgetMaster 9000 in a month with 30 days. So the answer is A) 2160.
2025-12-24 17:10:57 | INFO | Q851 id=gsm8k_mcq_00850 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the total number of goats before selling:\n\nTotal = Number of goats in Farm X + Number of goats in Farm Y\nTotal = 55 + 45\nTotal = 100\n\nWe also know that Mr. Smith sold 10 goats from Farm X and twice as many goats from Farm Y, which means he sold:\n\n10 * 2 = 20 goats from Farm Y\n\nSo the total number of goats remaining after selling is:\n\nTotal = Total before selling - Number of goats sold\nTotal = 100 - 10 - 20\nTotal = 70\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 70.\n\n反思：在第二轮问答中，我确认了我的答案是正确的。但是，在第一轮问答中，我没有仔细检查我的选择，并且选择了错误的答案。这提醒我在进行快速思考时要更加仔细和谨慎。
2025-12-24 17:11:00 | INFO | Q938 id=gsm8k_mcq_00937 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, each sheep needs 3 pounds less than twice the amount each goat needs. Since each goat needs 5 pounds, we can calculate that each sheep needs 5 * 2 - 3 = 7 pounds of hay. Therefore, the total amount of hay needed for the goats is 15 * 5 = 75 pounds. And the total amount of hay needed for the sheep is 12 * 7 = 84 pounds. So, the total amount of hay needed is 84 + 75 = 159 pounds. The answer is A) 159.
2025-12-24 17:11:00 | INFO | Q853 id=gsm8k_mcq_00852 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the cost of three baskets of green food is $25 x 3 = $75. The cost of three baskets of red food is $18 x 3 = $54. If you get $2 off for each basket of red food, you will receive $2 x 3 = $6 discount. Therefore, the total amount you will have to pay is $75 - $54 + $6 = $27. The answer is closest to choice A) $27.
2025-12-24 17:11:03 | INFO | Q940 id=gsm8k_mcq_00939 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can reason as follows:\n\n  * After ten rounds, Craig has spelled out 20 words with 15 letters each, for a total of 300 letters.\n  * If Craig's brother has spelled words with a total count of letters 50 more than Craig, then Craig's brother has spelled out 300 + 50 = 350 letters.\n  * Therefore, the total number of letters in the words they've spelled after the ten rounds is 300 + 350 = 650.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 650.
2025-12-24 17:11:07 | INFO | Q942 id=gsm8k_mcq_00941 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the teacher has 9 coupons that can be redeemed for 100 bottles of apple juice each. Therefore, she will have a total of 9 * 100 = 900 bottles of apple juice after redeeming all her coupons. Since the teacher gives each student 2 bottles of apple juice to drink for lunch, she will give away a total of 29 * 2 = 58 bottles of apple juice to the students. Therefore, the teacher will have 900 - 58 = 842 bottles of apple juice left for herself. Answer: C) 842
2025-12-24 17:11:09 | INFO | Q856 id=gsm8k_mcq_00855 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\n- My age = My brother's age - 3\n- My age = My sister's age + 2\n- My mom's age = 3 * My brother's age - 1\n\nWe can use these equations to find the values of each person's age.\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation gives:\n\nMy brother's age - 3 = My sister's age + 2\n\nSolving for My sister's age gives:\n\nMy sister's age = My brother's age - 5\n\nSubstituting this value into the third equation gives:\n\nMy mom's age = 3 * (My brother's age - 5) - 1\n\nSimplifying this equation gives:\n\nMy mom's age = 3 * My brother's age - 16\n\nSubstituting this value into the fourth equation gives:\n\n3 * My brother's age - 16 + My brother's age - 3 + My brother's age + 2 = 87\n\nSimplifying this equation gives:\n\n4 * My brother's age = 96\n\nDividing both sides by 4 gives:\n\nMy brother's age = 24\n\nSubstituting this value into the second equation gives:\n\nMy sister's age = 24 - 5 = 19\n\nSubstituting these values into the first equation gives:\n\nMy age = 24 - 3 = 21\n\nTherefore, I am 21 years old. Answer: D.
2025-12-24 17:11:11 | INFO | Q944 id=gsm8k_mcq_00943 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total cost of the 10 CDs is:\n\n10 * $15 = $150\n\nThe discount on each CD is 40%, so the price of each CD after the discount is:\n\n$15 - ($15 * 40%) = $12\n\nSince James does not like 5 of the CDs, he sells them for $40 each, which gives him a total revenue of:\n\n5 * $40 = $200\n\nTherefore, the total amount of money that James made from selling the CDs is:\n\n$200 - $150 = $50\n\nSo the answer is A) $50.
2025-12-24 17:11:13 | INFO | Q858 id=gsm8k_mcq_00857 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, the amount of water passing through the river at one point in time is 4000 gallons. After a day of heavy rain, the amount of water passing through the river doubles at the same point. This means that the amount of water passing through the river at that point after the rain is 2 * 4000 = 8000 gallons.\nIf the volume of water passing through the river at that point increases by 6000 gallons on the third day, the total amount of water passing through the river at that point would be 8000 + 6000 = 14000 gallons.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 14000.
2025-12-24 17:11:16 | INFO | Q860 id=gsm8k_mcq_00859 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Rafaela received 40 * $20 = $800 in tips. Since Julieta received 10% less money in tips than Rafaela, she received 800 * (1 - 10%) = $800 * 90% = $720 in tips. Therefore, together, Rafaela and Julieta received $800 + $720 = $1520 in tips. The correct answer is A) 1520.
2025-12-24 17:11:18 | INFO | Q946 id=gsm8k_mcq_00945 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the time it took James to swim 60% of the 20-mile distance:\n\n60% of 20 miles = 12 miles\n\nHe swam at a pace of 2 miles per hour, so it would take him:\n\n12 miles / 2 miles per hour = 6 hours\n\nHe rested for half as long as the swimming time, which is 6 hours / 2 = 3 hours.\n\nSo, the total time it took him to swim 60% of the distance was 6 hours + 3 hours = 9 hours.\n\nTo complete the remaining 40% of the distance, he swam at a slower speed of 2 miles per hour * 0.5 = 1 mile per hour.\n\nIt would take him:\n\n40% of 20 miles = 8 miles\n\nAt a speed of 1 mile per hour, it would take him:\n\n8 miles / 1 mile per hour = 8 hours\n\nTherefore, the total time it took James to cross the lake was:\n\n9 hours + 8 hours = 17 hours\n\n选D
2025-12-24 17:11:20 | INFO | Q862 id=gsm8k_mcq_00861 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that it takes Claire 12 months to earn one Girl Scout badge. Since琥珀（Amber）takes twice as long as Claire to earn a badge, it takes her 12 x 2 = 24 months to earn one badge. Similarly, since温蒂（Wendy）earns three times the amount of badges as Claire in the same time frame, it takes her 12 x 3 = 36 months to earn one badge. Therefore, in a 1-year time frame (12 months), Wendy earns 36 - 24 = 12 more badges than Amber. The answer is A) 12.
2025-12-24 17:11:21 | INFO | Q948 id=gsm8k_mcq_00947 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Jasmine started with 15 stickers, lost 7 during playtime, and received 5 more for helping her classmates. To find out how many stickers she has at the end, we need to add up the number of stickers she received and subtract the number she lost.\nSo, the total number of stickers Jasmine has at the end is 15 + 5 - 7 = 13.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 13.
