2025-12-24 17:11:38 | INFO | Q874 id=gsm8k_mcq_00873 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=David has $12.48 and wants to buy 16 bolts from a bin at the hardware store. Each bolt costs $0.03. To find out how much money he has left after buying the bolts, we need to calculate the total cost of the bolts.\nThe total cost of the bolts can be found by multiplying the number of bolts by their cost per bolt: 16 bolts * $0.03/bolt = $0.56\nTo find out how much money David has left, we subtract the cost of the bolts from his starting amount of cash: $12.48 - $0.56 = $12.42\nTherefore, David has $12.42 left after paying for the bolts.\nAnswer: C) 12
