2025-12-24 17:12:07 | INFO | Q973 id=gsm8k_mcq_00972 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Mrs. Harrington bought 12 boxes of oranges, which means she has a total of 12 * 20 = 240 oranges. She gave her mom and her sister each 2 boxes of oranges, which totals 2 * 20 = 40 oranges. Therefore, she kept 240 - 40 = 200 oranges. If she kept 1/4 of the oranges, then she sold 3/4 * 200 = 150 oranges. Therefore, Mrs. Harrington sold 150 oranges. The answer is A) 120.
