2025-12-24 17:12:49 | INFO | Q997 id=gsm8k_mcq_00996 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total age of four children is 20 years, so the average age of the group is 20/4 = 5 years old. Helene is twice as old as the average age of the group, which means she is 5 * 2 = 10 years old. Akbar is 3 years old and Alessandro is 4 years old, so Wilfred is 20 - 10 - 3 - 4 = 3 years old. Therefore, the age of Wilfred is C) 3.
2025-12-24 17:12:50 | INFO | Q917 id=gsm8k_mcq_00916 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount of money that Julia and Nadine received from their mother is not specified. Therefore, we cannot determine how much each of them received. The only information provided is that they combined their allowances to buy a cake, balloons, and ice cream, and spent some of the remaining money on these items. Without knowing the specific amounts that Julia and Nadine received, it is not possible to accurately determine how much their mother gave each of them. Therefore, the answer is unknown or "I don't know."
2025-12-24 17:12:52 | INFO | Q999 id=gsm8k_mcq_00998 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that the total number of cookies brought by the guests was 100 guests * 15 cookies/guest = 1500 cookies. The bride decided to give half of the cookies away, which is 1500 cookies / 2 = 750 cookies. If each person in the church next door received 15 cookies, then the number of people in the church next door would be 750 cookies / 15 cookies/person = 50 people.\nTherefore, the answer to the question is A) 50.
2025-12-24 17:12:53 | INFO | Q919 id=gsm8k_mcq_00918 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total number of students as follows:\n\nThere are 6 students playing tennis + twice that number playing volleyball = 6 + 6 * 2 = 18 students playing sports other than soccer.\n\nOut of these, 16 boys and 22 girls are playing soccer, so there are a total of 16 + 22 = 38 students playing soccer.\n\nTherefore, the total number of students participating in all three sports is 18 + 38 = 56 students.\n\nSo the answer is D) 56.
