2025-12-24 17:13:41 | INFO | Q945 id=gsm8k_mcq_00944 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount of money that Jen will earn from selling her root crops is:\n\n6 yams * $1.5 = $9\n10 sweet potatoes * $2 = $20\n4 carrots * $1.25 = $5\n\nTotal earnings = $9 + $20 + $5 = $34\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 34.\n\n反思：在第二轮问答中，我仔细检查了我的答案，并且确认了它是否与音频中的信息一致。我还提醒自己，在选择答案时要遵循要求，不能输出不确定的答案。这有助于我更好地理解和应用所学的知识。
2025-12-24 17:13:41 | INFO | Q1019 id=gsm8k_mcq_01018 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that James spends 10 minutes reading 3 pages, which means he reads 3/10 = 0.3 pages per minute. He reads 18 pages in total, so he spends 18/0.3 = 60 minutes reading. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 60.
2025-12-24 17:13:43 | INFO | Q947 id=gsm8k_mcq_00946 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The statement given is that the bakery has 40 less than seven times as many loaves of bread as Sam had last Friday. Let's call the number of loaves of bread that the bakery has x.\nWe can set up the equation as follows:\nx = 7 * 70 - 40\nSimplifying the right-hand side gives us:\nx = 490\nTherefore, the bakery has 490 loaves of bread. The answer is A.
2025-12-24 17:13:44 | INFO | Q1021 id=gsm8k_mcq_01020 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, John picks 4 bananas on Wednesday, 6 bananas on Thursday, and triple the number of bananas he picked on Wednesday, which is 3 * 4 = 12 bananas, on Friday. Therefore, the total number of bananas that John has is 4 + 6 + 12 = 22 bananas. The answer is C) 22.
2025-12-24 17:13:46 | INFO | Q1023 id=gsm8k_mcq_01022 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\n2x = 120\n\nWhere x represents the number of small stuffed animals sold.\n\nSolving for x, we get:\n\nx = 60\n\nTherefore, Teresa sold 60 small stuffed animals today.\n\nAnswer: B) 6
2025-12-24 17:13:48 | INFO | Q949 id=gsm8k_mcq_00948 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total commission that Cayley will earn from the sales of 6 copies of the New York Times and 10 copies of the Wall Street Journal can be calculated as follows:\n\nFor the New York Times:\n- He gets a 10% commission on each copy, so for 6 copies, he will earn 10/100 * 6 = $6\n\nFor the Wall Street Journal:\n- He gets an 8% commission on each copy, so for 10 copies, he will earn 8/100 * 10 = $8\n\nTherefore, the total commission that Cayley will earn from these sales is $6 + $8 = $14.\n\nHence, the correct answer is not among the options provided.
2025-12-24 17:13:48 | INFO | Q1025 id=gsm8k_mcq_01024 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Suzanne earned from selling cookies and cupcakes: 80 * $1 + 60 * $4 = $440\nShe gave her two sisters $10 each, so she spent: 2 * $10 = $20\nTherefore, she has $440 - $20 = $420 left from her earnings. The answer is A) 310.
2025-12-24 17:13:52 | INFO | Q951 id=gsm8k_mcq_00950 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Bahati scored the most points with 20 more than Azibo and 10 more than Dinar. Let's call the number of points scored by Azibo x.\nTherefore, we can set up the equation: x + 20 = 45\nWe can also add 10 to both sides to get: x + 30 = 55\nSubtracting 30 from both sides gives us: x = 25\nSo Azibo scored 25 points.\nAnswer: B) 25
2025-12-24 17:13:54 | INFO | Q1027 id=gsm8k_mcq_01026 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The statement given is that one dwarf can mine 12 pounds of ore per day with his bare hands and he can mine twice as much with an iron pickaxe and 50% more with a steel pickaxe than with an iron pickaxe. This means that with an iron pickaxe, the dwarf can mine 12 * 2 = 24 pounds of ore per day. With a steel pickaxe, the dwarf can mine 24 * 1.5 = 36 pounds of ore per day. Therefore, in total, 40 dwarves with steel pickaxes can mine 40 * 36 = 1440 pounds of ore per day. Since there are 30 days in a month, 40 dwarves with steel pickaxes can mine 1440 * 30 = 43200 pounds of ore in a month. The correct answer is B) 43200.
2025-12-24 17:13:56 | INFO | Q953 id=gsm8k_mcq_00952 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Vince stapled reports for a total of 11 hours (from 8:00 AM to 7:00 PM). Since he can staple 30 reports every 15 minutes, he will be able to staple a total of 30 * 2 = 60 reports during this time period. Therefore, the total number of reports that Vince stapled is 60 * 11 = 660. The closest choice is A) 360, which is approximately half of the total number of reports that Vince stapled. However, since the choices are given in whole numbers, the correct answer would be C) 1320, which is the next whole number greater than 660.
2025-12-24 17:13:58 | INFO | Q1029 id=gsm8k_mcq_01028 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the cost of the remaining portion of the bedroom set that Tom needs to pay for.\nThe total cost of the bedroom set is $3000, and Tom has already used $1000 to pay for part of it. So, the remaining cost of the bedroom set that he needs to pay for is $3000 - $1000 = $2000.\nTom also needs to pay 10% a month for the bedroom set, which means he needs to pay $2000 x 10% = $200 per month.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) $200.
2025-12-24 17:13:59 | INFO | Q955 id=gsm8k_mcq_00954 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given in the audio, we can calculate that Jonathan has 2 x 12 = 24 measuring cups. He gives Pedro 6 measuring spoons, so he has 24 - 6 = 18 measuring spoons remaining. Therefore, the total number of utensils Jonathan has remaining is 18 + 24 = 42. The answer is not among the choices provided, but the closest choice would be A) 26.
2025-12-24 17:14:01 | INFO | Q957 id=gsm8k_mcq_00956 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Robyn sends 7 work emails a day, which leaves 16 - 7 = 9 emails remaining. Two-thirds of these 9 emails are to family, which equals 9 * (2 / 3) = 6 emails. Therefore, Robyn sends 6 emails to her boyfriend a day.\nAnswer: A) 6
2025-12-24 17:14:04 | INFO | Q1031 id=gsm8k_mcq_01030 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the probability that Marcus will have to turn in his homework tomorrow is:\n\nIf the substitute teacher collects the homework: 50%\nIf the normal teacher gives everyone an extension: 40%\nIf Marcus convinces the teacher his dog ate his assignment and gets a personal extension: 20%\n\nTo calculate the overall probability, we need to add up these probabilities:\n\n50% + 40% + 20% = 110%\n\nTherefore, the percentage chance that Marcus will actually have to turn in his homework tomorrow is 110%, which is closest to choice A) 76.\n\nHowever, it's important to note that this calculation assumes that all three events (substitute teacher collecting homework, normal teacher giving extensions, and Marcus convincing the teacher for a personal extension) are independent and occur with equal likelihood. In reality, these events may be influenced by various factors such as the teacher's personality, the class dynamics, and other external circumstances. Therefore, the actual probability may differ from the calculated value.
2025-12-24 17:14:05 | INFO | Q959 id=gsm8k_mcq_00958 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can reason as follows:\n\n  * Kelly said that Courtney overstated the number of people in attendance by 20%.\n  * If Kelly was right, then the actual number of people in attendance should be 48 - 20% = 48 - 0.2 = 48 - 2 = 46.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 58.\n\nHowever, I agree with your second-round QA. The answer provided does not match the information given in the question. It is possible that there is an error in the question or the answer choices provided.
