2025-12-24 17:14:14 | INFO | Q966 id=gsm8k_mcq_00965 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The total distance that the bird travels is 10 hours * 30 miles per hour = 300 miles. The bird then flies 2 hours * 18 miles per hour = 36 miles towards the north. Finally, the bird flies 5 hours * 22 miles per hour = 110 miles towards the south. The total distance traveled from the northern home to the southern home is 300 + 36 + 110 = 446 miles. Therefore, the answer is B) 446.
2025-12-24 17:14:18 | INFO | Q968 id=gsm8k_mcq_00967 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total age of Nani, his brother, and his sister can be calculated as follows:\n\nNani = 8 years old\nBrother = 2 * 8 = 16 years old\nSister = 8 - 25% = 8 - 0.25 = 7.75 years old\n\nAdding up their ages gives us:\n\n8 + 16 + 7.75 = 31.75 years\n\nTherefore, the total age of all three family members is 31.75 years. The closest option from the choices provided is A) 26.\n\nHence, the final answer is A) 26.
2025-12-24 17:14:22 | INFO | Q970 id=gsm8k_mcq_00969 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the cost of each phone as follows:\n\n- The first two phones will cost full price, which is $600 each.\n- After that, each phone costs half price.\n\nTherefore, the cost of the next two phones would be $600 / 2 = $300 each.\nThe cost of the final two phones would also be $300 each.\n\nSo, the total cost of all four phones would be $600 + $600 + $300 + $300 = $1800.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) $1800.
