2025-12-24 17:14:33 | INFO | Q978 id=gsm8k_mcq_00977 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, Pamela will be outside for a total of 4 hours x 8 days = 32 hours. She applies sunscreen every hour, so she will use 32 hours / hour = 32 ounces of sunscreen. Each bottle contains 8 ounces of sunscreen, so she will need 32 / 8 = 4 bottles of sunscreen.\nTherefore, the answer is C) 4.
