2025-12-24 17:14:43 | INFO | Q1048 id=gsm8k_mcq_01047 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can reason that Rory retrieved 19 tennis balls in all sets combined. In the first set, he had to retrieve four more balls than in the second set, which means he retrieved 21 tennis balls in the first set. In the third set, he retrieved half as many balls as in the second set, which means he retrieved 10 tennis balls in the third set. Therefore, the total number of tennis balls Rory retrieved in the first set is 21. The answer is A) 3.
