2025-12-24 17:15:22 | INFO | Q1006 id=gsm8k_mcq_01005 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of porcupines in the park is 50, and the number of female porcupines is 3/5 of the total population. This means that there are 3/5 * 50 = 30 female porcupines in the park.\nIf each female porcupine gives birth to four babies every month, then the total number of babies born per month is 30 * 4 = 120.\nAfter a year (12 months), the total number of babies born will be 120 * 12 = 1440.\nTherefore, there will be 50 + 1440 = 1490 porcupines in the park after a year.\nAnswer: A) 1490
2025-12-24 17:15:23 | INFO | Q1074 id=gsm8k_mcq_01073 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The third monkey eats 19 bananas each day because the total number of bananas bought by Mr. Robles is 315, which is enough to feed his three monkeys for a week. One monkey eats 10 bananas each day, so the second monkey eats 10 + 4 = 14 bananas each day. Since there are three monkeys, the third monkey gets the remaining 315 - 10 - 14 - 14 = 19 bananas each day. Therefore, the answer is C) 35.
