2025-12-24 17:15:54 | INFO | Q1090 id=gsm8k_mcq_01089 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the ball will go up to two-thirds of its starting height on its second bounce. Since the starting height is not specified, we can assume it to be some unit of length, say meters. Let's call this height h.\nOn the first bounce, the ball goes up to two-thirds of h, which is 2/3 * h = h/3.\nAfter the first bounce, the ball has gained height, so its new height on the second bounce will be h + h/3 = 4/3 * h.\nSince each floor in the mall is 24 feet high, the third floor balcony is at a height of 3 * 24 = 72 feet. Therefore, the ball will go up to 4/3 * 72 = 96 feet on its second bounce.\nSo the correct answer is D) 48.
2025-12-24 17:15:56 | INFO | Q1022 id=gsm8k_mcq_01021 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can reason that:\n\n  * 40% of the 60 questions are easy, which means there are 60 x 40/100 = 24 easy questions.\n  * Aries is sure to get 75% of the easy questions, which means she will get 24 x 0.75 = 18 easy questions correct.\n  * The remaining 60 - 24 = 36 questions are either average or difficult. These are equally divided, so each group contains 36 / 2 = 18 questions.\n\nTherefore, Aries is sure to get 18 + 18 = 36 points if she answers all the questions correctly.\n\nSo the answer is A) 36.
