2025-12-24 17:16:30 | INFO | Q1106 id=gsm8k_mcq_01105 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Lauren needs to save $100,000 for a 20-year retirement period at 40% of her current salary, which would be $40,000 per year. If she saves 20% of her $100,000 salary each paycheck, which is $20,000, it will take her approximately 5 years to save the necessary amount. Therefore, Lauren needs to work for another 5 years to save enough for her retirement goals. Answer: C) 20
2025-12-24 17:16:31 | INFO | Q1042 id=gsm8k_mcq_01041 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total amount that Molly will pay for the catering can be calculated as follows:\n\n10 people want the chicken salad, which costs $6.50 per person, so the cost for the chicken salad is 10 * $6.50 = $65.\n\n6 people want the pasta salad, which also costs $6 per person, so the cost for the pasta salad is 6 * $6 = $36.\n\nTherefore, the total amount that Molly will pay for the catering is $65 + $36 = $101.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 101.
