2025-12-24 17:16:49 | INFO | Q1055 id=gsm8k_mcq_01054 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the cost of the new floor tiles as follows:\n\nArea of kitchen floor = 200 sq ft\nCost per tile = $12\nLength of each tile side = 1 ft\n\nTo find the number of tiles needed, we need to divide the total area of the floor by the area covered by each tile:\n\nNumber of tiles needed = Total area / Area covered by each tile\n= 200 sq ft / (1 ft x 1 ft)\n= 200 sq ft / 1 sq ft\n= 200\n\nSo, the total cost of the new floor tiles would be:\n\nTotal cost = Number of tiles x Cost per tile\n= 200 x $12\n= $240\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) $240.\n\nIs there anything else I can help you with?
2025-12-24 17:16:50 | INFO | Q1122 id=gsm8k_mcq_01121 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Sofie will walk 10 miles per day for 7 days, which means she will walk a total of 70 miles in those 7 days. Since Sofie will walk twice as far as Brian, we can infer that Brian will walk half as far as Sofie, which is 70 miles / 2 = 35 miles in 7 days. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 35.
