2025-12-24 17:18:01 | INFO | Q1089 id=gsm8k_mcq_01088 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of minutes John spends in class per week is 40 minutes * 5 days = 200 minutes. He also spends 1/16 of his weekly minutes on Saturday and Sunday, which is 7*60 = 420 minutes. The total number of minutes John spends learning per week is 200 + 420 = 620 minutes. Therefore, the answer is A) 36 hours.
2025-12-24 17:18:03 | INFO | Q1091 id=gsm8k_mcq_01090 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The fourth child is three inches taller than the third child, who is five inches shorter than the second child. Therefore, the fourth child is six inches taller than the second child. Since the second child is two inches taller than the first child, the fourth child must be eight inches taller than the first child. So the answer is B) 82 inches.
2025-12-24 17:18:07 | INFO | Q1162 id=gsm8k_mcq_01161 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, Abraham will be able to sell 80 - 50 = 30 square meters of land after selling half of it for $50. This means he will be left with 30 / 2 = 15 square meters of land. He will then sell another 15 / 4 = 3.75 square meters of land for $30, which gives him a total of 30 + 3.75 = 33.75 dollars. Finally, he will sell the remaining 15 - 3.75 = 11.25 square meters of land for $3 per square meter, which gives him a total of 11.25 * 11.25 = 126 dollars. Therefore, Abraham will be able to earn a total of 33.75 + 126 = 159.75 dollars after selling all his unused land. The closest choice from the options provided is A) 200, which is incorrect. The correct answer is D) 140.
2025-12-24 17:18:08 | INFO | Q1093 id=gsm8k_mcq_01092 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that the triceratops had 540 kilograms of meat before the T-Rex ate it. Here's how:\n\n  * The T-Rex ate half of the triceratops, which means it consumed 540 / 2 = 270 kilograms of meat.\n  * After the T-Rex left, a pack of velociraptors scavenged half of what was left, which is also 270 kilograms of meat.\n\nTherefore, the total amount of meat that was on the triceratops before the T-Rex ate it was 540 kilograms. Answer: D) 540
2025-12-24 17:18:09 | INFO | Q1164 id=gsm8k_mcq_01163 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Tyrion changes his face mask two times every time he goes out, and he goes out three times a day. Therefore, he uses 2 face masks per day. Since there are 2 days in every 2-day period, Tyrion uses 2 face masks every 2 days.\nAnswer: A) 10
