2025-12-24 17:18:12 | INFO | Q1166 id=gsm8k_mcq_01165 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that the total number of apartments in the last complex is 200 * 1.6 = 320. So, the total number of apartments across all three complexes is 200 + 200 + 320 = 720. He makes $0.40 per collection for each apartment, so he makes 720 * $0.40 = $240 per week. Therefore, the answer is C) 240.
