2025-12-24 17:18:15 | INFO | Q1097 id=gsm8k_mcq_01096 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Billy can help two people per hour for three hours a day, which means he can help a total of 2 * 3 = 6 people per day. If he takes 20% of the days between March 1st and April 19th off, which is approximately 15 days, then he will be available to help people on 31 - 15 = 16 days. Therefore, the total number of people that Billy will help is 6 * 16 = 96 people. The answer is A) 240.
2025-12-24 17:18:17 | INFO | Q1170 id=gsm8k_mcq_01169 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can reason that:\n\n  * Rissa received 3 times as much money as Ronnie, which means she received 5 x 3 = $15\n  * After giving an equal amount of money to their little sister, Rissa is left with 4/5 of her original amount, which is $15 x 4/5 = $12\n  * Therefore, Ronnie must have given $12 - $5 = $7 to their little sister\n\nSo the answer is A) 3.
2025-12-24 17:18:18 | INFO | Q1099 id=gsm8k_mcq_01098 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJeff = Martha + 10\nMartha = Mike - 4\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation gives:\n\nJeff = (Mike - 4) + 10\nJeff = Mike + 6\n\nGiven that Mike is 24 years old, we can substitute that value into the equation above to find Jeff's age:\n\nJeff = 24 + 6\nJeff = 30\n\nTherefore, Jeff is 30 years old.\n\nAnswer: A) 30
