2025-12-24 17:18:36 | INFO | Q1178 id=gsm8k_mcq_01177 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that:\n\nOne-third of the girls are on varsity, which means 12 / 3 = 4 girls are on varsity.\nOne-quarter of the boys are on varsity, which means 12 / 4 = 3 boys are on varsity.\n\nTherefore, the number of students who are not on varsity is:\n\n12 + 12 - 4 - 3 = 13\n\nSo the answer is C) 13.\n\n反思：在回答问题时，要仔细听清楚问题的条件和要求，并且不能随意猜测答案。只有经过严密的推理和计算，才能得出正确的答案。
