2025-12-24 17:18:45 | INFO | Q1182 id=gsm8k_mcq_01181 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equations:\n\nWendy = 5 * (Colin + 7)\nColin + 7 = 3 * (Wendy - 25)\n\nSolving for Colin in the second equation gives us:\n\nColin = 3 * (Wendy - 25) - 7\n\nSubstituting that value into the first equation gives us:\n\nWendy = 5 * ((3 * (Wendy - 25) - 7) + 7)\n\nExpanding and simplifying gives us:\n\nWendy = 5 * (3 * Wendy - 18)\n\nDividing both sides by 5 gives us:\n\nWendy = 3 * Wendy - 3\n\nAdding 3 to both sides gives us:\n\n3 * Wendy = 3 * Wendy + 3\n\nSubtracting 3 * Wendy from both sides gives us:\n\n3 = 3\n\nThis equation is true, but it doesn't give us any information about Colin's age. It seems like there might be an error in the problem statement or the calculations.\n\nTherefore, I cannot be sure about the correctness of the given answer.
2025-12-24 17:18:47 | INFO | Q1113 id=gsm8k_mcq_01112 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each person will receive 12 kg / (1 + 1/4 + 1/3) = 12 kg / (5/12 + 4/12 + 3/12) = 12 kg / 10/12 = 12 kg * (12/10) = 12 kg * 1.2 = 14.4 kg.\nSince each person received 14.4 kg of apples, and there were three people in total (Pierre, Paul, and Jacques), the total amount of apples that they bought together was 14.4 kg * 3 = 43.2 kg.\nTherefore, James will have 12 kg - 43.2 kg = -31.2 kg of apples left. Since the result is negative, it means that James will not have any apples left and will be short by 31.2 kg.\nTherefore, the answer is A) 5.
