2025-12-24 17:19:52 | INFO | Q1154 id=gsm8k_mcq_01153 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that:\n\n  * Jim collected 27 seashells, which was 5 more than what Carlos collected.\n  * Carlos collected twice as many as Carrey.\n\nTherefore, we can infer that:\n\n  * Carrey collected 27 - 5 = 22 seashells\n  * Carlos collected 22 x 2 = 44 seashells\n\nAltogether, they collected 27 + 22 + 44 = 93 seashells.\n\nSince they divided them equally among themselves, each person got 93 / 3 = 31 seashells.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 31.
