2025-12-24 17:22:17 | INFO | Q1231 id=gsm8k_mcq_01230 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Charlie earns $80 per hour for his standard lessons. He has four lessons scheduled at this rate, which will bring him a total of $80 x 4 = $320\. Additionally, he has two lessons scheduled with a veteran, for which he reduces his rate by 25%. The reduced rate for these lessons is 80 * (1 - 25%) = $60 per hour. Therefore, he will earn $60 x 2 = $120 for these two lessons. Altogether, Charlie will make $320 + $120 = $440 for the day. Answer: A) 440
2025-12-24 17:22:19 | INFO | Q1233 id=gsm8k_mcq_01232 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Eve gave away half of the pomelos she originally had, which is equal to 20 / 2 = 10 pomelos. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 10 pomelos.
