2025-12-24 17:22:21 | INFO | Q1304 id=gsm8k_mcq_01303 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it takes Nate 14 days to dig all the holes that his dog digs during his vacation. After Nate comes home, they start filling in the holes together at a rate of 9 holes per day. The dog continues to dig 6 new holes each night, so in total they are digging 9 + 6 = 15 holes per day. It will take them 14 / 15 = 1.14 days to fill in all the holes. Since there are 7 days in a week, it will take them approximately 1.14 * 7 = 8 weeks to fill in all the holes. Therefore, the answer is C) 4.
