2025-12-24 17:22:37 | INFO | Q1243 id=gsm8k_mcq_01242 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that half of the hats are red, which means there are 100 / 2 = 50 red hats. The remaining number of hats is 100 - 50 = 50. If three fifths of these remaining hats are blue, then there are 3 / 5 * 50 = 30 blue hats. Therefore, the number of white hats is 50 - 30 - 30 = 10. Answer: C) 20
