2025-12-24 17:24:38 | INFO | Q1311 id=gsm8k_mcq_01310 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\nAaron's time = 16 minutes\n\nVanessa's time = 4 miles / 2 times Aaron's speed\n\nWe know that Aaron's speed is twice Vanessa's speed, so:\n\nVanessa's speed = 1 mile / Aaron's speed\n\nSubstituting this into the equation above, we get:\n\nVanessa's time = 4 miles / (1 mile / Aaron's speed)\n\nMultiplying both sides by Aaron's speed, we get:\n\nVanessa's time = 4 miles * Aaron's speed\n\nSince Aaron's speed is twice Vanessa's speed, we can substitute that value in:\n\nVanessa's time = 4 miles * 2 Aaron's speed\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nVanessa's time = 8 miles\n\nTherefore, Vanessa took 8 minutes to complete her part of the race.\n\nAnswer: A) 8
2025-12-24 17:24:42 | INFO | Q1313 id=gsm8k_mcq_01312 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total revenue generated by Tom's restaurant per day as follows:\n\n6 reservations x $5 meal cost = $30 in meal sales per day\n2 bottles of $5 wine cost = $10 in wine sales per day\n\nSo, the total daily revenue generated by Tom's restaurant is $30 + $10 = $40.\n\nSince Tom's restaurant is open two days a week, their weekly revenue would be:\n\n$40 per day x 2 days = $80 per week\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is not among the options provided. The correct answer is C) 80.
2025-12-24 17:24:46 | INFO | Q1315 id=gsm8k_mcq_01314 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that James is currently 19 years + 2 times 12 years = 33 years old. Since Dora will turn 12 in 3 years, she is currently 12 years - 3 years = 9 years old. Therefore, John's youngest son, who was born when John was 32, is currently 32 years - 9 years = 23 years old. In 3 years, he will be 23 years + 3 years = 26 years old. Therefore, the correct answer is not among the options given.
2025-12-24 17:24:50 | INFO | Q1317 id=gsm8k_mcq_01316 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the total cost of the new radiator is $400, and Mark got it at a junk shop for 80% off, so he paid $400 * (1 - 80%) = $400 * 20% = $80 less than the original price. Therefore, the final price Mark paid for the radiator is $400 - $80 = $320.\nThe installation of the radiator took 3 hours at $50 an hour, so the total cost of labor is 3 hours * $50 = $150\. Adding the cost of the radiator, Mark paid $320 + $150 = $470 for the new radiator and labor.\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) $470.
2025-12-24 17:24:52 | INFO | Q1319 id=gsm8k_mcq_01318 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that there will be a total of 7 x 8 = 56 slices of pizza. If Henry and his friends want to share the pizzas equally, then each of them should be able to have 56 / 4 = 14 slices of pizza.\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 14.
2025-12-24 17:24:56 | INFO | Q03 id=gsm8k_mcq_00564 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=In the first week, Judy read for 15 minutes each night, so she read for a total of 7 * 15 = 105 minutes. In the second week, she read a total of 100 pages. If she can read 2 pages per 1.5 minutes, then she read 100 / (2 * 1.5) = 66.67 pages. Therefore, she read a total of 105 + 66.67 = 171.67 pages in two weeks. Answer: C) 240
2025-12-24 17:25:00 | INFO | Q03 id=gsm8k_mcq_00660 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant= | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\n2x + 4y = 70\n\nWhere x represents the number of sheep and y represents the number of geese.\n\nWe also know that the total number of heads is 20, so:\n\nx + y = 20\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\n2x + 4(20 - x) = 70\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n2x + 80 - 4x = 70\n-2x = -10\nx = 5\n\nTherefore, there are 5 sheep on Lee's farm. The answer is D.
