2025-12-24 17:27:58 | INFO | Q78 id=gsm8k_mcq_00077 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equations:\n\nRaymond = 1/2 * Sarah\nSarah = 4 * David\n\nSubstituting the values for Sarah into the equation for Raymond, we get:\n\nRaymond = 1/2 * 4 * David\nRaymond = 2 * David\n\nTherefore, the difference in the amount of laundry Raymond and David do is 2 times the amount of laundry that David does.\n\nPlugging in the value given in the question that Sarah does 400 pounds of laundry, we can find that David does:\n\nDavid = 400 / 4 = 100 pounds of laundry\n\nTherefore, the difference between the amount of laundry Raymond and David do is:\n\n2 * 100 = 200 pounds\n\nThe answer is D) 200.
