2025-12-24 17:28:27 | INFO | Q95 id=gsm8k_mcq_00094 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 60 - 12(x + 1)\n\nWhere x represents the number of cats.\n\nSince there are two cats for every dog, we can also say that:\n\nNumber of dogs = Number of cats / 2\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 60 - 12((Number of cats / 2) + 1)\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 60 - 12(number of cats + 1)\n\nSubstituting the value of number of dogs, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 60 - 12(60/2 + 1)\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 60 - 12(31)\n\nSubtracting 60 from both sides, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = -12(31)\n\nMultiplying both sides by -1, we get:\n\nNumber of rabbits = 372\n\nTherefore, the total number of pets in the neighborhood is 372. The answer is C).
