2025-12-24 17:31:31 | INFO | Q197 id=gsm8k_mcq_00196 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it can be calculated that each restaurant will receive 2 pounds of carrots. Therefore, a total of 40 * 2 = 80 pounds of carrots will be distributed to all 40 restaurants. To find out how many pounds of carrots will not be used, we need to subtract the amount of carrots distributed from the total amount available. The total amount of carrots available is 200 pounds, so the number of pounds of carrots that will not be used is 200 - 80 = 120 pounds. Therefore, the answer is B) 120.
2025-12-24 17:31:33 | INFO | Q200 id=gsm8k_mcq_00199 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that Mark earns 5 cents per sentence from Publisher A, so he makes 5 * 1000 = 5000 cents from Publisher A per week. We also know that Publisher B pays double what Publisher A pays, so they pay 2 * 5 = 10 cents per sentence. Therefore, Mark earns 10 * 1000 = 10000 cents per week from Publisher B. In total, Mark makes 5000 + 10000 = 15000 cents per week. The answer is A) 15000.
