2025-12-24 17:33:42 | INFO | Q268 id=gsm8k_mcq_00267 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The total time it takes for the oil to heat up to 300 degrees is 20 minutes. It then takes 40% longer for the oil to heat up to the desired temperature of 400 degrees, which is 40/100 * 20 = 8 minutes longer. So it takes 20 + 8 = 28 minutes for the oil to heat up to 400 degrees.\nAfter warming the oil, it takes 5 minutes less time to cook than it took to warm up the oil. This means it takes 28 - 5 = 23 minutes to cook the chicken.\nTherefore, the total time that passes from starting the oil to having cooked chicken is 23 + 28 = 51 minutes. The answer is A) 51.
