2025-12-24 17:35:18 | INFO | Q317 id=gsm8k_mcq_00316 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total weight of marbles Solomon has in the store as follows:\n\nSolomon bought 20 marbles from Johanna, so there are now 20 + 50 = 70 marbles in the store.\n\nHis father gave him 2/5 times as many marbles as he bought from Johanna, which is 2/5 * 20 = 8 marbles.\n\nSo, the total number of marbles Solomon has in the store is now 70 + 8 = 78 marbles.\n\nTherefore, the total weight of marbles Solomon has in the store is 78 * 2kg = 156kg.\n\nThe answer is A) 156.
