2025-12-24 17:36:42 | INFO | Q381 id=gsm8k_mcq_00380 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=To calculate the monthly payment, we need to find out how much interest Karan needs to pay each month. The formula for calculating simple interest is: Amount = Principal x Rate x Time\nIn this case, the Principal is $3,650, the Rate is 10% (or 0.1), and the Time is 5 months (or 5/12).\nSo, the amount of interest Karan needs to pay is: $3,650 x 0.1 x 5/12 = $1,416.50\nSince she has to pay an equal amount every month, she will have to pay $1,416.50 as her monthly payment.\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 760.
2025-12-24 17:36:44 | INFO | Q363 id=gsm8k_mcq_00362 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the total amount of stuffing needed for the 4 chihuahua beds as follows:\n\n4 chihuahua beds * 2 pounds of stuffing per bed = 8 pounds of stuffing\n\nWe can also calculate the total amount of stuffing needed for the 3 collie beds as follows:\n\n3 collie beds * average amount of stuffing between a Rottweiler bed and a chihuahua bed = (8 + 2) / 2 = 5 pounds of stuffing\n\nTherefore, the total amount of stuffing needed for all 7 beds is:\n\n8 + 5 = 13 pounds of stuffing\n\nSo the answer is closest to C) 17.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 17.
