2025-12-24 17:37:36 | INFO | Q409 id=gsm8k_mcq_00408 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate how long it will take for Toby to read the book by dividing the number of pages by the average number of words per page: 45 pages / 200 words/page = 0.225 hours. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, it will take Toby approximately 12 minutes to read the book.\nWe also know that it takes 10 minutes to get to the airport and that Toby has 60 minutes until his flight. Therefore, he has 50 minutes remaining to make it to the airport.\nTo determine how many minutes early Toby will be, we need to subtract the time it takes him to read the book from the total time he has before his flight: 60 minutes - 12 minutes - 10 minutes = 48 minutes. Thus, Toby will be 48 minutes early to the airport.\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 50.
2025-12-24 17:37:37 | INFO | Q392 id=gsm8k_mcq_00391 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\nBetty + Sam = 165\nLet x be the number of popsicles Betty has and y be the number of popsicles Sam has. We can write the above equation as:\nx + y = 165\nSince the ratio of popsicles that Betty and Sam have is 5:6, we can say that x/y = 5/6.\nSubstituting the value of x from the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n5y/6 + y = 165\nMultiplying both sides by 6, we get:\n5y + 6y = 1014\nSimplifying, we get:\n11y = 1014\nDividing both sides by 11, we get:\ny = 93\nTherefore, Sam has 93 more popsicles than Betty.\nAnswer: C) 90
