2025-12-24 17:37:41 | INFO | Q394 id=gsm8k_mcq_00393 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total amount of time Carol spent on the song is 4 hours + 90 minutes = 4.9 hours. Half of this amount of time is 4.9 hours / 2 = 2.45 hours. Therefore, Carol spent 2.45 hours recording the song. The total amount of time she spent on the song is therefore 4.9 hours + 2.45 hours = 7.35 hours. Thus, Carol spent 90 minutes / 7.35 hours = 12.68% of her total work time editing the song. The closest choice from the options provided is C) 13. Therefore, the answer is C).
