2025-12-24 17:37:43 | INFO | Q413 id=gsm8k_mcq_00412 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Shannon needs to make enough cookies to last her for 30 days, and her recipe makes one dozen madeleine cookies. To determine how many dozens of cookies she needs to make, we can divide the number of days she wants the cookies to last by the number of days each batch of cookies lasts.\nIf each batch of cookies lasts 30 days, then Shannon would need to bake 30 batches of cookies to last her for 30 days. Since each batch makes one dozen cookies, Shannon would need to bake 30 * 12 = 360 cookies in total.\nTherefore, Shannon will need to make 360 / 12 = 30 dozens of cookies to last her for 30 days.\nAnswer: C) 30
