2025-12-24 17:37:48 | INFO | Q415 id=gsm8k_mcq_00414 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, the total cost of the discounted blouses can be calculated as follows:\n\n    Each blouse has a regular price of $20.\n    Misha picks out 4 blouses from the 30% off rack.\n    To find the discount per blouse, we need to calculate 30% of $20, which is:\n\n        30% × $20 = $6\n\nSo each blouse is being sold at $20 - $6 = $14.\n\nTherefore, the total cost of the 4 discounted blouses is:\n\n    4 × $14 = $56\n\nThus, the correct answer is D) 56.\n\nSecond-round QA:\n\n    Is the answer 56?\n\nYes, the answer is 56.
