2025-12-24 17:38:51 | INFO | Q450 id=gsm8k_mcq_00449 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Beatrice bought a total of 6 + 4 = 10 packets of crayons. Each packet of six had 8 pieces of colors, so there were a total of 6 * 8 = 48 pieces of colors from the six packets. Each packet of 16 had 16 pieces of colors, so there were a total of 16 * 4 = 64 pieces of colors from the four packets. Therefore, Beatrice bought a total of 48 + 64 = 112 pieces of colors. The answer is A) 112.
