2025-12-24 17:39:09 | INFO | Q467 id=gsm8k_mcq_00466 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the cost of apples for both Becky and Kelly:\n\nBecky: 20 apples * $0.45/apple = $9\nKelly: 20 apples * $0.50/apple = $10\n\nThe discount that Becky received was $1, so she paid $9 - $1 = $8. The discount that Kelly received was 10%, which is equal to $10 * 0.10 = $1. So Kelly paid $10 - $1 = $9.\n\nTherefore, Kelly paid $1 more than Becky.\n\nAnswer: A) 3
