2025-12-24 17:39:15 | INFO | Q444 id=gsm8k_mcq_00443 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that James' time for the swim was 40 minutes / 1.1 = 36.7 minutes faster than Jon's time. This means that James' time for the swim was 36.7 minutes + 40 minutes = 76.7 minutes. Since James took 5 minutes longer on the bike than Jon, his time for the bike was 60 minutes + 5 minutes = 65 minutes. Therefore, James' total time for the triathlon was 76.7 minutes + 65 minutes + 50 minutes = 201.7 minutes. If Jon won by 10 minutes, then his time for the run was 201.7 minutes - 10 minutes = 191.7 minutes. Answer: B) 51
