2025-12-24 17:39:20 | INFO | Q446 id=gsm8k_mcq_00445 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the cost of the hay as follows:\n\nFor every mile the horse runs, it eats 1/2 a bail of hay. Since the horse runs for 30 minutes at 32MPH, which is approximately 17 miles, the horse will eat 17/2 = 8.5 bales of hay.\n\nThe cost of these 8.5 bales of hay is 8.5 x $3 = $25.5.\n\nMichael has six 5-dollar bills, so he has a total of $6 x 5 = $30.\n\nAfter buying the hay, Michael has $30 - $25.5 = $4.5 left over.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) $4.
