2025-12-24 17:39:53 | INFO | Q466 id=gsm8k_mcq_00465 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Miss Maria has a total of 6 x 25 = 150 basketball cards. We also know that she has 5 x 40 = 200 baseball cards. Adding these two numbers together, we get a total of 150 + 200 = 350 cards. Since Miss Maria keeps 50 cards for herself, she gives the remaining 350 - 50 = 300 cards to her students. If her students each receive 10 cards, then Miss Maria has 300 / 10 = 30 students. Therefore, the answer is D) 30.
2025-12-24 17:39:53 | INFO | Q495 id=gsm8k_mcq_00494 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The height of the human pyramid can be found by adding up the heights of each layer. \n\nThe bottom layer has 4 girls who are all 64" tall, so their total height is 4 * 64 = 256" feet.\n\nThe second layer has 3 girls who stand on top of the 4 from the bottom layer, so their total height is 3 * (64 + 60) = 288" feet.\n\nThe third layer has 2 girls who stand on top of the 3 from the second layer, so their total height is 2 * (288 + 60) = 768" feet.\n\nFinally, the top layer has the shortest girl who stands at the top, so her height is 60" feet.\n\nTherefore, the total height of the human pyramid is 256 + 288 + 768 + 60 = 1372" feet, which is equal to 22 feet.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C) 22.
