2025-12-24 17:41:34 | INFO | Q526 id=gsm8k_mcq_00525 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that each batch of oatmeal cookies requires 3/4 cup of raisins, which is equal to 0.75 cups of raisins. If Heather divides the bag of 27 cups of raisins equally among the oatmeal cookies, granola, and snack mix, then each batch will require 0.75 cups of raisins. Therefore, Heather can make 27 / 0.75 = 36 batches of oatmeal cookies. The answer is B) 36.
