2025-12-24 17:41:40 | INFO | Q553 id=gsm8k_mcq_00552 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To calculate Antonella's earnings, we need to determine how much commission she made from each sales range.\n\nFirst, we find that for sales between $1000 and $2500, Antonella earns 30% commission on the first $1000 and an additional 10% commission on the remaining $1500. To calculate her commission on the first $1000, we multiply $1000 by 30% (or 0.3), which equals $300. To calculate her commission on the remaining $1500, we multiply $1500 by 10% (or 0.1), which equals $150.\n\nTherefore, Antonella earned a total commission of $300 + $150 = $450 for selling goods worth $2500.\n\nSo the correct answer is C) 450.
2025-12-24 17:41:40 | INFO | Q530 id=gsm8k_mcq_00529 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Tom spent $48 on a CD and a headphone set. If he had decided not to buy the headphones, he would have saved $48 - $4 = $44. Since each CD costs $4, Tom would have been able to buy $44 / $4 = 11 more CDs if he had not bought the headphones set. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 11.
