2025-12-24 17:42:13 | INFO | Q548 id=gsm8k_mcq_00547 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The question states that each family calls three other families, and this process continues for four rounds. Therefore, in the first round, there are 3 families called. In the second round, each of these three families calls three other families, resulting in 9 families being called. In the third round, each of these 9 families calls three other families, resulting in 27 families being called. In the fourth round, each of these 27 families calls three other families, resulting in 81 families being called.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 81.
2025-12-24 17:42:13 | INFO | Q576 id=gsm8k_mcq_00575 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Kate has 3 boxes of 64 crayons, which means she has a total of 3 * 64 = 192 crayons. She plans to melt 8 small pieces of crayons together to make crayon muffins. If she can sell each muffin crayon for $1.50, then she will be able to sell a total of 192 / 8 = 24 muffin crayons. Therefore, the amount of money that Kate can make is 24 * $1.50 = $36. Answer: C
