2025-12-24 17:43:18 | INFO | Q583 id=gsm8k_mcq_00582 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the value of Juan's house as follows:\n\nHerb's house = $76,000\nJuan's house is 30% less expensive than Herb's, so it costs 76,000 * (1 - 30%) = 76,000 * 70% = $53,200\n\nTherefore, the total value of the two houses combined is:\n\nHerb's house + Juan's house = $76,000 + $53,200 = $129,200\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 129200.
2025-12-24 17:43:18 | INFO | Q619 id=gsm8k_mcq_00618 | baseline_pred=D | gold=D | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of seats in the school auditorium is 4 rows * 18 seats = 72 seats.\nOne fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators, which is 72 seats / 4 = 18 seats.\nSo, one third of the remaining seats were occupied by the parents, which is 72 seats - 18 seats = 54 seats.\nTherefore, the number of students who were there in the school auditorium is 54 seats + 18 seats = 72 seats.\nAnswer: C) 72
2025-12-24 17:43:22 | INFO | Q621 id=gsm8k_mcq_00620 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total number of times both DVDs can be played before they break as follows:\n\nOne DVD has been played 356 times, so it will last for 1000 - 356 = 644 more plays.\n\nThe other DVD has been played 135 times, so it will last for 1000 - 135 = 865 more plays.\n\nTherefore, the total number of times both DVDs can be played before they break is 644 + 865 = 1509.\n\nSo the answer is A) 1509.
2025-12-24 17:43:25 | INFO | Q585 id=gsm8k_mcq_00584 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the cost of each pair of contacts as follows:\n\n  * There are 90 single use contacts in each box, which will last Pete 45 days, so each contact lasts for approximately 1.83 days.\n  * Each box costs $100.00, and there is currently a 10% discount, so the discounted price of each box is $100.00 - $10.00 = $90.00.\n  * If Pete buys two boxes of contacts, he will receive a total of 180 single use contacts.\n\nTherefore, the cost of each pair of contacts would be:\n\n  * 180 single use contacts / 2 pairs = 90 contacts per pair\n\nPlugging in the number of contacts per pair into the formula above, we get:\n\n  * 90 contacts per pair / 1.83 days per contact = $49.66 per pair\n\nTherefore, the closest option from the choices provided is A) $2.22. However, it's important to note that the actual cost of each pair of contacts may be slightly higher than $2.22 due to the manufacturing cost and other factors.
2025-12-24 17:43:27 | INFO | Q623 id=gsm8k_mcq_00622 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, Jim chewed gum during the school day for 8 hours / 2 hours = 4 hours. He chewed 1 piece on the way home and 1 stick after dinner, so he chewed a total of 1 + 1 = 2 pieces. At the beginning of the day, Jim had 20 packs of gum * 1 piece = 20 pieces. After chewing 2 pieces, Jim has 20 - 2 = 18 pieces of gum. Since Jim gives half of the gum he has remaining to his sister, he gives away 18 / 2 = 9 pieces of gum. Therefore, Jim has 18 - 9 = 9 pieces of gum left at the end of the day. The answer is C) 7.
2025-12-24 17:43:29 | INFO | Q588 id=gsm8k_mcq_00587 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that the jar contains 4500/3=1500 red jelly beans. The note on the jar states that there are 1% fewer red jelly beans than blue jelly beans, so there are 1500-1=1499 blue jelly beans. The note also states that there are 1% more green jelly beans than blue jelly beans, so there are 1499+1=1500 green jelly beans. Therefore, the jar contains 1500-1499=1 more green jelly bean than red jelly beans. The answer is C) 1.
2025-12-24 17:43:29 | INFO | Q625 id=gsm8k_mcq_00624 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The baseball coach spent $27 on baseballs because 9 x 3 = 27. The basketball coach spent $112 on basketballs because 8 x 14 = 112. The basketball coach spent $85 more than the baseball coach because 112 - 27 = 85. Answer: A
2025-12-24 17:43:32 | INFO | Q627 id=gsm8k_mcq_00626 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate Ashley's internet connection speed in MB per hour as follows:\n\n20 KB/second x 3600 seconds/hour = 72000 KB/hour\n\nTo convert KB to MB, we divide by 1000:\n\n72000 KB / 1000 = 72 MB/hour\n\nTherefore, Ashley's internet connection speed in MB per hour is 72.\n\nAnswer: D) 72
2025-12-24 17:43:33 | INFO | Q590 id=gsm8k_mcq_00589 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, Martin will lose 1.25 pounds per week if he eats Cheerios every day for breakfast and gain 1.75 pounds per week if he eats donuts every day for breakfast. Therefore, over 5 weeks, he will gain 5 * 1.75 = 8.75 pounds if he eats donuts every day for breakfast and lose 5 * 1.25 = 6.25 pounds if he eats Cheerios every day for breakfast. The difference in his weight at the end of 5 weeks between the two breakfast options will be 8.75 - 6.25 = 2.5 pounds. Answer: A) 2.5
2025-12-24 17:43:33 | INFO | Q629 id=gsm8k_mcq_00628 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, Adam will need to grow 4 inches taller to ride the roller coaster. Since he grows 2 inches a year, it will take him approximately 2 years to reach the necessary height. Therefore, the answer is A) 2.
2025-12-24 17:43:38 | INFO | Q592 id=gsm8k_mcq_00591 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the weight of the Mastiff can be calculated as follows:\n\n- The Dachshund weighs twice as much as the Affenpinscher, who weighs 10 pounds, so the Dachshund weighs 2 x 10 = 20 pounds.\n- The Papillon weighs one-fourth as much as the Dachshund, who weighs 20 pounds, so the Papillon weighs 20 / 4 = 5 pounds.\n- The Mastiff weighs 44 times the weight of the Papillon, who weighs 5 pounds, so the Mastiff weighs 44 x 5 = 220 pounds.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 880.
2025-12-24 17:43:38 | INFO | Q631 id=gsm8k_mcq_00630 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate the number of men who can stay upright on the wave as follows:\n\nOut of 100 surfers, 60% are women, so 100 - 60 = 40% are men.\n\nWhen a wave over 30 feet arrives, only 25% of the riders can stay upright. Since 40% of the riders are men, we can multiply 40% by 25% to find the number of men who can stay upright on the wave:\n\n40% x 25% = 10%\n\nTherefore, out of 100 surfers, 10% of them, which is equal to 10 men, can stay upright on the wave.\n\nSo the answer is B) 10.
2025-12-24 17:43:41 | INFO | Q594 id=gsm8k_mcq_00593 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The beanstalk will double in height every day, so after one day it will be 4 * 2 = 8 feet tall. After two days it will be 8 * 2 = 16 feet tall. After three days it will be 16 * 2 = 32 feet tall. After four days it will be 32 * 2 = 64 feet tall. Therefore, it will take four days for the beanstalk to be taller than Mark's window. Answer: B) 4
2025-12-24 17:43:41 | INFO | Q633 id=gsm8k_mcq_00632 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Max bought 16 snowflake stamps, 3 more truck stamps than snowflake stamps, which equals 16 + 3 = 19 truck stamps. He also bought 9 fewer rose stamps than truck stamps, which equals 19 - 9 = 10 rose stamps. Therefore, Max bought a total of 16 + 19 + 10 = 45 stamps at the post office. The answer is C) 45.
2025-12-24 17:43:44 | INFO | Q596 id=gsm8k_mcq_00595 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Jerry is currently x years old. Since Jerry is twice as old as he was five years ago, we can set up the equation: x = 2 * (x - 5). Solving for x gives us x = 13. Therefore, Jerry is currently 13 years old. In three years, Jerry will be 13 + 3 = 16 years old. The answer is A) 16.
2025-12-24 17:43:45 | INFO | Q635 id=gsm8k_mcq_00634 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equation for the number of fish caught by Tommy:\n\nTommy = Darren + 3\n\nWe also know that Darren caught six less than Naomi, so:\n\nDarren = Naomi - 6\n\nSubstituting this into the equation for Tommy, we get:\n\nTommy = (Naomi - 6) + 3\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nTommy = Naomi - 3\n\nFinally, we know that Naomi caught 17 fish, so:\n\nTommy = 17 - 3\n\nTherefore, Tommy caught 14 fish. The answer is A.
2025-12-24 17:43:46 | INFO | Q598 id=gsm8k_mcq_00597 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The sum of the three angles in a triangle is 180 degrees. Let x be the smallest angle. Then, the other two angles are 2x and 3x. Adding all the angles gives us 180 = x + 2x + 3x = 6x. Therefore, x = 30 degrees. So the largest angle is 3x = 3 * 30 = 90 degrees. Answer: A
2025-12-24 17:43:48 | INFO | Q637 id=gsm8k_mcq_00636 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate Julie's daily production by multiplying Jewel's daily production by 2: 50 * 2 = 100 customers\nSince there are 5 working days in a week, Julie's weekly production would be: 100 * 5 = 500 customers\nTherefore, the total weekly production for the two is 500 + 50 = 550 customers. The closest option is C) 700, so the final answer is C).
2025-12-24 17:43:50 | INFO | Q600 id=gsm8k_mcq_00599 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the question, each dog has 4 legs, each cat has 4 legs, and each bird has 2 legs. Therefore, the total number of legs for all the pets in the store is:\n\n5 dogs * 4 legs/dog + 2 cats * 4 legs/cat + 10 birds * 2 legs/bird = 20 legs\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 17.\n\nSecond-round QA response: The correct answer is C) 17 because each animal has its corresponding number of legs.
2025-12-24 17:43:52 | INFO | Q639 id=gsm8k_mcq_00638 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the cost of each item separately.\nThe cost of four apples is $5.20, so the cost per apple is $5.20/4 = $1.30.\nThe cost of three oranges is $3.30, so the cost per orange is $3.30/3 = $1.10.\nTherefore, the total cost of five apples and five oranges would be $1.30 x 5 + $1.10 x 5 = $10.70.\nHence, the correct answer is C) 10.70.
2025-12-24 17:43:55 | INFO | Q602 id=gsm8k_mcq_00601 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it can be inferred that Steve receives 5 games for his birthday each year, and he saves up enough money to buy 1 game per month for a year, so at the end of the first year he will have bought 12 games + 5 games = 17 games. The following year, he starts buying 2 games a month, so at the end of the second year he will have bought 24 games + 5 games = 29 games. In the third year, he buys 4 games a month, so at the end of the third year he will have bought 36 games + 5 games = 41 games. Therefore, after 3 years, Steve will have 17 games + 29 games + 41 games = 87 games. The closest choice from the options provided is C) 89, which is therefore the most likely answer.
2025-12-24 17:44:00 | INFO | Q641 id=gsm8k_mcq_00640 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, the total cost of Bill's new truck can be calculated as follows:\n\nThe base price of the truck is $30,000.\n\nThe king cab upgrade costs an extra $7,500, so the total cost of the king cab is $30,000 + $7,500 = $37,500.\n\nLeather seats are one-third the cost of the king cab upgrade, which means they cost $7,500 / 3 = $2,500 each. Since Bill is purchasing four leather seats, the total cost of leather seats is $2,500 x 4 = $10,000.\n\nRunning boards are $500 less than the leather seats, so their cost is $10,000 - $500 = $9,500.\n\nThe upgraded exterior light package costs $1,500, so the total cost of all additional features is $7,500 + $10,000 + $9,500 + $1,500 = $38,000.\n\nTherefore, the total cost of Bill's new truck is $38,000 + $30,000 = $68,000.\n\nHence, the correct answer is not among the choices provided.
2025-12-24 17:44:00 | INFO | Q604 id=gsm8k_mcq_00603 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Ruiz makes 120 pounds of chocolates in two hours, which means he makes 120 pounds / 2 hours = 60 pounds per hour. Marissa makes three-fourths as many pounds of chocolates in an hour as Ruiz does in two hours, which means she makes 3/4 * 60 pounds = 45 pounds per hour. Therefore, if they both work for 12 hours in a day, Ruiz will make 60 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 720 pounds. Marissa will make 45 pounds per hour x 12 hours = 540 pounds. Together, they will make 720 pounds + 540 pounds = 1260 pounds of chocolates. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 1260.
