2025-12-24 17:44:41 | INFO | Q664 id=gsm8k_mcq_00663 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it can be inferred that James delivers a certain number of newspapers to each district. In this case, he delivers 198 newspapers to District A, some to District B, and 209 newspapers to District C. To find out how many newspapers he delivers to District B, we need to add up the number of newspapers he delivers to all three districts.\nTherefore, the total number of newspapers delivered by James is 198 + some + 209 = 607 newspapers. Since James delivers 600 newspapers in a day, it can be concluded that he delivers 607 - 600 = 7 newspapers to District B.\nTherefore, the answer to the question is C) 203.
