2025-12-24 17:44:58 | INFO | Q676 id=gsm8k_mcq_00675 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the total number of dogs in the shelter before James bought any toys was 4 dogs + 8 dogs = 12 dogs. Since each dog needs one toy, James initially needed 12 dogs * 1 toy = 12 toys. After buying more toys, the total number of dogs in the shelter became 12 dogs + 2 times the initial number of dogs = 12 dogs + 24 dogs = 36 dogs. Since 3 dogs were gone when James came back, he no longer needed those toys, so he still needs 36 dogs - 3 dogs = 33 toys. Therefore, the answer is A) 33.
