2025-12-24 17:45:10 | INFO | Q682 id=gsm8k_mcq_00681 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information given, we can set up the following equations:\n\nKatarina = Max - 5\nMax = Cookie Monster + 12\nSummer = Max + 23\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the third equation gives:\n\nSummer = (Cookie Monster + 12) + 23\nSummer = Cookie Monster + 35\n\nSubstituting this back into the first equation gives:\n\nKatarina = Max - 5\nKatarina = (Cookie Monster + 35) - 5\nKatarina = Cookie Monster + 30\n\nTherefore, Katarina has 30 more cookies than the Cookie Monster. If Katarina has 68 cookies, then the Cookie Monster has 68 - 30 = 38 cookies. Max has 38 + 12 = 40 cookies. And Summer has 40 + 23 = 63 cookies. In total, they have 68 + 40 + 63 = 171 cookies.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 268.
2025-12-24 17:45:12 | INFO | Q648 id=gsm8k_mcq_00647 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the time it takes Bill to dig through each layer separately.\nFirst, let's find out how long it would take him to dig through 24 feet of soil at a rate of 4 feet per hour:\n\n24 feet / 4 feet per hour = 6 hours\n\nNext, let's find out how long it would take him to dig through 8 feet of clay at a rate of 4 feet per hour:\n\n8 feet / 2 feet per hour = 4 hours\n\nNow we can add the time it took him to dig through each layer to find the total time it would take him to dig the well:\n\n6 hours + 4 hours = 10 hours\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) 10.\n\nFinal Answer: It will take Bill 10 hours to dig the well.
