2025-12-24 17:45:47 | INFO | Q704 id=gsm8k_mcq_00703 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can set up the following equation:\n\n8m + 6f = D\n\nWhere m represents the number of dumplings eaten by the males and f represents the number of dumplings eaten by the females.\n\nWe know that each male ate one more dumpling than each female, so:\n\nm = f + 1\n\nSubstituting this into the equation above, we get:\n\n8(f + 1) + 6f = D\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n8f + 8 + 6f = D\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n14f + 8 = D\n\nWe also know that there were no leftovers, so:\n\nD = 6f + 8\n\nSubstituting this expression for D into the previous equation, we get:\n\n6f + 8 = 8f + 8\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n2f = 0\n\nTherefore, f = 0.\n\nThis means that each female ate three dumplings, and since there were six females, Larry cooked a total of 6 * 3 = 18 dumplings.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 42.
2025-12-24 17:45:50 | INFO | Q706 id=gsm8k_mcq_00705 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can determine that Martha's cat is five times faster than her turtle. If the cat can run 15 feet per second, then the turtle can crawl at a speed of 15 / 5 = 3 feet per second.\nTherefore, in 40 seconds, the turtle can crawl a total distance of 40 x 3 = 120 feet. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 120.
