2025-12-24 17:46:57 | INFO | Q746 id=gsm8k_mcq_00745 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total value of the cards that Mark bought:\n\n3 packs * $1800 = $5400\n\nThe total value of the two cards that Mark got is $4000 + $1000 = $5000.\n\nSo far, Mark has spent $5400 - $5000 = $400 on the packs.\n\nThere are 30 more cards worth an average of $50 each, so their total value is 30 * $50 = $1500.\n\nTherefore, Mark made a profit of $5000 - $400 - $1500 = $900.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) $6500.
