2025-12-24 17:47:12 | INFO | Q714 id=gsm8k_mcq_00713 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, Mr. Boarden would need 24 mosaic tiles for every square foot of his bathroom. Therefore, to cover two-thirds of his 36 sq ft bathroom, he would need 24 x 0.6 = 14.4 mosaic tiles. Since we cannot use fractional tiles, we round up to 15 mosaic tiles. Therefore, the answer is C) 288.
2025-12-24 17:47:14 | INFO | Q758 id=gsm8k_mcq_00757 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate the total number of shirts needed as follows:\n\n11 students need size extra-small = 11 shirts\nTwice as many students need size small as extra small = 2 * 11 = 22 shirts\nFour less than the number of size small students need size medium = 22 - 4 = 18 shirts\nHalf as many students need size large as size medium = 18 / 2 = 9 shirts\nSix more students need size extra-large than large = 9 + 6 = 15 shirts\n\nTherefore, the total number of shirts needed is 11 + 22 + 18 + 9 + 15 = 75 shirts.\n\nTherefore, the answer is B) 75.
