2025-12-24 17:47:56 | INFO | Q741 id=gsm8k_mcq_00740 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equation:\n\nNumber of students who like to play video games = Number of students who like to play music\n\nWe also know that the number of students who like to play music is twice the number of students who prefer playing basketball. Therefore, we can write:\n\nNumber of students who like to play music = 2 * Number of students who like to play basketball\n\nSubstituting the value for the number of students who like to play basketball from the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n\nNumber of students who like to play video games = 2 * 5 = 10\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 30.
