2025-12-24 17:49:25 | INFO | Q795 id=gsm8k_mcq_00794 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The zookeeper has counted 12 female lions, which means there are 1/2 as many male lions as female lions. If we multiply the number of female lions by 1/2, we get the number of male lions. So there are 12 / 2 = 6 male lions. Adding the number of female lions and male lions gives us 12 + 6 = 18 lions. Since the zookeeper also counted 14 lion cubs, the total number of lions in the enclosure is 18 + 14 = 32. Therefore, the answer is C) 32.
2025-12-24 17:49:28 | INFO | Q837 id=gsm8k_mcq_00836 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can set up the following equations:\n\nJada = 2x\nRory = x + 20\nKora = x\n\nGiven that Kora made 20 clay dishes, we can substitute x = 20 into the equation for Kora to find the value of x:\n\nKora = 20\n\nSubstituting this value back into the equation for Rory gives us:\n\nRory = 20 + 20 = 40\n\nFinally, substituting these values into the equation for Jada gives us:\n\nJada = 2(20) = 40\n\nTherefore, the total number of clay dishes that Jada, Rory, and Kora made together is:\n\n40 + 40 + 20 = 100\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 100.\n\nSecond-round QA ends here.
