2025-12-24 17:49:34 | INFO | Q799 id=gsm8k_mcq_00798 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, we can calculate that Billy's earnings after two months would be $10 + $0.50 = $10.50 per hour. After one year, his earnings would be $10.50 + $1 = $11.50 per hour. Therefore, over 20 hours, Billy would earn $11.50 x 20 = $230.\nSally's starting salary is $0.50 more per hour than Billy's original salary of $10, so her starting salary is $10 + $0.50 = $10.50 per hour. Over 20 hours, Sally would earn $10.50 x 20 = $210.\nTherefore, Billy will earn $230 - $210 = $20 more than Sally over 20 hours. The answer is A) 20.
