2025-12-24 17:49:45 | INFO | Q848 id=gsm8k_mcq_00847 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The formula for calculating simple interest is A = P * i * t, where A is the amount of interest earned, P is the principal amount (the initial investment), i is the annual interest rate expressed as a decimal, and t is the number of years the money is invested.\nIn this case, the principal amount is $300, the annual interest rate is 3/4, and the time period is 3 years. Substituting these values into the formula gives us:\nA = $300 * (3/4) * 3\nA = $187.5\nSo after 3 years, Brenda will have earned $187.5 in interest.\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 525.
