2025-12-24 17:49:48 | INFO | Q808 id=gsm8k_mcq_00807 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, it seems that Milo can use two bags of 72 glass chips to make his mosaic. Since each bag contains 72 chips, he will have a total of 144 chips to work with. To determine the height of his mosaic, we need to divide the number of chips by the number of square inches per inch of the mosaic. Since each square inch requires 12 chips, Milo will have 144 / 12 = 12 square inches of space for his mosaic. Therefore, his mosaic will be 3 inches tall since he wants it to be 3 inches wide. So the answer is C) 2.
2025-12-24 17:49:50 | INFO | Q852 id=gsm8k_mcq_00851 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that James spends $2640 on shoes per year, and he buys 2 pairs of shoes per month. Therefore, he spends $2640/12 = $220 on shoes per month. So, the average cost per pair of shoes is $220/2 = $110. Therefore, the answer is D) 110.
2025-12-24 17:49:50 | INFO | Q810 id=gsm8k_mcq_00809 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it seems that Dale has already sold 150 butterscotch candies and then ordered 100 more, so he now has a total of 250 butterscotch candies. If he wants to sell all of his candy, he will need to sell 250 more butterscotch candies. Therefore, the answer is A) 0.
2025-12-24 17:49:53 | INFO | Q812 id=gsm8k_mcq_00811 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, it can be inferred that Felix climbed a certain number of branches during the week to make $105. The cost for each branch is $0.25, so the total revenue generated from climbing branches would be $105 / $0.25 = 420 branches. Therefore, on average, Felix climbed 420 / 7 = 60 branches per day. Answer: A
2025-12-24 17:49:54 | INFO | Q855 id=gsm8k_mcq_00854 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided in the audio, the town will build 12 homes in the first year, which is the starting point. In the second year, they will build three times as many homes as the previous year, which would be 3 * 12 = 36 homes. In the third year, they will double the number of homes built in the second year, which would be 2 * 36 = 72 homes. Therefore, the total number of homes built over the next three years will be 12 + 36 + 72 = 220 homes. The correct answer is A) 220.
2025-12-24 17:49:56 | INFO | Q857 id=gsm8k_mcq_00856 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, Mr. Jackson needs to buy 27 / 8 = 3 packs of glue sticks. However, he expects to have some extra glue sticks left over, so he should buy 3 + 1 = 4 packs of glue sticks. Therefore, the correct answer is B) 4.
2025-12-24 17:49:56 | INFO | Q814 id=gsm8k_mcq_00813 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the information provided, we can calculate that there are a total of 35 - 3 = 32 marshmallows left in the bag. Since John makes 9 s'mores and DeSean makes 9 s'mores, they use a total of 9 + 9 = 18 marshmallows. Therefore, each kid can have 32 - 18 = 14 s'mores with the marshmallows left in the bag. Answer: A
