2025-12-24 17:52:53 | INFO | Q956 id=gsm8k_mcq_00955 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The hospital has a capacity of 1000 beds and currently 1/5 of them are occupied. This means that 1000*(1/5)=200 beds are occupied. Each day, 50 more patients are admitted, so the total number of occupied beds after one day will be 200+50=250. After two weeks (7 days), the total number of occupied beds will be 250*7=1750. Therefore, the total number of unoccupied beds in the hospital after two weeks is 1000-1750=-750, which is closest to choice C) 100.
