2025-12-24 18:07:40 | INFO | Q44 id=gsm8k_mcq_00043 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=If a 300g bag of chips has 5 servings and each serving contains 250 calories, then the total number of calories in the bag is:\n\n300g x 250calories/serving = 7500 calories\n\nIf your daily calorie target is 2000 calories and you have already consumed 1800 calories, then you have consumed 2000 - 1800 = 200 calories less than your daily target.\n\nTo determine how many grams of chips you can eat, we need to divide the total number of calories in the bag by the number of calories per gram:\n\n7500 calories / 250 calories/g = 300 grams\n\nTherefore, you can eat 300 grams of chips if your daily calorie target is 2000 and you have already consumed 1800 calories.\n\nSo the correct answer is C) 300.
