2025-12-24 18:08:20 | INFO | Q64 id=gsm8k_mcq_00063 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=We can reason about this problem as follows:\n- The streaming service charges $140 per month for 12 months, so for the first six months, Aleena pays $140 x 6 = $840\n- For the second six months, the streaming service charges her 10% less money than the previous six months. Since 10% is equal to 0.1, we can calculate 0.1 x $840 = $84\n- Therefore, for the second six months, Aleena pays $840 - $84 = $756\n- Adding up the amounts she paid for the first six months and the second six months, we get $840 + $756 = $1596\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 1596.
