2025-12-24 18:08:51 | INFO | Q86 id=gsm8k_mcq_00085 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate that Gene has been vacationing for 34 - 23 = 11 years. Since each row is made of blocks from a different year of vacations, and he goes on four vacations a year, he has 4 * 11 = 44 blocks in total. Therefore, the answer is D) 44.
2025-12-24 18:08:52 | INFO | Q77 id=gsm8k_mcq_00076 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The information given tells us that Cecilia needs to feed the puppy 1 cup of dog food every day for the first 180 days, and then 2 cups of dog food every day for the rest of its life. We also know that each bag of dog food contains 110 cups.\nTo find out how many bags of dog food Cecilia will need in the first year, we need to calculate how many cups of dog food the puppy will need in total over the course of the first year. The first 180 days is equal to 180/365 = 0.5 years. Since the puppy will need 1 cup of dog food per day for the first 180 days, it will need a total of 180 x 1 = 180 cups of dog food during this time period.\nAfter the first 180 days, the puppy will need 2 cups of dog food per day for the rest of its life. Since there are 365 days in a year, this means the puppy will need 2 cups of dog food per day for approximately 365 - 180 = 185 days. Therefore, the puppy will need a total of 180 + 185 = 365 cups of dog food over the course of the first year.\nSince each bag of dog food contains 110 cups, Cecilia will need 365 / 110 = 3.32 bags of dog food in the first year. However, since we cannot purchase fractional bags of dog food, we must round up to the nearest whole number. Therefore, Cecilia will need 4 bags of dog food in the first year.\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) 4.
