2025-12-24 18:10:04 | INFO | Q123 id=gsm8k_mcq_00122 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, Sadie slept 8 hours on Monday and then slept 2 hours less for the next two days, so she slept 8 - 2 = 6 hours each day for those two days. Therefore, she slept a total of 6 + 6 = 12 hours for those two days. If she slept 1 hour more than that for the rest of the week, she would have slept 12 + 1 = 13 hours per day for the rest of the week. Since there are 7 days in a week, Sadie slept a total of 13 * 7 = 91 hours throughout the week.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
