2025-12-24 18:10:23 | INFO | Q130 id=gsm8k_mcq_00129 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The hospital makes $10000 from these visits. \n\nTo calculate the profit, we need to find out how much revenue the hospital receives from each patient. Since each patient is seen for an average of 24 minutes at a cost of $150 per hour, the hospital earns $150 x 24 = $360 per patient.\n\nSince the hospital charges the patients $200 per hour, they receive $200 x 24 = $480 per patient.\n\nTherefore, the hospital's profit per patient is ($480 - $360) = $120. \n\nSince the hospital sees 500 patients per day, their total daily revenue is 500 x $120 = $60000.\n\nTherefore, the hospital makes a profit of $60000 - $50000 = $10000 from these visits. \n\nThus, the correct answer is B) $10000.
2025-12-24 18:10:24 | INFO | Q139 id=gsm8k_mcq_00138 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred= | followup_correct=False | raw=We can set up an equation for the total number of questions Mark answered between the two tests. Let x be the number of questions Mark answered during the first test. Then, during the second test, he answered 100 - x questions. Since he completed both tests at a rate of 5 questions per hour, we can say that x/5 + (100 - x)/5 = 8 + 6, which simplifies to x + 200 - x = 44, or 200 = 44, which is not true. This means that our initial assumption was incorrect, and there must be some other factor affecting the completion time of the tests. Without more information, it is impossible to determine exactly how many questions Mark left incomplete. Therefore, the answer is unknown.
