2025-12-24 18:10:28 | INFO | Q141 id=gsm8k_mcq_00140 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the percentage of semi-automatic cars as follows:\n\nTotal number of cars = 20\nNumber of automatic cars = 12\nNumber of manual cars = 4\n\nNumber of semi-automatic cars = Total - Number of automatic cars - Number of manual cars\n= 20 - 12 - 4\n= 4\n\nTherefore, the percentage of semi-automatic cars is:\n\nNumber of semi-automatic cars / Total number of cars * 100%\n= 4 / 20 * 100%\n= 20%\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 20.
