2025-12-24 18:10:35 | INFO | Q146 id=gsm8k_mcq_00145 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate that John has a total of 10 x 100 = 1000 pineapples. Since he can harvest his pineapples every three months, he will be able to harvest 1000 / 3 = 333.33 pineapples per quarter. Therefore, within a year, John can harvest 333.33 x 4 = 1333.33 pineapples.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (D) 4000.
