2025-12-24 18:12:02 | INFO | Q189 id=gsm8k_mcq_00188 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=We can set up an equation for the total revenue generated from selling the bags. Let B be the number of bags sold. We know that the revenue is equal to the selling price times the number of bags sold, so we have:\n\n30B = 400 + 2B\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\n28B = 400\n\nDividing both sides by 28, we get:\n\nB = 14.2865\n\nHowever, since we cannot sell a fraction of a bag, we must round down to the nearest whole number. Therefore, the trader sold 14 bags.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
