2025-12-24 18:12:22 | INFO | Q205 id=gsm8k_mcq_00204 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=After buying 6 bags of blue pens and 2 bags of red pens, Janet has:\n\n22 green pens + 10 yellow pens + 6 x 9 blue pens + 2 x 6 red pens = 22 + 10 + 54 + 12 = 98 pens\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 98.
2025-12-24 18:12:24 | INFO | Q202 id=gsm8k_mcq_00201 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate John's annual salary for the year he received the award as follows:\n\nFirst, we need to determine the amount of his raise. Since his salary will increase by 5% after receiving the award, we can calculate his raise as follows:\n\n5% of $2000 = $100\n\nSo, his new weekly salary will be:\n\n$2000 + $100 = $2100\n\nSince there are 52 weeks in a year, we can calculate John's total annual salary for the year as follows:\n\n$2100 x 52 = $114,200\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) $114,200.\n\nNote: We assume that John received the award on the first day of the year and worked for the entire year without any vacation or sick leave. Also, we assume that John's salary is paid weekly and that the raise takes effect immediately after receiving the award.
