2025-12-24 18:14:29 | INFO | Q271 id=gsm8k_mcq_00270 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of M&Ms Mary bought is the sum of the number of M&Ms in each of the three bags. We can find this by adding the number of M&Ms in each bag together.\n\nThe first bag has 300 M&Ms.\nThe second bag has 12 more M&Ms than the first, which means it has 300 + 12 = 312 M&Ms.\nThe third bag has half as many M&Ms as the first bag, which means it has 300 / 2 = 150 M&Ms.\n\nTherefore, the total number of M&Ms Mary bought is:\n\n300 + 312 + 150 = 762\n\nSo the correct answer is B) 762.
