2025-12-24 18:15:07 | INFO | Q288 id=gsm8k_mcq_00287 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The total number of stars on the flag is 76. We can break this down into groups of 8, 6, and 5 stars as follows:\n\n  * 3 rows of 8 stars = 24 stars\n  * 2 rows of 6 stars = 12 stars\n  * 5 rows of 5 stars = 25 stars\n\nTherefore, there are a total of 24 + 12 + 25 = 61 stars on the flag that are not 5 stars. Since the flag has 76 stars, there must be 76 - 61 = 15 rows of 5 stars.\n\nHence, the answer is (D).
2025-12-24 18:15:10 | INFO | Q297 id=gsm8k_mcq_00296 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The given information states that each member of the household consumes 0.2 kg of rice every meal, and there are five members in the household. Therefore, the total amount of rice consumed by the household per day is:\n\n5 members × 0.2 kg/person = 1 kg\n\nSince there are two meals a day (lunch and dinner), the total amount of rice consumed by the household per week is:\n\n2 meals × 1 kg/meal = 2 kg\n\nTherefore, a 42 kg bag of rice will last for:\n\n42 kg ÷ 2 kg/week = 21 weeks\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 21.
2025-12-24 18:15:12 | INFO | Q299 id=gsm8k_mcq_00298 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=We can reason that the price of the desk increases by $50 after each bid, so after three other people bid once, the price will be $200 + 3 * $50 = $350\. Since Carmen bids after each of these three people and wins, she ends up paying $350 for the desk. Therefore, the correct answer is D) 350.
2025-12-24 18:15:15 | INFO | Q290 id=gsm8k_mcq_00289 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The information given tells us that the car in the fast lane traveled 60 mph for 480 miles. To find the time it took the car in the slow lane to travel the same distance, we need to first convert the speed of the car in the slow lane from miles per hour to meters per second. We can do this by multiplying the speed by 2.2369: 60 mph * 2.2369 = 134.57 m/s.\n\nNext, we can use the formula for distance equals rate times time to find the time it took the car in the slow lane to travel 480 miles:\n\ndistance = rate x time\n\nWe know the distance traveled by the car in the fast lane is 480 miles, so we can set up the equation as follows:\n\n480 = 134.57 m/s x time\n\nTo solve for time, we divide both sides of the equation by 134.57 m/s:\n\ntime = 480 / 134.57 m/s\n\nSimplifying the right side gives:\n\ntime = 3.67 hours\n\nTherefore, the car in the slow lane took approximately 3.67 hours to travel 480 miles. The answer is C).
2025-12-24 18:15:15 | INFO | Q301 id=gsm8k_mcq_00300 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=On Tuesday, Peter has to exercise double the amount of time he did on Monday, which is 2 * 16 = 32 minutes. He also has to exercise double the amount of time he did on Sunday, which is 2 * 23 = 46 minutes. Therefore, Peter has to exercise a total of 32 + 46 = 78 minutes on Tuesday to reach his goal.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (B).
2025-12-24 18:15:17 | INFO | Q292 id=gsm8k_mcq_00291 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of chocolate bars is 8 packets * 5 chocolate bars = 40 chocolate bars. The adults will get 40 chocolate bars - 6 chocolate bars per adult = 34 chocolate bars. The children will get 34 chocolate bars / 8 children = 4 chocolate bars per child.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
2025-12-24 18:15:18 | INFO | Q303 id=gsm8k_mcq_00302 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation to represent the amount of money Annika spent on food and snacks. Let X be the amount she spent on food and snacks. We know that X/2 = $50 - $10, so X = $50 - $10 * 2 = $30.\n\nTherefore, Annika has $50 - $30 = $20 left.\n\nThe answer is A) 25.
2025-12-24 18:15:21 | INFO | Q294 id=gsm8k_mcq_00293 | baseline_pred=D | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=After the third round, Mike has 21 points, so Jim has 21 - 3 = 18 points. Tony has 2 * 21 = 42 points. In the fourth round, Mike gets an extra point for having over 20 points, so he has 21 + 1 = 22 points. Jim also gets an extra point for having over 20 points, so he has 18 + 1 = 19 points. Tony does not get an extra point because he already has 42 points. Therefore, all three players have a total of 22 + 19 + 42 = 83 points after the extra points had been distributed. The answer is A) 83.
2025-12-24 18:15:22 | INFO | Q305 id=gsm8k_mcq_00304 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate Watson's earnings for the entire month by multiplying his hourly rate by the number of hours he works each week and then adding his bonus for the month.\nAssuming there are 4 weeks in a month, Watson works 10 hours per day x 5 days per week = 50 hours per week. So he works a total of 50 hours x 4 weeks = 200 hours in April.\nHis earnings for the month would be $10 per hour x 200 hours = $2000.\nTherefore, Watson made $2000 in April if the company performed very well for the whole month.\n选 A.
2025-12-24 18:15:24 | INFO | Q307 id=gsm8k_mcq_00306 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=In the morning, 60 x 2 / 3 = 40 loaves of bread are sold. So, 60 - 40 = 20 loaves of bread are left. Half of it will be sold in the afternoon and evening, so 20 / 2 = 10 loaves of bread are sold in the afternoon.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
2025-12-24 18:15:27 | INFO | Q310 id=gsm8k_mcq_00309 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=We can reason that after 3 days, the person will grow 2 extra limbs (1 arm + 1 leg). After another 5 days, 2 more extra limbs will grow (1 arm + 1 leg). Therefore, in total after 15 days, the person will grow 4 extra limbs (2 arms + 2 legs). So the answer is C) 7.
2025-12-24 18:15:28 | INFO | Q296 id=gsm8k_mcq_00295 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total count of the activities Darren has done in the two days is:\n\nOn the first day, he did 100 pushups + 50 squats + 20 dumbbell presses = 170 exercises\n\nOn the second day, he did 20 more pushups than on the first day, which is 20 + 100 = 120 pushups. So, he did a total of 120 + 170 = 290 pushups. Additionally, he did 10 fewer squats than on the first day, which is 50 - 10 = 40 squats. And he doubled the number of dumbbell presses, so he did 2 x 20 = 40 dumbbell presses. Therefore, on the second day, he did a total of 40 + 40 = 80 exercises.\n\nSo, the total count of the activities Darren has done in the two days is 290 + 80 = 370 exercises.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 370.
2025-12-24 18:15:31 | INFO | Q312 id=gsm8k_mcq_00311 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The family consumes 3 * 5 = 15 eggs from the three people eating three eggs each day. The remaining 2 * 5 = 10 eggs are consumed by the other two members who eat two eggs each day. Therefore, the family consumes a total of 15 + 10 = 25 eggs in a week. The answer is not among the given choices, but the closest choice would be A) 70, which is obtained by multiplying 25 by 7. However, since we are required to choose only one letter, we cannot select A) as our answer.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 65, which is obtained by subtracting 25 from 70.
2025-12-24 18:15:33 | INFO | Q298 id=gsm8k_mcq_00297 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=We can subtract the number of crates sold each day from the total target to find out how many crates Sam was off from his target for the week.\n\nOn Monday and Friday, Sam was closed, so he did not sell any crates. On Tuesday, he sold 15 crates. On Wednesday, he sold 12 crates. On Thursday, he sold 18 crates. On Friday, he was closed again, so he did not sell any more crates. Adding up all the sales gives us:\n\n15 + 12 + 18 = 45 crates\n\nThe total target for the week is 120 crates, so Sam was 120 - 45 = 75 crates off from his target for the week.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 75.
2025-12-24 18:15:34 | INFO | Q314 id=gsm8k_mcq_00313 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Noah was 46 - 6 = 40 years old six years ago. Three thousand times the age of Noah is 3000 * 40 = 120000. The population of Chile six years ago was 120000 / 2 = 60000. Chile's current population is 60000 * 2 = 120000.\n\nThe answer is (B).
2025-12-24 18:15:37 | INFO | Q300 id=gsm8k_mcq_00299 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The cost of driving can be calculated as follows:\nNumber of miles driven per week = 70 miles (5 days x 14 miles per day)\nNumber of miles driven per year = 70 x 50 = 3,500 miles\nTotal cost of driving = $2 per mile x 3,500 miles = $7,000\n加上每月给司机的奖金$150，每年总共给司机的奖金=12个月 x $150 = $1,800\n所以，他每年需要支付的总费用为$7,000 + $1,800 = $8,800。\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
