2025-12-24 18:16:12 | INFO | Q331 id=gsm8k_mcq_00330 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The customer received $1 in rewards for every $20 they spent, so for their $80 shopping trip, they would receive $4 in rewards. They spent $43 on this trip, so they would use $4 in rewards + $4 in coupons = $8 in savings. The original price of the items was $80, so with the $8 in savings, the customer paid $80 - $8 = $72 on this shopping trip.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (B).
2025-12-24 18:16:15 | INFO | Q333 id=gsm8k_mcq_00332 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The number of unmanned ruined castles in Scotland can be calculated as follows:\n\nOut of 220 castles in Scotland, 40% are ruins, which means 40/100 * 220 = 88.\n\nOut of the 88 ruined castles, half of them are unmanned, which means 88/2 = 44.\n\nTherefore, there are 44 unmanned ruined castles in Scotland.\n\nAnswer: C) 88
