2025-12-24 18:16:53 | INFO | Q342 id=gsm8k_mcq_00341 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred= | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation for the total weight of the animals in the container:\n\n50 + [the weight of the other three animals] = 20 + 20\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\n50 + [the weight of the other three animals] = 40\n\nSubtracting 50 from both sides, we get:\n\n[the weight of the other three animals] = 40 - 50\n\nSimplifying this expression, we get:\n\n-10\n\nThis means that the total weight of the other three animals is negative, which is not possible since weight cannot be negative. This indicates that there must be an error in the problem statement or the calculations.\n\nTherefore, I cannot provide an accurate answer to this question with the given information.
