2025-12-24 18:18:04 | INFO | Q390 id=gsm8k_mcq_00389 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by calculating the total cost of the rides that David and Dasha will take if they each buy a single ticket:\n\nDavid + Dasha = 2 + 2 = 4 tickets\n\nSo the total cost of the tickets would be:\n\n4 tickets * $2/ticket = $8\n\nNow let's calculate the total cost of the ride bracelet:\n\n$30\n\nFinally, we subtract the cost of the tickets from the total cost of the ride bracelet to find out how much David saves:\n\n$30 - $8 = $22\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) $6.
