2025-12-24 18:18:07 | INFO | Q407 id=gsm8k_mcq_00406 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\n2x = 40 (twice as many corns as cannoli)\nx = 20 (number of corns)\n\nAllan bought 60 more cannoli, so he now has:\n\n40 + 60 = 100 cannoli\n\nHe also bought 40 fewer corns than the number of cannoli, so he now has:\n\n20 - 40 = -20 corns\n\nHowever, this cannot be the answer since we cannot have a negative number of corns. There must be an error in the problem statement or the calculation.\n\nTherefore, I cannot provide an answer with the given information.
2025-12-24 18:18:11 | INFO | Q394 id=gsm8k_mcq_00393 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=To calculate the percentage of time Carol spent editing, we need to first find out how many hours and minutes she spent in total on all three activities. We can do this by adding the number of hours and minutes for each activity:\n\n4 hours + 0.5 hours + 90 minutes = 4.5 hours\n\nNext, we can divide the amount of time Carol spent editing by the total amount of time she spent on all three activities, and multiply the result by 100% to express the answer as a percentage:\n\n90 minutes / 4.5 hours * 100% = 20%\n\nTherefore, Carol spent 20% of her total work time editing.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is A) 20.
2025-12-24 18:18:11 | INFO | Q409 id=gsm8k_mcq_00408 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=We can calculate how long it will take Toby to read the book by dividing the number of pages by the average number of words per page: 45 pages / 200 words/page = 0.225 hours. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, this equals 12 minutes. Toby needs to read for 12 minutes + 10 minutes to get to the airport = 22 minutes. Since he reads at a rate of 300 words per minute, he will finish the book in 22 minutes. Therefore, he will arrive at the airport 60 minutes - 22 minutes = 38 minutes early.\n\nThe answer is D.
