2025-12-24 18:18:28 | INFO | Q417 id=gsm8k_mcq_00416 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by setting up an equation to represent the number of dromedaries in the herd. Let x be the number of dromedaries. Since each dromedary has one hump, we can say that the total number of bumps from dromedaries is x. Similarly, since each camel has two humps, the total number of bumps from camels is 2y, where y is the number of camels.\n\nSince there are 180 heads in the herd, we can write:\n\nx + 2y = 180\n\nAnd since there are 304 bumps in the herd, we can write:\n\nx + y = 304\n\nSubstituting the first equation into the second equation, we get:\n\n2y + y = 304\n3y = 304\ny = 101\n\nNow we know that there are 101 camels in the herd. Substituting this value into the first equation, we get:\n\nx + 2(101) = 180\nx + 202 = 180\nx = -22\n\nHowever, we cannot have a negative number of dromedaries, so this solution does not make sense. It's possible that there was an error in the problem statement or the calculation.\n\nTherefore, I do not have enough information to give a definitive answer to this question.
2025-12-24 18:18:29 | INFO | Q406 id=gsm8k_mcq_00405 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=To find out how much money Tyson would spend on the meat and cheese, we need to calculate the total amount of meat and cheese needed to make 20 sandwiches. Since each sandwich requires 1 pound of meat and cheese, we need 20 pounds of meat and 20 pounds of cheese.\n\nThe meat costs $7.00 per pound, so 20 pounds of meat will cost 20 * $7 = $140.00.\n\nThe cheese costs $3.00 per pound, so 20 pounds of cheese will cost 20 * $3 = $60.00.\n\nTherefore, Tyson would spend a total of $140.00 + $60.00 = $200.00 on the meat and cheese to make enough sandwiches to serve 20 people.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 70.
