2025-12-24 18:18:48 | INFO | Q429 id=gsm8k_mcq_00428 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation based on the information given. Let x be the number of guests who got exactly one hot dog. Then, 36 - 2x is the number of guests who got two hot dogs. Since everyone who showed up wanted a second hotdog, we can set up the equation:\n\n36 - 2x = 40\n\nSolving this equation gives us:\n\n2x = 4\nx = 2\n\nTherefore, 22 guests got exactly one hot dog. So, the number of guests who did not get a second hotdog is:\n\n36 - 22 = 14\n\nThus, the answer is C) 14.\n\nTherefore, the total number of guests who did not get a second hotdog is 14.
