2025-12-24 18:21:32 | INFO | Q533 id=gsm8k_mcq_00532 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation for the age of Jame's cousin in 8 years. Let x be the current age of Jame's cousin. In 8 years, he will be x + 8 years old. Also, we know that in 8 years, his cousin will be 5 years younger than twice his age, which can be written as x + 8 = 2x - 5. Solving this equation gives us x = 13, so Jame's cousin is currently 13 years old.\n\nNow we can use the given information to find out how many years separate the ages of Jame and his cousin now. If Jame is 27 years old in 5 years, then he is currently 27 - 5 = 22 years old. Since Jame's cousin is currently 13 years old, the difference between their ages is 22 - 13 = 9 years.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 9.
2025-12-24 18:21:34 | INFO | Q514 id=gsm8k_mcq_00513 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by setting up an equation representing Julie's initial amount of money as 500:\n\n500 = A\n\nWhere A represents the initial amount of money Julie had.\n\nNext, we find out how much she spent on clothes:\n\n20% × 500 = 100\n\nSo she spent 100 dollars on clothes.\n\nNow we subtract that amount from her original amount of money to find out how much is left:\n\n500 - 100 = 400\n\nFinally, we find out how much she spent on CDs:\n\n25% × 300 = 75\n\nSo she spent 75 dollars on CDs.\n\nTo find out how much money Julie has left, we subtract the amount she spent on clothes and CDs from her initial amount of money:\n\n400 - 75 - 100 = 225\n\nTherefore, Julie has 225 dollars left.\n\nThe answer is C) 300.
2025-12-24 18:21:35 | INFO | Q535 id=gsm8k_mcq_00534 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=The information given is that the boys brought back 60 shells each and the girls brought an amount equal to the number of shells brought by the boys plus four times as many seashells as the boys. We can set up an equation to represent this information:\n\n60 = x + 4 * 60\n\nwhere x represents the number of shells brought by the girls.\n\nSolving for x, we get:\n\n60 = 60 + 240\n60 = 300\n\nTherefore, the girls brought 300 seashells each.\n\nAnswer: D) 300
2025-12-24 18:21:36 | INFO | Q516 id=gsm8k_mcq_00515 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate Tara's profit as follows:\n\nTara bought 8 packs × 5 canvas bags = 40 canvas bags\nShe earned $8 per bag × 40 bags = $320\n\nTherefore, the profit Tara earned on her bags is $320 - $40 = $280.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) $32.
