2025-12-24 18:21:50 | INFO | Q545 id=gsm8k_mcq_00544 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\nJeff + Brad = 100\nJeff = 4 * Brad\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\n4 * Brad + Brad = 100\n5 * Brad = 100\nBrad = 20\n\nNow we can find out how much Jeff gets by multiplying his value by 4:\n\nJeff = 4 * 20 = 80\n\nTherefore, Jeff gets $80 in dollars.\n\nThe answer is (C).
