2025-12-24 18:21:55 | INFO | Q547 id=gsm8k_mcq_00546 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by finding out how many times Elise writes each letter of the alphabet. Since she writes the alphabet in full twice, we can say that she writes each letter twice. Additionally, she writes half of the alphabet once, which means she writes each letter once and a half. Therefore, the total number of letters that Elise writes is:\n\n2 (full alphabet) + 1 (half of the alphabet) = 3\n\nHowever, since Elise also re-writes everything she has already written, we need to add one more time for each letter she has written. Let's assume that Elise has written 10 letters so far. Then, she will rewrite those 10 letters plus the additional 3 letters she wrote earlier, for a total of 13 letters.\n\nTherefore, the total number of letters that Elise has written is 13. The answer is B) 130.
2025-12-24 18:21:57 | INFO | Q528 id=gsm8k_mcq_00527 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The information given is that one person can paint half a house in five days. We need to determine how long it would take for five people to paint a whole house.\n\nTo do this, we can divide the time it takes for one person to paint half a house by two. Since half a house is equal to one quarter of a house, we can say that one person can paint one quarter of a house in one day. \n\nTherefore, if one person can paint half a house in five days, they can paint one quarter of a house in one day. To paint a whole house, which is four quarters, it would take four times as long. So, it would take four days for five people to paint a whole house.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 48.
