2025-12-24 18:22:47 | INFO | Q562 id=gsm8k_mcq_00561 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The total weight of Mark and Susan is 150 + 20 = 170 pounds. Bob's weight is twice that of Susan, so Bob weighs 2 * 20 = 40 pounds. The total weight of all three friends is 170 + 40 = 210 pounds. The average weight per person is 210 / 3 = 70 pounds. The answer is A) 180.
2025-12-24 18:22:50 | INFO | Q564 id=gsm8k_mcq_00563 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate that each candle costs $3/5 = $0.6. Since James has two sons, he needs to buy 2 * $0.6 = $1.2 worth of candles. Therefore, James spends $1.2 on candles.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (B).
2025-12-24 18:22:51 | INFO | Q578 id=gsm8k_mcq_00577 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the total number of birds that Mack saw over the week as follows:\n\nOn days one and two, Mack saw a total of 50 birds + 50 birds = 100 birds.\n\nOn day three, he saw none, so we add zero to the total.\n\nOn days four and five, he saw 120 birds + 120 birds = 240 birds.\n\nOn day six, he saw 20 birds, so we add twenty to the total.\n\nOn day seven, he saw 90 birds, so we add ninety to the total.\n\nThe total number of birds that Mack saw over the week is 100 birds + zero + 240 birds + twenty + ninety = 389 birds.\n\nTherefore, the average number of birds that Mack saw per day is 389 birds / 7 days = 55.57 birds per day.\n\nSince we cannot have a fraction of a bird, we round down to 55 birds per day. Therefore, the answer is closest to option D) 40.\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 40.
2025-12-24 18:22:52 | INFO | Q580 id=gsm8k_mcq_00579 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The boy has 5 cards, and his brother has 3 fewer cards than he has, so the brother must have 5 - 3 = 2 cards. Therefore, they have 5 + 2 = 7 cards together. The answer is A) 7.
2025-12-24 18:22:52 | INFO | Q567 id=gsm8k_mcq_00566 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=We can set up an equation to represent the situation. Let X be the age of Shiloh's nephew. In 7 years, Shiloh will be 44 + 7 = 51 years old. At that time, Shiloh’s nephew will be 51 / 3 = 17 years old. Therefore, his nephew is currently 17 - 7 = 10 years old. So the answer is D) 10.
