2025-12-24 18:24:51 | INFO | Q651 id=gsm8k_mcq_00650 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=On Tuesday, Clara bought 20 pomegranates at $20 each, so she paid 20 x $20 = $400. She got $2 off because she had a voucher, so her final payment was $400 - $2 = $398. The next day, the price shot to $30 per fruit, so she would have paid 20 x $30 = $600. However, the store also offered a 10% discount on the total cost, which amounted to $600 x 10 / 100 = $60 discount. So, her final payment for the next day was $600 - $60 = $540. Therefore, the difference between the final prices paid for the pomegranates on the two days is $540 - $398 = $142.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (B).
