2025-12-24 18:24:55 | INFO | Q634 id=gsm8k_mcq_00633 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=We can use the formula for relative speed to solve this problem. The relative speed of two objects is the ratio of their speeds.\n\nRelative speed = (Tom's speed) / (Bob's speed)\n\nIn this case:\n\nRelative speed = (70 mph) / (55 mph) = 1.29\n\nThis means that Tom is driving at a speed 1.29 times faster than Bob's speed.\n\nTo find how long it will take Tom to catch up with Bob, we can use the formula:\n\nTime = Distance / Speed\n\nThe distance between Bob and Tom is 75 miles. We can assume that they are driving in a straight line, so their distance apart remains constant.\n\nTime = 75 miles / (70 mph + 55 mph) = 75 miles / (125 mph) = 0.6 hours\n\nTherefore, it will take Tom 0.6 hours to catch up with Bob.\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 5.
