2025-12-24 18:25:22 | INFO | Q648 id=gsm8k_mcq_00647 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=False | raw=The total distance Bill needs to dig is 24 feet of soil + 8 feet of clay = 32 feet. He can dig 4 feet per hour through soil, so it will take him 32 feet / 4 feet per hour = 8 hours to dig through the soil. He can dig half as fast through clay, which means it will take him 8 hours * 0.5 = 4 hours to dig through the clay. Therefore, it will take Bill a total of 8 + 4 = 12 hours to dig the well.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (B).
