2025-12-24 18:25:38 | INFO | Q680 id=gsm8k_mcq_00679 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=The given information states that 6 potatoes can make 36 hash browns. To find out how many hash browns can be made out of 96 potatoes, we need to divide the number of potatoes by the number of hash browns per potato.\nSo, if 6 potatoes make 36 hash browns, then 1 potato makes 36 / 6 = 6 hash browns.\nTherefore, to find out how many hash browns can be made out of 96 potatoes, we simply need to multiply the number of potatoes by the number of hash browns per potato.\nSo, 96 potatoes can make 96 x 6 = 576 hash browns.\nHence, the correct answer is B) 576.
