2025-12-24 18:25:46 | INFO | Q682 id=gsm8k_mcq_00681 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=To solve this problem, we need to use the given information to find out how many cookies each person has.\n\nFirst, we know that Katarina has 5 fewer cookies than Max. We can represent this as:\n\nMax = Katarina + 5\n\nNext, we know that Max has 12 more cookies than the Cookie Monster. We can represent this as:\n\nCookie Monster = Max - 12\n\nFinally, we know that Summer has 23 more cookies than Max. We can represent this as:\n\nSummer = Max + 23\n\nUsing these equations, we can substitute the values we know into them to find out how many cookies each person has:\n\nMax = Katarina + 5 Max = (Cookie Monster - 12) + 5 Max = Cookie Monster - 7 Max = 61\n\nSummer = Max + 23 Summer = 61 + 23 Summer = 84\n\nNow we know that Max has 61 cookies, Summer has 84 cookies, and Katarina has 68 cookies. To find out how many cookies they have in total, we can add up their numbers:\n\nTotal = Max + Summer + Katarina Total = 61 + 84 + 68 Total = 203\n\nTherefore, the total number of cookies that Katarina, Max, and Summer have is 203. The answer is not among the choices given, so we cannot be certain which letter represents the correct answer.
