2025-12-24 18:26:22 | INFO | Q710 id=gsm8k_mcq_00709 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The rate at which the ice cream factory produces chocolate ice cream is 100 quarts / 2 hours = 50 quarts/hour. The rate at which it produces vanilla ice cream is 50 quarts / 4 hours = 12.5 quarts/hour. In 48 hours, the factory will produce chocolate ice cream at a rate of 50 quarts/hour for 48 hours for a total of 2400 quarts. It will also produce vanilla ice cream at a rate of 12.5 quarts/hour for 48 hours for a total of 560 quarts. In total, the factory will produce 2400 + 560 = 2960 quarts of ice cream in 48 hours.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
