2025-12-24 18:26:55 | INFO | Q727 id=gsm8k_mcq_00726 | baseline_pred=B | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=To find the length of one of Bobby's shoes, we can set up the following equation:\n\n8 feet and 4 inches = 9 times the length of one of Bobby's shoes + 10 inches\n\nWe can simplify this equation by multiplying both sides by 12 inches (since there are 12 inches in one foot):\n\n96 inches = 9 times the length of one of Bobby's shoes + 120 inches\n\nSubtracting 120 inches from both sides gives us:\n\n-34 inches = 9 times the length of one of Bobby's shoes\n\nDividing both sides by 9 gives us:\n\n-4 inches = the length of one of Bobby's shoes\n\nTherefore, the length of one of Bobby's shoes is 4 inches.\n\nSo the answer is D) 8.2.
