2025-12-24 18:27:39 | INFO | Q739 id=gsm8k_mcq_00738 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start with the given information:\n\n- Alice has six more books than Steven.\n- Clara has two times as many books as Steven.\n\nFrom this, we can infer that:\n\n- Alice has 6 + x = y books, where x is the number of books Steven has and y is the number of books Alice has.\n- Clara has 2y = 20 books.\n\nSubstituting the second equation into the first equation, we get:\n\n- 6 + x = 2(6 + x)\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n- 6 + x = 12 + 2x\n\nSubtracting 6 from both sides, we get:\n\n- x = 6\n\nTherefore, Alice has 6 + 6 = 12 books. And Clara has 20 = 2 * 12 = 24 books. \n\nSo, Clara has 24 - 12 = 12 more books than Alice. The answer is A) 12.
2025-12-24 18:27:40 | INFO | Q758 id=gsm8k_mcq_00757 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by organizing the information given in the problem:\n\n11 students need size extra-small\nTwice as many students need size small as extra small = 2 * 11 = 22 students\nFour less than the number of size small students need size medium = 22 - 4 = 18 students\nHalf as many students need size large as size medium = 18 / 2 = 9 students\nSix more students need size extra-large than large = 9 + 6 = 15 students\n\nNow we can add up the number of shirts needed for each size:\n\nSize extra-small: 11\nSize small: 22\nSize medium: 18\nSize large: 9\nSize extra-large: 15\n\nTherefore, the total number of shirts Krissa ordered is:\n\n11 + 22 + 18 + 9 + 15 = 75\n\nSo the answer is B) 75.
