2025-12-24 18:28:58 | INFO | Q773 id=gsm8k_mcq_00772 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=To solve this problem, we need to first find out how much time Tatiana spends reading and playing video games. We can do this by setting up a proportion:\n\nTime spent reading + Time spent playing video games = Total time available\n\nWe know that Tatiana reads for 3 hours and plays video games for 1/3 of the remaining time, so we can set up another proportion:\n\n3 + 1/3x = 7 + 5\nMultiplying both sides by 3 gives:\n\n9 + x = 22\nSubtracting 9 from both sides gives:\n\nx = 13\n\nSo Tatiana spends 13 hours playing video games. This means she has 7 - 3 - 13 = -8 hours left for soccer. Since negative time doesn't make sense, we must have made a mistake somewhere. Let's check our calculations.\n\nWe divided the total time available (7 + 5 = 12) by the amount of time Tatiana spends reading (3), which gave us 4 as the result. However, if she reads for 3 hours and plays video games for 1/3 of the remaining time (which is 1 hour), then she should have 12 - 3 - 1 = 8 hours left for soccer. This means our initial calculation was incorrect.\n\nLet's try again. We divide the total time available (7 + 5 = 12) by the amount of time Tatiana spends reading (3), which gives us 4 as the result. Then we subtract the time she spends reading from the total time available to get 12 - 3 = 9 hours. Finally, we divide this remaining time by the amount of time Tatiana spends playing video games (1/3 of 9, which is 3 hours), giving us 9 - 3 = 6 hours left for soccer.\n\nTherefore, Tatiana spends 6/12 = 1/2 of her weekend playing soccer. This means she spends 1/2 * 7 = 3.5 hours playing soccer on Saturday and 1/2 * 5 = 2.5 hours playing soccer on Sunday, for a total of 6 hours over the weekend. This is closest to choice A, which is 50%.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 50%.
