2025-12-24 18:33:59 | INFO | Q977 id=gsm8k_mcq_00976 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the total number of gingerbread and apple pie boxes sold over the two days as follows:\n\nSaturday - 10 gingerbread boxes + 4 fewer apple pie boxes = 6 gingerbread boxes + 11 apple pie boxes\nSunday - 5 more gingerbread boxes + 15 apple pie boxes = 10 gingerbread boxes + 20 apple pie boxes\n\nSo, in total, Sunny sold 6 + 11 + 10 + 20 = 47 gingerbread boxes and 11 + 15 + 20 = 46 apple pie boxes.\n\nThe total earnings from gingerbread sales would be $6 x 47 = $282.\nThe total earnings from apple pie sales would be $15 x 46 = $705.\n\nTherefore, Sunny earned a total of $282 + $705 = $987 for two days.\n\nHence, the correct answer is B) 540.
