2025-12-24 18:34:08 | INFO | Q937 id=gsm8k_mcq_00936 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate the cost for a 12-hour stay as follows:\n\n12 hours * 1000 pesos = 12000 pesos\n\nFor an additional 8 hours, he chooses to pay 70 pesos per hour:\n\n8 hours * 70 pesos = 560 pesos\n\nSo the total cost for a 24-hour stay would be:\n\n12000 + 560 = 12560 pesos\n\nTherefore, the amount that Cameron saves by choosing the option of adding on 70 pesos for every additional hour is:\n\n12560 - 12000 = 560 pesos\n\nThus, the answer is (D) 250.\n\nTherefore, the total amount that Cameron saves is 250 pesos.
