2025-12-24 18:35:10 | INFO | Q1013 id=gsm8k_mcq_01012 | baseline_pred=B | gold=B | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the charge of the power bank when Maria left for the park as follows:\n\nInitially, the power bank was 100% charged.\n\nAfter charging her friend's phones for 5 hours, the power bank lost 9% of its total capacity per hour, so it lost 9% * 5 = 4.5% of its total capacity. Since the power bank had a total capacity of 100%, this means it had 100 - 4.5 = 95.5% of its capacity left.\n\nThree hours later, the battery started to lose 7% of its total capacity per hour instead of 9%. Since the power bank had already lost 4.5% of its capacity, it lost an additional 7% * 3 = 2.1% of its capacity. This means that the power bank now has 95.5 - 2.1 = 93.4% of its capacity left.\n\nFinally, the power bank had 28% of its capacity remaining after charging her friends' phones for 5 hours and then losing 2.1% of its capacity over the next three hours. Therefore, the charge of the power bank when Maria left for the park was approximately 93%.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) 92.
