2025-12-24 18:35:14 | INFO | Q1015 id=gsm8k_mcq_01014 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, Jamaar can buy $10 - ($3 + $4 + $2 + $5) = $9 worth of fruit. Out of these, he has already spent $3 + $4 + $2 + $5 = $14 on peaches, pears, kiwis, and apples. Therefore, he can buy $9 - $14 = -$5 worth of plums, which is equivalent to 5 plums. Since plums cost $.25 each, Jamaar can buy a maximum of 5 plums.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
