2025-12-24 18:35:26 | INFO | Q984 id=gsm8k_mcq_00983 | baseline_pred=C | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=True | raw=Based on the given information, we can set up the following equation:\n\nCharlie's boot size = 5 x Sophie's boot size\n\nIf Sophie wears size five boots, then the average size of shoe worn by the two would be:\n\nAverage shoe size = (Charlie's boot size + Sophie's boot size) / 2\n\nSubstituting the value we found for Charlie's boot size, we get:\n\nAverage shoe size = (5 x 5 + 5) / 2\nAverage shoe size = 30 / 2\nAverage shoe size = 15\n\nTherefore, the average size of shoe worn by the two is 15.\n\nAnswer: D) 15
