2025-12-24 18:35:36 | INFO | Q1027 id=gsm8k_mcq_01026 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=B | followup_correct=True | raw=We can start by calculating how much ore one dwarf can mine in a month with 30 days:\n\n12 pounds per day x 30 days = 360 pounds\n\nNow let's calculate how much ore one dwarf can mine with an iron pickaxe:\n\n12 pounds per day x 2 = 24 pounds per day\n\nSo, one dwarf can mine 24 pounds + 360 pounds = 384 pounds per month with an iron pickaxe.\n\nFinally, let's calculate how much ore one dwarf can mine with a steel pickaxe:\n\n24 pounds per day x 1.5 = 36 pounds per day\n\nSo, one dwarf can mine 36 pounds + 384 pounds = 420 pounds per month with a steel pickaxe.\n\nTherefore, 40 dwarves with steel pickaxes can mine 40 x 420 pounds = 16800 pounds of ore in a month with 30 days.\n\nThe correct answer is B) 43200.
2025-12-24 18:35:38 | INFO | Q992 id=gsm8k_mcq_00991 | baseline_pred=C | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=False | raw=The information given is that Bill saw the comet a second time when he was three times the age his father was when he saw the comet. We can use this information to find Bill's age at his first sighting of the comet.\n\nFirst, we need to determine how many years had passed since Bill's dad saw the comet. We know that Bill's dad saw the comet when he was 30 years old, so we can subtract that from now to find out how long it has been:\n\n2023 - 1953 = 70 years\n\nNext, we need to find out how old Bill was when he saw the comet for the first time. We know that Bill saw the comet a second time when he was three times the age his father was when he saw the comet. Since Bill's dad saw the comet when he was 30, that means Bill saw the comet for the first time when he was:\n\n30 * 3 = 90 years old\n\nTherefore, Bill was 90 years old when he saw the comet for the first time.\n\nWe can check our answer by looking at the choices: A) 15, B) 60, C) 90, D) 30. Only choice C, 90, matches the given information.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 90.
