2025-12-24 18:36:20 | INFO | Q1050 id=gsm8k_mcq_01049 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The number of Spanish books is the remaining percentage of the total number of books that are not English or German. \n\nSo, the number of Spanish books can be found by subtracting the percentage of English and German books from 100%.\n\nIn this case:\n\n50% (English) + 10% (German) = 60%\n\n60% - 60% (Spanish) = 0%\n\nTherefore, there are 0 Spanish books.\n\nHowever, since we need to choose a letter, we will select the closest option which is A) 20.
