2025-12-24 18:36:36 | INFO | Q1060 id=gsm8k_mcq_01059 | baseline_pred=C | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=The information given is that Imma feeds her cats twice a day with 60 grams of cat food, and we want to know how many days 720 grams of cat food will last. To solve this problem, we can set up an equation:\n\nNumber of days = (Total amount of cat food) / (Amount of cat food per day)\n\nPlugging in the values given, we get:\n\nNumber of days = (720 grams) / (60 grams per day)\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\nNumber of days = 12\n\nTherefore, 720 grams of cat food will last 12 days.\n\nSo the correct answer is D) 12.
