2025-12-24 18:38:11 | INFO | Q1085 id=gsm8k_mcq_01084 | baseline_pred=A | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The audio does not provide enough information to determine the answer with certainty. However, we can make some assumptions based on the given information.\n\nFirstly, it is stated that Harry will get 60 feet more than Sam. This means that Harry will receive 100 + 60 = 160 feet of fence. \n\nSince the total fence is 100 + 160 = 260 feet, we can assume that Sam will receive the remaining 260 - 160 = 100 feet of fence.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 30.
2025-12-24 18:38:11 | INFO | Q1108 id=gsm8k_mcq_01107 | baseline_pred=A | gold=A | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=True | raw=The problem states that 40% of the school population consists of 240 boys. To find the number of girls in the school, we need to first calculate 40% of the total school population.\n\nLet X be the total number of students in the school. Then, 40% of X = 0.4X.\n\nWe are given that 0.4X = 240, so:\n\nX = 240 / 0.4\nX = 600\n\nTherefore, the total number of students in the school is 600. Since 40% of the population is made up of 240 boys, the remaining 60% is made up of 600 - 240 = 360 girls.\n\nSo the answer is A) 360.
