2025-12-24 18:38:15 | INFO | Q1112 id=gsm8k_mcq_01111 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of balls is 3 + 11 + 25 = 49\. The revenue from selling red balls is 3 * 49 = $147\. The revenue from selling blue balls is 5 * 49 = $245\. The revenue from selling green balls is 3 * 49 = $147\. The total revenue from selling all the balls is 147 + 245 + 147 = $549\. The store will have received $549 after all the balls are sold.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
