2025-12-24 18:38:43 | INFO | Q1130 id=gsm8k_mcq_01129 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start by setting up an equation for each person's number of eggs. Let x be the number of eggs Arnold and Madeline painted. Therefore, we can write two equations:\n\nx + y = 56 (where y is the number of eggs Madeline and Arnold painted)\nx + z = 30 (where z is the number of eggs Sarah and Camden painted)\n\nSince we know that Camden painted 12 more eggs than Sarah, we can add 12 to the second equation to get:\n\nx + z = 30 + 12\n\nSubstituting the value from the first equation into the third equation, we get:\n\nx + (56 - x) = 42\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\n2x = 14\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\nx = 7\n\nTherefore, Arnold painted 7 eggs. To find out how many more eggs Camden painted than Arnold, we can subtract the number of eggs Arnold painted from the number of eggs Camden painted:\n\n30 - 7 = 23\n\nTherefore, Camden painted 23 more eggs than Arnold.\n\nThe answer is A) 13.
