2025-12-24 18:39:10 | INFO | Q1145 id=gsm8k_mcq_01144 | baseline_pred=B | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can begin by setting up an equation representing the total ratio of men to women on the bus as 5x + 9y = 84. Since there are 84 people on the bus, we can write 5x + 9y = 84.\n\nWe also know that 20 women alight from the bus at the next stop. This means that 84 - 20 = 64 women remain on the bus.\n\nSubstituting this value into our original equation, we get:\n\n5x + 9(64 - x) = 84\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n5x + 576 - 9x = 84\n-4x = -482\nx = 121\n\nNow that we know the value of x, we can find the value of y by substituting x back into the equation 5x + 9y = 84:\n\n5(121) + 9y = 84\n605 + 9y = 84\n9y = -141\ny = -15.67\n\nHowever, since y must be a whole number (since it represents the number of men remaining on the bus), we cannot have more than 15 men remaining on the bus. Therefore, the closest option would be 15.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 74.
