2025-12-24 18:39:54 | INFO | Q1140 id=gsm8k_mcq_01139 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=Based on the given information, we can calculate the cost of each bagel after the discount as follows:\n\nIf Russell orders 4 packs of bagels, he will receive a 10% discount. To find the total cost of the bagels after the discount, we need to first calculate the original price of the 4 packs of bagels:\n\n4 packs * $10/pack = $40\n\nTo find the discounted price, we multiply the original price by 90% (since there are 9 bagels in each pack and we get 10% off):\n\n$40 * 0.90 = $36\n\nNow that we know the discounted price, we can find the cost of each individual bagel by dividing the discounted price by the number of bagels in each pack:\n\n$36 / 9 bagels = $4 bagel\n\nTherefore, each single bagel will cost $4 after purchasing 4 packs of bagels with a 10% discount.\n\nThe answer is A) $1.00.
