2025-12-24 18:41:16 | INFO | Q1218 id=gsm8k_mcq_01217 | baseline_pred=B | gold=A | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=D | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate the total amount that Pauline spent on the museum visits as follows:\n\nFirst, we find out how much the cost of one visit increased after 5 years by multiplying the initial cost by 150%: $2 * 150% = $3\n\nSince Pauline visited the museum three times a year, she went to the museum 3 * 5 = 15 times in 5 years.\n\nTherefore, the total amount she spent on the museum visits in 5 years is: 15 * $2 + 3 = $33\n\nAfter another 3 years, during which the cost of one visit remained at $3, Pauline visited the museum another 3 * 3 = 9 times.\n\nTherefore, the total amount she spent on the museum visits over 8 years is: $33 + 9 * $3 = $57\n\nHence, the correct answer is D) 57.\n\nTherefore, Pauline spent $57 on all visits to the museum.
