2025-12-24 18:42:55 | INFO | Q1243 id=gsm8k_mcq_01242 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=incorrect | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=To solve this problem, we need to use some basic math. Let's start by finding out how many of the hats are red.\n\nWe know that half of the hats are red, so:\n\n100 / 2 = 50\n\nTherefore, there are 50 red hats.\n\nNow we need to find out how many of the remaining hats are blue. We can do this by subtracting the number of red hats from the total number of hats:\n\n100 - 50 = 50\n\nSo there are 50 hats left.\n\nNext, we need to find out how many of these 50 hats are blue. We can do this by multiplying the number of remaining hats by 3/5:\n\n50 x 3/5 = 30\n\nTherefore, there are 30 blue hats.\n\nFinally, we can subtract the number of red and blue hats from the total number of hats to find out how many white hats there are:\n\n100 - 50 - 30 = 20\n\nTherefore, Skyler has 20 white hats.\n\nBased on our reasoning, the correct answer is C) 20.
