2025-12-24 18:43:18 | INFO | Q1304 id=gsm8k_mcq_01303 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=It takes 14 days for Nate's dog to dig 6 * 14 = 84 holes. While Nate is on vacation, the dog digs 6 * 14 = 84 holes. When Nate comes back, they together dig 9 + 6 = 15 holes per day. It will take them 84 / 15 = 5.6 weeks to fill in all the holes.\n\nThe answer is (C).
