2025-12-24 18:44:11 | INFO | Q1285 id=gsm8k_mcq_01284 | baseline_pred=D | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The number of children following the truck at any given point can be found by adding the number of children on each street as they join the group. \n\nOn the first street, there are 5 children.\nOn the second street, each child is joined by another child, so there are 5 * 2 = 10 children.\nOn the third street, each child in the existing group is joined by another two children, so there are 10 + 5 = 15 children.\n\nTherefore, by the time the truck reaches the end of the third street, there are 15 children following the truck. The original 5 children then give up and leave the group, so the final number of children following the truck is 15 - 5 = 10.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A) 7.
