2025-12-24 18:44:22 | INFO | Q1293 id=gsm8k_mcq_01292 | baseline_pred=A | gold=D | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can start with the given information that Anne is twice the size of Albert, who is 36" tall. This means that Anne's height is 2 * 36 = 72 inches. \n\nJackie grew 3 inches over the summer, so her current height is 72 - 3 = 69 inches. \n\nHowever, we are also told that Jackie is two inches shorter than Anne. Since Anne's height is 72 inches, this means that Jackie's height before summer was 72 - 2 = 70 inches. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) 70.
