2025-12-24 18:44:32 | INFO | Q1301 id=gsm8k_mcq_01300 | baseline_pred=D | gold=B | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=We can calculate Josh's earnings for two weeks as follows:\n\n  * There are 5 days of the week that Josh works: Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, Friday, Saturday\n  * He works 3 cars per day on those days, so he works with a total of 5 × 3 = 15 cars per week\n  * He gets paid $4 per car, so he makes 15 × 4 = $60 per week\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 60.
2025-12-24 18:44:35 | INFO | Q1303 id=gsm8k_mcq_01302 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=correct | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The total number of toys that Matthew sold would be 12 / 2 = 6 toys. So, he would earn 6 * 5 = $30 for the first half of his collection. And he would also earn 6 * 7 = $42 for the second half of his collection. Therefore, the total amount of money that Matthew would earn is 30 + 42 = $72.\n\nTherefore, the answer is (C).
